hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"32065","(32065) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Hafsa, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein. : He did not inherit from the child of adultery, even if the man claimed it."
"32066","(32066) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: I told him: What your father used to say about Is the child of illegitimate emancipated by his master, or his lady, and his father seizes him, even though his master knows that he is his son? He said: He used to say: He does not inherit."
"32067","(32067) Al-Dahhak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he said: He will inherit it if his master knows that he is his son. And if his masters and opponents deny him, he does not inherit."
"32068","(32068) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever commits adultery with a free woman, or the mother of a people, he neither inherits nor is heir. (Ibn Hibban 5996 and Abd al-Razzaq 13851)"
"32069","(32069) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, in Ibn"
"32070","(32070) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The child of adultery does not inherit, but rather he who does not inherit The punishment will be imposed on his father, and his mother will acquire property through marriage or purchase."
"32071","(32071) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Tell me that the child of adultery does not The one who claims it will inherit it, but the newborn will not inherit it."
"32072","(32072) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He inherits by the lower of the two lineages."
"32073","(32073) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who left his daughter and his sister. And his wife. He said: She inherits according to her closest relative. He said: And his leaders said: She has all the wealth."
"32074","(32074) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Magians do not inherit except one person."
"32075","(32075) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah: They used to inherit The Magians from both sides."
"32076","(32076) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, who said: I asked Hammad about the inheritance of the Magians? He said: They inherit from the face that is permissible."
"32077","(32077) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan: There was a Magusian who married his daughter and had two daughters by her, then she died. One of them after the death of the father. He said: To her sister by her father and to her mother is half, and to her sister by her father and to her mother is a sixth. To complete the two-thirds, she blocked herself with herself."
"32078","(32078) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ata’: That a man freed a freed slave of his, and he died and left behind money. Ibn Masoud was asked? He said: The people of Islam do not go captive. Rather, the people of the pre-Islamic era used to go captive. You are his master and the guardian of His blessings. And the people are entrusted with his inheritance. Otherwise, show him here and a large inheritance. Meaning: the treasury."
"32079","(32079) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ibn Masoud was given money given to people who freed him. And he said to his masters: This is the property of your master. They said: We have no need of it, for we had freed him as a free man. So Ibn Masoud: Indeed, there is a place for it in the wealth of Muslims."
"32080","(32080) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar said: Al-Sa’ibi and Al-Sadaqah for today."
"32081","(32081) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Bakr Ibn Abdullah Al-Muzani: that Ibn Umar was brought with thirty A thousand. He said: I think so. He said: I set him free, so he ordered that slaves be bought for him."
"32082","(32082) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, about a man who freed a freed slave of his. He said: Inheritance. To his master"
"32083","(32083) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about Al-Sa’ibi’s inheritance? He said: Every freed man is free."
"32084","(32084) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I do not know of Al-Sa’ib’s inheritance except for his master, except that"
"32085","(32085) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhil, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaibani, who said: Abdullah said: A traveler leaves his money wherever he wants."
"32086","(32086) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Bastam bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah: Tariq bin Al-Murqa’ freed a boy It was for the sake of God, so he died and left behind money, so it was presented to his master Tariq, and he said: I have made something for God, and I will not return to it. So he wrote About that to Omar, so Omar wrote: Offer the money to Tariq, if he accepts it; otherwise, buy a slave with it and set him free. He said: It reached fifteen heads."
"32087","(32087) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: That a woman from the Ansar freed a freed man, then she said: To him: Friend of whomever you wish. So he appointed Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah as ally, and he was injured on the Day of Al-Yamam, so his wealth was given to him. I set him free"
"32088","(32088) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Asama Ibn Zayd said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Two different religions do not inherit each other. \n(Abu Dawud 2903. Ahmed 178)"
"32089","(32089) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab: that Al-Ash’ath Ibn Qais: A paternal paternal uncle who was a polytheist and a Jew died, so Umar did not inherit from her, and he said: Her family inherited it. Religion"
"32090","(32090) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil: His blindness belongs to Al-Ash’ath. Ibn Qais died as a Jew, so Umar did not inherit anything from her, and he said: Her religious people will inherit her."
"32091","(32091) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Omar, he said: The family inherited it. Religion, every sect follows its own sect."
"32092","(32092) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, who said: Al-‘Ars bin Qais sent to me. Al-Kindi asked me about two Christian brothers, one of whom converted to Islam and the other died and left behind money? So I said: Muawiyah used to say: If he had been a Christian and had inherited it, Islam would have only increased his strength. Al-‘Aras bin Qais said: He refused. This is upon us, Omar bin Al-Khattab, regarding his paternal uncle Al-Ash’ath bin Qais, who died while he was Jewish, and Omar did not leave any heirs to him. Something"
"32093","(32093) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali: He said: The Muslim infidel does not inherit, nor The unbeliever Muslim."
"32094","(32094) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, the same, and he added In it: unless he is his slave and he inherits it."
"32095","(32095) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Omar: In Judiyah, she died. He said: The people of her religion will inherit it."
"32096","(32096) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Christian does not inherit a Muslim, nor does The Christian Muslim, this is the statement of Ali and Zaid, and as for Abdullah bin Masoud, he used to decree that they They will be withheld and will not bequeath any inheritance."
"32097","(32097) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Omar said: The infidel Muslim does not inherit, nor does the Muslim inherit. The infidel"
"32098","(32098) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Omar said the same thing."
"32099","(32099) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel, nor does The infidel Muslim according to the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor the covenant of Abu Bakr, nor the covenant of Omar, so when he was appointed Muawiyah said: The Muslim inherited from the infidel, but the infidel did not inherit from the Muslim. He said: So the caliphs took that until Umar ibn Abdul-Aziz, so he reviewed the first Sunnah, then Yazid bin Abdul-Malik followed that, and when Hisham bin Abdul-Malik rose He adopted the Sunnah of the Caliphs. (Muslim 1233)"
"32100","(32100) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man shall not inherit anyone other than his family. His religion, unless he is a man’s slave or his female slave."
"32101","(32101) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Abi al-Hakim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Buraida, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, said: Muadh was in Yemen, so they went to him because a Jew had died. His brother was a Muslim, and Muadh said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Islam increases and does not decrease. So he inherited it.\n(Ahmad 230. Tabarani 338)"
"32102","(32102) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, he said: I have not seen a judge After a judgment was made by the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, better than a judgment he made regarding the People of the Book, he said: We inherit from them and they do not inherit from us, just as it is permissible for us to marry them, but it is not permissible for them to marry us."
"32103","(32103) Waki’ told us, he said, Sufyan told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A Jew does not inherit from a Christian, A Christian does not inherit from a Jew."
"32104","(32104) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan said: Islam is a religion and polytheism is a religion."
"32105","(32105) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: Islam is a religion and polytheism is a religion."
"32106","(32106) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin: Concerning a man who freed a Christian slave of his and then he died. He said: No. He inherits it."
"32107","(32107) Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Hakim: Omar bin Abdul Aziz He freed a Christian servant of his and he died, so he put his inheritance in the treasury."
"32108","(32108) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to say: If a boy dies and one of his parents is Muslim, He said: The Muslim inherits from them, but not the non-Muslim from them."
"32109","(32109) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim. And on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a donor, and the like."
"32110","(32110) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a boy whose parents are Muslim? They said: He is with the Muslim. He inherits the Muslim and the Muslim inherits him."
"32111","(32111) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: His parents disputed over him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them was a Muslim and the other was an unbeliever, so he gave him the choice, so he inclined towards The infidel, and he said: Oh God, guide him, so he turned to the Muslim, and he decided for him."
"32112","(32112) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, who said: The child is with the Muslim parent."
"32113","(32113) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, similar to this."
"32114","(32114) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is for the Muslim father."
"32115","(32115) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ and Al-Hasan: Concerning a Jew and a Christian, he converts to Islam: the child is with the Muslim."
"32116","(32116) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He said: If a Jew or Christian dies under A Muslim woman has small children, then the child is with their Muslim father, but if they die while they are young, then their inheritance goes to their father. Muslim, their mother does not have any inheritance as long as they are young."
"32117","(32117) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash, who said: A man had intercourse with his newborn, then He sold her to someone else, so they fell in love with her, and they came together to marry her in a single ritual, and she gave birth to a boy. So they came to Ali, and Ali said: He is your heir but not his mother, and he is for the rest of you in the same position as his mother."
"32118","(32118) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Two men were judged for having intercourse with a woman in a bird. One, and she gave birth, and he decreed that he should make them between them, and they would inherit them and they would inherit from him, and he would live as long as he lived."
"32119","(32119) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar was judged in it by saying the rhyme."
"32120","(32120) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar called his mother and asked her which of them she was from? She said: I don't know. They fell on me in a state of purity, and Omar put it between them."
"32121","(32121) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Khalil Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam, he said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from Yemen came to him and Ali was with her, and he made The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, speaks and informs him. He said: O Messenger of God, three people came to Ali and disputed over a son. They all claimed that it was his son who had sexual intercourse with a woman during the same period of ritual impurity, and Ali said: You are quarreling partners, and indeed... He cast lots among you, so whoever cast lots will have the child and a third of the blood money for his companion. He said: So he cast lots among them, and one of them cast lots. So he gave the child to him and imposed on him two-thirds of the blood money. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his molars were visible. Or his molars."
"32122","(32122) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib On the authority of his father: Omar judged two men who claimed a man whose father he did not know, so Omar said to the man: Follow Whatever you want."
"32123","(32123) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He is most in need of his inheritance. And he is a captive."
"32124","(32124) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: He inherits."
"32125","(32125) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning the inheritance of a prisoner, he said: He is in need of inheritance"
"32126","(32126) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The captive inherits."
"32127","(32127) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Abraham say: The prisoner does not inherit."
"32128","(32128) Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: Concerning the prisoner in the hands of the enemy. He said: He does not inherit."
"32129","(32129) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: He did not inherit any inheritance. The captive"
"32130","(32130) Ma’an bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The prisoner’s wealth and his wife are inherited."
"32131","(32131) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: A newborn is not inherited until He deserves it"
"32132","(32132) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Bishr bin Ghalib, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr asked Al-Hussein bin Ali on the authority of the newborn? He said: If it is appropriate, it is obligatory for him to give and provide."
"32133","(32133) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Bishr bin Ghalib, who said: Ibn Al-Zubayr met Al-Hussein bin Ali, and he said: O Abu Abdullah, give us a fatwa regarding the newborn being born into Islam. He said: It is obligatory to give and provide for him."
"32134","(32134) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When a boy begins, he prays. upon him, and he inherited, and if he did not inherit, then he did not inherit and no blessings be upon him."
"32135","(32135) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: If a boy begins it, the prayer is prayed upon him and he inherits, and if He is worthy of blessings and he is not bequeathed to him."
"32136","(32136) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he recites the beginning, his inheritance and inheritance are complete."
"32137","(32137) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: That he said regarding the newborn: The prayer should not be prayed over him, nor It will be inherited, and the blood money will not be completed until it is completed."
"32138","(32138) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: A woman gives birth and he does not receive menstruation? He said: If he moves, it is known that his movement is a result of life and not a convulsion that is inherited, even if his movement is only a result of a convulsion. It is not from a life that was not inherited."
"32139","(32139) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: He does not pray on a fallen one, nor He is inherited."
"32140","(32140) Waki` narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he begins The boy inherited and inherited and may the blessings of God be upon him."
"32141","(32141) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He is not inherited. The newborn until he receives the testimonial."
"32142","(32142) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman gave birth to a son and their wives witnessed that he had intercourse. He was born alive, but they did not bear witness to its establishment, so Shurayh said: The living inherits the dead, then he invalidated his inheritance because they did not They bear witness to the establishment of God."
"32143","(32143) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Za’idah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Istilalal means shouting."
"32144","(32144) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Istilal The boy: his shouting."
"32145","(32145) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad said: Istilal: calling and sneezing."
"32146","(32146) Ma’an bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I see: sneezing means istihlal."
"32147","(32147) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no child born but it is pricked by Satan and then it shouts from the prick of Satan. Except for the son of Maryam and his mother. (Muslim 1838; Abd al-Razzaq 119)"
"32148","(32148) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning brothers, one of them calls him brother, and the others deny him. He said: He will enter with them in the position of a slave, being among the brothers, so one of them will be freed from his share.\n He said: Amer, Al-Hakam, and their companions used to say: It is not included except in the share of the one who recognized it."
"32149","(32149) Ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Some of the people of Sana’a told me that a peacock destroyed his children. The father of four had one of them testify that his father had married a slave who was among them, so Tawoos did not permit the joining by lineage, but he He gave the slave a fifth of the inheritance from the wealth of the one who testified that his father had claimed possession of him, and the slave was freed from the wealth of the one who testified."
"32150","(32150) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: Concerning a man who acknowledged With a brother, he said: I made it clear that he is your brother."
"32151","(32151) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who calls a brother or sister, He said: It is nothing until they all acknowledge it."
"32152","(32152) Waki` narrated to us, he said: If they were brothers, and one of them claimed to be a brother and the other denied it, he said: He was the son of my father. Layla says: Of the six: for the one who did not claim three, for the one who claimed two shares, and for the one who claimed one share.\n He said: Abu Hanifa said: It is one of four: for the one who did not claim two shares, for the one who claimed one, two shares, and for the one who claimed one share."
"32153","(32153) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim: There was a mother who gave birth to three children, and her master claimed the first and the middle. And the other denied it? He said: It is as he said."
"32154","(32154) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir: Concerning a man who has two children and then one of them is denied. He said: He acknowledges them all, or denies them all."
"32155","(32155) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, Omar and Zaid: They did not leave inheritances. Women are of the guardianship, except those whom they have freed."
"32156","(32156) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Women do not inherit from the offspring except what they have emancipated or Our writers"
"32157","(32157) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jamm, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Women do not inherit from the lineage, except what they have written down. Or he emancipated, or he emancipated whom he emancipated."
"32158","(32158) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He said: Women who are close relatives do not inherit except those who have been emancipated, or those who have been emancipated. Emancipate, except for the cursed woman, for she inherits her son from whom his father has been estranged."
"32159","(32159) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz, who said: He does not inherit. Women are of the guardianship, except those who are registered or emancipated."
"32160","(32160) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Women do not inherit anything from male guardians except what They wrote, or they freed."
"32161","(32161) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab: Concerning a woman who died and left behind her master, he said: He is her master, when he dies, any of the male heirs will inherit from her."
"32162","(32162) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Women do not inherit from Loyalty, except what they have freed or written down."
"32163","(32163) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Women do not inherit from the lineage, except those They were freed."
"32164","(32164) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Concerning a man who writes to his servant, Then he dies and leaves behind children: men and women. He said: The money is divided between them in shares, and loyalty goes to the men and not the women."
"32165","(32165) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, on the authority of Abu Salama and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: About a man who appoints a servant to his servant, then he dies and leaves behind children: men and women. He said: The money is divided between them in shares. Loyalty is to men, not women. (Darimi 3144, Bayhaqi 10)"
"32166","(32166) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: A woman freed Salim, so he appointed Abu Hudhayfah as guardian. And he adopted him, and he died, and his inheritance was given to her."
"32167","(32167) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jamm, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a woman who bought out her father and freed him, and he died. And she has a sister. He said: They have two-thirds according to the Book of God, and she has the remaining third because she is his wife. Abu Bakr said: And this is what I say."
"32168","(32168) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin al-Ja’d, on the authority of his leaders: A woman emancipated a slave of hers and then Who did he die for? His loyalty to her clan, or to her son’s clan? He said: Al-Hasan and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab used to say: He is the boy’s Asabah.\n His leaders said: Khalas told me that Ali appointed him as the servant of the boy.\n He said: Saleh bin Al-Khalil told us that Ibn Abbas said that."
"32169","(32169) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him say: The male child of a woman has more right With the inheritance of her master from her clan, and if it was a crime, then her clan is responsible for it."
"32170","(32170) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: Concerning a woman who freed a man and then died. He said: Loyalty is to her children and wisdom is upon them. He said: Amer used to say: Loyalty is to her children and wisdom is upon them."
"32171","(32171) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Riyab bin Hudhayfah bin Saeed bin Sahm married the mother of Wael, son of Muammar Al-Jumahiyah, and she bore him three children. Then their mother died, so her four sons inherited her and the loyalty of her masters, so Amr bin Al-Aas went with them to the Levant. They died in the plague of Emmaus. He said: Amr inherited them, and he was their clan. When Amr returned, Banu Muammar came and disputed with him over the matter. Their sister’s loyalty was to Omar bin Al-Khattab. Omar said: I will decide between you according to what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: Whatever the child or the father achieves, it is up to his family, whoever he may be. He said: So he decided. We have it, and he wrote for us a book in which there are testimonies of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, Zayd ibn Thabit, and others.\n Even when Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan was appointed successor, her heir died and left two thousand dinars, and I was informed that this ruling had been decided. He was changed, so his opponents disputed with him to Hisham bin Ismail, so we referred it to Abd al-Malik and brought him the letter of Omar, and he said: If you see This is one of the decisions about which there is no doubt, and I did not think that the matter of the people of Medina had reached this point that they should doubt it. This is the ruling, so he decided it for us, and we have not stayed on it yet. (Nasa’i 6349. Ahmad 27)"
"32172","(32172) Yahya bin Azhar told us, he said: Mandal told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ali said in A woman emancipates a man: loyalty is to her children and her children’s children, as long as there are males left among them. If they die out, they return to their clan."
"32173","(32173) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shuraih and Zayd ibn Thabit: Concerning a man who died. He left behind his son, his father, and his master, then the master died and left behind money, so Shurayh said: A sixth is for his father, and whatever remains is for the son.\nZaid bin Thabit said: The money is for the son, but the father has nothing."
"32174","(32174) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about a man who freed a slave of his and he died and died. The master left behind the one who had freed him, his father and his son, so Abraham said: One-sixth is for his father, and whatever remains is for his son."
"32175","(32175) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is for the son."
"32176","(32176) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He used to say that."
"32177","(32177) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Al-Hakam and Hammad saying: It is for the son."
"32178","(32178) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, Hammad, and Abu Iyas Muawiyah bin Qurayh about A woman emancipated a boy of hers, then she died and left behind her father and son. They said: Loyalty is to the son, and Abu Iyas said: Loyalty For her children, whatever remains of them."
"32179","(32179) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Loyalty is to the son."
"32180","(32180) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I was informed on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit that he said: Loyalty is to the son."
"32181","(32181) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, he said: Loyalty is to the son.\n This is the saying of Sufyan."
"32182","(32182) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, he said: Abraham used to say: To the father is a sixth of the loyalty. And the son gets one-fifth-sixths of the loyalty. Shu'ba said: I said to Abu Ma'shar: I heard it from Abraham saying it. He said: I heard it, and Mughiry said: I heard it from Abraham says:"
"32183","(32183) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to say: Loyalty is in its status. Money"
"32184","(32184) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: That he used to carry out loyalty as Money"
"32185","(32185) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a giving regarding a man who died and left behind a client of his. And his grandfather and brother, to whom is his master’s loyalty? Ataa said: The loyalty between them is two halves."
"32186","(32186) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: I was informed on the authority of Al-Zuhri that he said: Loyalty is for the grandfather."
"32187","(32187) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri: Concerning a man who left his grandfather and his brother, he said: Loyalty is to the grandfather because he is attributed to the grandfather, and not to the brother."
"32188","(32188) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar: Among the slaves he married a free woman and she gave birth to him. Children, then he will be freed. He said: The loyalty of his sons will be attached to him."
"32189","(32189) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, Al-A’mash said: I see it on the authority of the lions, Omar said: If it was The free woman is under the slave of the slave and gives birth, so her child’s loyalty is to the mother’s slave, so if the father is freed, the loyalty is taken away."
"32190","(32190) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Omar, Ali, Abdullah, and Zaid, they used to say: If The freedmen followed him, and he had children from a free woman whose loyalty was dragged, so I said to Al-Sha’bi: The grandfather. He said: The grandfather is a dragoon just like the father."
"32191","(32191) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Loyalty returns to the father’s loyalist. If he was freed, and it happened that Omar and Uthman judged him, and Shurayh did not judge him, then he judged him."
"32192","(32192) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father: That someone appointed to Al-Zubayr married the mother of a son. To Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: She gave birth to children, then he was freed. Al-Zubayr and Rafi’ disputed over their loyalty to Uthman, and he decided. With loyalty to Al-Zubayr."
"32193","(32193) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid al-Araj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi: that Othman Ibn Affan pledged allegiance to Al-Zubayr."
"32194","(32194) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: So The father was freed due to loyalty."
"32195","(32195) Waki’ told us, he said: Aban bin Sam’a told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he marries The free woman owned by the slave, so whatever happened within the uterus, its loyalty is to the mother’s slave, so if the father is freed, the loyalty follows."
"32196","(32196) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of a man from the Ansar who was called: Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, he said: If the father is freed, then loyalty will be taken away."
"32197","(32197) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih: He did not rule with a jirr. Loyalty until Al-Aswad told him, on the authority of Abdullah that he had decided on it, so Shurayh decided it."
"32198","(32198) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khaled, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz, he said: A loyalty is required. His son"
"32199","(32199) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He rewards the loyalty of his son."
"32200","(32200) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Loyalty is returned to the father’s servant if he is freed."
"32201","(32201) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id and Khalas: They said: If a slave marries a free woman and she gives birth to children, and then he is emancipated, then he is rewarded with loyalty."
"32202","(32202) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: The grandfather brings Loyalty"
"32203","(32203) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid. On the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, and Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdul Malik, they said: What If she is born while he is a slave, then loyalty is to the mother’s slave, and if she is born while he is free, then loyalty is to the father’s slave."
"32204","(32204) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: He used to say: Loyalty is not valid, except as long as she gives birth. And he is free."
"32205","(32205) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A man married a free woman and she gave birth, then he was freed. The servant, to whom is his son’s loyalty? He said: His son’s loyalty is to his mother’s family."
"32206","(32206) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who used to say: If a man is freed and his son frees another man, The loyalty of his father, so Muhammad bin Sirin came to him and said: Omar says this? He said: We say it."
"32207","(32207) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who was freed by a people and whose fathers were freed by others. He said: They are inherited through the wombs, and their crimes are upon the wise men of their masters."
"32208","(32208) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ali and al-Zubayr disputed over the matter. He was a guardian of Safiyah to Omar, so Omar decided that the inheritance would go to Al-Zubayr and the inheritance would go to Ali."
"32209","(32209) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, he said: Omar wrote to Abdullah: If anyone The gangster approached his mother and gave him the money."
"32210","(32210) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God decided May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding the religion before the will, and you read: (After a will, he bequeaths it, or Religion) and that the particular descendants of the mother inherit without the descendants of the relatives: the brothers from the father and the mother, not the brothers from the father."
"32211","(32211) Waki’ told us, he said: Malik bin Mughal, he said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about up to three paternal and maternal cousins? And from one to two paternal cousins? Al-Sha’bi said: The money is for the people of Al-Alat."
"32212","(32212) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: If there is a relative, one of them is closer to the mother, The money is his in loyalty."
"32213","(32213) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: That Ali, Abdullah, and Zaid said: Loyalty For arrogance."
"32214","(32214) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, Abdullah, and Zaid, they said: Loyalty to pride."
"32215","(32215) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: It was decided as it is decided. Concerning money, he said: Ali and Zaid used to make it for arrogance."
"32216","(32216) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim bin Riyah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Maqil, on the authority of Ali, said: Loyalty is a branch of slavery, so whoever achieves inheritance achieves loyalty."
"32217","(32217) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Riyah, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, who said: Loyalty is to pride."
"32218","(32218) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, he said: Loyalty is to pride."
"32219","(32219) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Malik al-Ghaffari, he said: If he dies The first emancipator, so which of you is the one who inherits it? He has the loyalty of his master."
"32220","(32220) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: When the leader of the people dies, he looks at the people closest to him. So his inheritance was made for him."
"32221","(32221) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There was a shareholder who used to carry out loyalty like money. He said Al-Shaabi: And the people of Medina say: Loyalty is to pride."
"32222","(32222) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun: that Shurayh ruled regarding the Al-Ash’ath family that loyalty is between Uncle and nephew."
"32223","(32223) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Sunan heard Abu Jamilah say: I found someone shunned during the reign of Omar. Then Arifi mentioned him to Omar, so he called me and asked me, so I told him. He said: He is free, and his loyalty is to you, and it is upon us to breastfeed him."
"32224","(32224) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali said: The outcast is free, if he likes to The ally of the one who plucked it: his lord, and if he likes to be ally of someone else: his lord."
"32225","(32225) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The fallen person can be loyal to whomever he wishes."
"32226","(32226) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The inheritance of a foundling is equal to the inheritance of a foundling."
"32227","(32227) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: His inheritance is in the treasury, and his inheritance is for them."
"32228","(32228) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: that Omar bin Al-Khattab gave the inheritance of the outcast For the one who guaranteed it."
"32229","(32229) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Omar bin Ru’ba, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, on the authority of Wathili bin al-Asqa’, He said: A woman inherits three things: her foundling, her freed woman, and the cursed woman: her two sons."
"32230","(32230) Waki’ told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhab, he said: I heard Tamim al-Dari say: I said: O Messenger of God, what is the law regarding a man from the People of the Book greeting a man from among the People of the Book? Muslims? He said: He is the most deserving of people in terms of his life and death. (Tirmidhi 2112, Ahmad 102)"
"32231","(32231) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid: That a man came to Omar and said: A man said hello at my hands and died. And he left behind a thousand dirhams, so you were embarrassed and took them to you? He said: What do you think if he had committed a crime against whom would it have been? He said: Ali. He said: So his inheritance is yours."
"32232","(32232) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: that Omar ibn al-Khattab said: If a man appoints another man as his guardian, he will have his inheritance. May his mind be upon him."
"32233","(32233) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man submits to Islam at the hands of another man, he will have his inheritance. May his mind be upon him."
"32234","(32234) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Omar narrated to us, saying: My father ruled regarding a man from the people of the people of the people of Islam who converted to Islam. At the hands of a man, and he died and left behind a son, so he gave her half to his daughter, and the one who converted to Islam at his hands gave half."
"32235","(32235) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Muntashir, on the authority of Masruq, he said: There was a man among us who was coming from Daylam, and he died and left behind three hundred dirhams. So I went to Ibn Masoud and asked him? He said: Does he have any relatives? Or does any of you have a pledge of allegiance to him? We said: No. He said: Here we have many heirs. Meaning: the treasury."
"32236","(32236) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of his master, he said: I asked Omar about a man who greeted Ali. My hand and made a contract with me and died? He said: You are the people most deserving of his inheritance as long as he does not leave an heir. If he does not leave an heir, then if you refuse, then this is the treasury."
"32237","(32237) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Abi Salih Al-Aslami narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh nicknamed Abu Mudrik: That a man from The people of Sawad are called: An Ethiopian who came to Ali to be his guardian, but he refused to be his guardian and rejected him. He said: So he came to Al-Abbas - Or Ibn Abbas - so he appointed him."
"32238","(32238) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say about a man who converted to Islam at the hands of another man, and he said: He has his inheritance unless he has a sister. If she is a sister, then she has the money and she has more right to it."
"32239","(32239) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Hisham informed us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Abul Dhail greeted Ali. It was given to a man, and he died and left behind ten thousand dirhams. Abu al-Dhudhail brought it to Ziyad, and Ziyad said: You have more right to it. He said: I have no need for it, so Ziyad said: You are his heir, but he refused, so Ziyad took it and put it in the treasury."
"32240","(32240) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi. On the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, they said: His inheritance is for the Muslims, and his reward is for them."
"32241","(32241) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Abdullah narrated to us, saying: We had a wife, and she had a son who greeted me. Our hands: He died and left behind money, so I asked Al-Shaabi? He said: Give him to his mother."
"32242","(32242) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There are no loyalties except for those who are blessed."
"32243","(32243) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who befriended another man and greeted him at his hand. He said: No. He inherits it, but if he wishes, he will leave all of his wealth to him."
"32244","(32244) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Asbahani, on the authority of Mujahid bin Wardan, On the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha: A servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell from a palm tree and died, leaving behind some wealth. He did not leave a child or an intimate partner, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give his inheritance to a man from the people of your village.\n(Abu Dawud 2894. Tirmidhi 2105)"
"32245","(32245) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd. Al-Rahman ibn Thawban: A man from Jurham died in prison and left money, so he wrote about it to Omar, so Omar wrote to the Levant. They did not find a single crime left, so Omar divided his inheritance among the people among whom he died."
"32246","(32246) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Sahl, he said: A client of Uthman’s covenant died and he had no guardian, so Uthman ordered his money to be taken into the treasury."
"32247","(32247) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq: He was asked about a man who died and left no guardian. A freedman or an heir? He said: His wealth is wherever he puts it. If he did not bequeath anything, then his wealth is in the Bayt al-Mal."
"32248","(32248) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ahmar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father, he said I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came and said: O Messenger of God, I have the inheritance of a man from Azd. And I did not find a Azadi to pay him to. He said: Go and look for a Azadi of general - or a year old - and I will give him to him. He said: So he set out, then came to him in the seventh year and said: O Messenger of God, I have not found anyone to push him to. He said: Go to the first place. You find a Khuza’i, so take him to him. He said: When he stood up, he said: I have to do it with him. He said: So go and push him to the largest Khuza’i.\n(Abu Dawud 2895, Ahmed 347)"
"32249","(32249) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah, On the authority of Omar: A man died without leaving behind a descendant, so Omar said: He who was angry will inherit it due to his and his neighbors’ anger."
"32250","(32250) Zaid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Utbah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, he said: A man from Abyssinia died, and his inheritance was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Look, does he have an heir? They did not find an heir for him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Look who is here among the Muslim Abyssinians, so push back. To them is his inheritance."
"32251","(32251) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather: that Amr ibn al-Aas wrote to Omar about the monk dying and having no heir, so he wrote to him: to give him his inheritance. Those who were paying his tribute."
"32252","(32252) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: With regard to someone who dies and has no heir, he said: An inheritance for his family. His village seeks help from him in their taxes."
"32253","(32253) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Mughirah, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who sold allegiance to a woman from the family. He had something of hers with him, but he threw it away and did not find her. Should he put it in the treasury of the Muslims? He said: Yes."
"32254","(32254) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I was the last of people to promise Omar. So I heard him say: Al-Kalala is the one who has no children."
"32255","(32255) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abu Bakr said: I saw an opinion about Al-Kalalaila. If you are correct, then it is from God, and if you are wrong, then it is from me and Satan: the calamity is nothing but the child and the parent."
"32256","(32256) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, he said: He said to me Ibn Abbas: Al-Kalala is someone who has no children or parents."
"32257","(32257) Al-Muqri’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib narrated to me, on the authority of my father. Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Aamir: He said: I did not treat the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, anything I did not do with them. The glory"
"32258","(32258) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I asked him about Al-Kalāla, and he said: What is less than a child? And the father"
"32259","(32259) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Saad bin Malik: He recited This letter: He has a brother or a maternal sister."
"32260","(32260) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Abd al-Saluli, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Kalala, except for the father and the child."
"32261","(32261) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Al-Sumait, who said: Omar used to say: Al-Kalalālă except for the child. And the father."
"32262","(32262) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Kalala is The dead"
"32263","(32263) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him from selling loyalty, and from gifting it."
"32264","(32264) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ali said: Loyalty is in his position. The oath, it cannot be sold or given away. Confirm it as God Almighty has made it."
"32265","(32265) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Loyalty is only like lineage. His lineage?"
"32266","(32266) Jarir, Hafs, and Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Loyalty does not It will be sold or given away."
"32267","(32267) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Omar, who said: Loyalty is like kinship. It will be sold or given away."
"32268","(32268) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Loyalty is like lineage, it cannot be sold or sold. Yahweh"
"32269","(32269) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: Loyalty Lineage, neither sold nor given away."
"32270","(32270) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Miskin, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Loyalty cannot be sold, nor Yahweh"
"32271","(32271) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, that they said: Loyalty is a condition like lineage, it cannot be sold. And he will not be rewarded."
"32272","(32272) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Loyalty is neither sold nor given."
"32273","(32273) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Loyalty cannot be sold, given away, or given in charity. With it"
"32274","(32274) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Maymunah gave the loyalty of Suleiman bin Yassar to Ibn Abbas."
"32275","(32275) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who freed another man, and the freed man went off and appointed someone else as his guardian? He said: He does not have that unless the freedman gifts it to him."
"32276","(32276) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm: That a woman From a warrior who gave his slave’s loyalty to himself and freed him and he freed himself, he said: So he gave himself to Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he said: And she died, so the loyalist disputed with Uthman, he said: So Uthman called for evidence based on what he said: He said: So he came to him. With the clear evidence, so Othman said: Go and do justice to whomever you wish.\n Abu Bakr: He appointed Abdul-Rahman bin Amr bin Hazm as governor."
"32277","(32277) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Mansour informed me, on the authority of Ibrahim and Shu’abi, They both said: There is no harm in selling a free man’s loyalty and giving it away."
"32278","(32278) Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of his leaders: A woman who pledged loyalty She is loyal to her husband, and he said: Hisham bin Hubira: As for me, I think it is for her husband as long as he lives, so if he dies, I will return it to her. The woman inherited"
"32279","(32279) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm if the master gives permission to be a ruler. Change it"
"32280","(32280) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders - I found it in another place, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab - that: He saw no harm in selling a loyalty if it was from his office, and he hated it if it was a manumission."
"32281","(32281) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Ibrahim about the sale of loyalty? He said: It is modern."
"32282","(32282) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Women do not inherit from a woman except What they freed."
"32283","(32283) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Zakariya narrated to us, I heard Amir saying, Concerning a woman who died while she had Three sons, boys, and two daughters, one of whom is absent in Syria, and the other is with her, so she claimed that she was with her daughter. She who is in the Levant for money, and she said to her sons: I would like for you to ask for the money that she has for what befalls her. My inheritance. They said: Yes. She said: I would like for you to give whatever befalls her from my inheritance to her sister, so her inheritance is the same. A man among you will be afflicted, and they said: Yes, then her daughter came after they had divided the inheritance and asked for what befalls her. Her inheritance. She said: Why do I have Abraham’s money? So he said: A straight arrow will be taken from each of them and he will return it to her. And Amer said: One of the two arrows will be taken from them. The slave-girl has struck, and it is returned to her sister, so each one of them gets a share, and each man gets two shares."
"32284","(32284) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Adam Al-Sadusi, on the authority of some of his people: that a woman died while he was a Muslim. She left behind a Christian mother, so her mother converted to Islam before her daughter’s inheritance was divided. So they went to Ali and mentioned that. He said: There is no inheritance for her. Then he said: How much did she leave? They told him, and he said: Give her something from him."
"32285","(32285) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If the deceased dies, the inheritance is returned to his family."
"32286","(32286) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibn Ibrahim, he said: Whoever was freed upon death, or he converted to Islam upon death, none of them has any right, because rights are due upon death."
"32287","(32287) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I saw an old man leaning on a staff. It was said: This is the heir of Safiyya. He accepted an inheritance, but he did not inherit it."
"32288","(32288) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who accepted Islam in exchange for an inheritance? They said: He shall not inherit."
"32289","(32289) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: Concerning a slave who is freed on the basis of inheritance: that he has no right Something"
"32290","(32290) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Yazid bin Qatada: that his father died. He is a Christian, and Yazid is a Muslim, and he has Christian brothers, so Umar did not inherit from him, then Yazid’s mother died. She was a Muslim, so her brothers converted to Islam after her death, so they asked for an inheritance, so they went to Uthman and he asked about that. So he inherited from them."
"32291","(32291) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If a Christian dies, the deceased is given to him, and the portion is divided. his inheritance and some of it remained, then he converted to Islam and he reached you."
"32292","(32292) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Whoever entrusts an inheritance, he said: He inherits what has not been divided. Concerning a slave who is freed on the basis of an inheritance, he said: He inherits what has not been divided."
"32293","(32293) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ali said: Whoever surrenders his inheritance, it is his."
"32294","(32294) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zayed narrated to us, saying: I took these obligations from Firas, who claimed Al-Sha’bi wrote to him:\n1. Zayd bin Thabit and Ibn Masoud ruled: Brothers from the father and mother are partners with brothers from the mother in their offspring: mention them. And their females, and Ali ruled that the mother’s sons are distinct from the father’s and mother’s sons.\n2. Ali and Zaid ruled that the paternal grandfather does not inherit from her father along with her son, and Abdullah inherited a sixth of it with her son.\n3. A woman who left her mother and her brothers as infidels and slaves. Ali and Zayd ruled: for her mother a third and for her female relatives. The two-thirds were not inherited by an infidel or a slave from a free Muslim, nor were they to be veiled from it, and Ibn Masoud was veiling it. And he does not inherit from them, so it was decided: The mother gets a sixth and the female descendant gets what remains.\n4. A woman left her husband and her mother’s siblings, and she had a son, a mamluk: Ali and Zaid ruled: for her husband half, And to her brothers is a third, and to the descendants what remains, and Abdullah ruled: The husband gets a quarter, and whatever remains is the descendants.\n5. A woman who left her mother and her brothers as infidels and slaves: Ali and Zayd decided: for her mother a third, and for the gang a third. He remained, and Abdullah ruled: her mother gets a sixth and the female slave gets what remains.\n6. A woman who left her husband and sisters to her mother,And there is no descendant of hers. Zayd ruled: The husband gets half and the brothers get a third, and Ali and Abdullah ruled: That he return what remained from Ali. The two brothers on the mother’s side, because they did not refuse any of the obligatory duties imposed on the husband in any way, but rather referred her to the closest relative. He knows\n7. If a woman leaves her mother, they all owe a third to the mother, and Ali and Ibn Masoud made a ruling: return what remained to the mother.\n8. A man who left his sister to his father and mother, and to his mother, they paid a full amount: to his sister, to his father and mother, half, and to his mother, a third. Ali and Abdullah decided that what was left - which was a share - would be returned to them according to what they inherited, so the sister would get three Fifths, and the mother gets one-fifth of the money.\n9. A man left his sister to his father, his grandmother, and his wife. They paid a half for his sister, and for his wife, a quarter, and for his grandmother, an share. He returned what was left to his sister and grandmother according to what was obligatory for them. As for Abdullah, he returned it to his sister because he was not It is returned to my grandfather, unless there is no heir other than her.\n10. A woman who left behind her mother and her sister was given a full payment: for her mother a third and for her sister a sixth, and what was left was returned to me. Ali is responsible for dividing his duty, so the mother gets two-thirds, and the sister gets a third, and Abdullah ruled: What remains must be returned to Ali. mother,Because he did not return to his maternal brothers with a mother, so the mother gets five-sixths, and the sister gets one-sixth.\n11 A woman who left her sister to her father and mother, and her sister to her father were all killed, as was her sister to her father and mother. The half, and to her sister, to her father, a sixth. He returned what remained from them according to their portion of their due share, so it would be for the sister from the father and mother. Three-quarters, and for the paternal sister a quarter, and Abdullah returned what remained to the sister from the father and mother, so she became five-sixths. The money, and the father’s sister gets a sixth of the money. It was not appropriate for a father’s sister to have a mother’s and father’s sister.\n12 A woman who left her sisters to her father and mother, and her mother, they paid all together: to her mother a sixth and to her sisters a third, and he returned what What is left over from them is their share of their obligatory share, so the mother gets a third and the brothers get two-thirds, and as for Abdullah, he returned what What remains is due to the mother, so the mother gets two-thirds and the brothers get a third.\n13 A woman left behind her daughter and her son’s son. They all paid a debt: for her daughter the half, and for her son the sixth, and he responded to what He remained in charge of what was left over from them according to their share of their obligatory duty, and Abdullah returned what remained to his son exclusively.\n14 A woman left behind her daughter and her grandmother, they paid half for the son, and for the grandmother a sixth.He returned to me what remained from them according to their share of their obligation, and Abdullah returned what remained from his son exclusively.\n15 A woman left behind her daughter, her son’s son, and her mother. They decided together that her daughter gets half and her son gets a sixth. And for her mother one-sixth, and he returned what remained to them according to their share of their obligatory share, and Abdullah returned what remained to the son and mother, and as for Zayd ibn Thabit, for he placed the surplus from all of that in the treasury. He does not return anything to the heir, nor will it ever be more. Something about God’s obligations.\n16 A woman who left her brothers from her mother, men and women, and they were her kinsfolk: they divide the third equally among them. And two-thirds are for their males, not for their women."
"32295","(32295) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Amir, that he was asked about a man who made a will to be freed and given charity for the sake of God? Shurayh said: Each one of them will be given his share."
"32296","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(32296) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdul Muttalib Ibn Rabi’a: Some of the Ansar said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: We hear from your people that the one who said Among them: The example of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is like a palm tree that grew palm trees. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace be upon him: O people, who am I? They said: You are the Messenger of God, peace be upon you. He said: I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib. He said: So what we heard belongs to you. He never kissed her, then he said: Indeed, God created His creation, then divided them into two groups, and made me one of the best of the two groups. Then He made them tribes, so He made me one of the best tribes among them. I am the best of you in family and the best of you in soul.\n(Tirmidhi 3532, Ahmed 166)"
"32297","(32297) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Tufayl bin Ubayy, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, you will be an imam. People, their fiancé, and the one who intercedes for them, and no pride. (Ahmad 1371, Tirmidhi 3613)"
"32298","(32298) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I went out From sexual intercourse, I did not come out of incest from the place of Adam. The incest of the pre-Islamic times did not affect me. (Bayhaqi 190)"
"32299","(32299) Hushaym told us, Sayyar told us, Yazid al-Faqir told us, Jabir bin Abdullah told us: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You were given five things that no one has given you. You became terrified a month’s journey away, and the earth was made for you. A pure place and a mosque, so whichever man from my nation is able to pray, let him pray, and the spoils have been made lawful for me, but they were not made lawful for anyone before me. And I was given intercession, and the Prophet was sent to his people specifically, and I was sent to the people in general."
"32300","(32300) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid and Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was given five, and I do not say this with pride: I was sent to the red and the black, and the earth was made for me. A sanctuary and a mosque, and the spoils were made lawful to me, but they were not lawful to anyone before me. And I was given the right of intercession, and I postponed it for my nation until the Day of Resurrection, and it will be granted to you, God willing, whoever does not associate God with you. Something"
"32301","(32301) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I was supported by terror, and I was given the most comprehensive words, and the spoils were made lawful to me, and while I was sleeping I was brought With the keys of the treasures of the earth, they were twisted in my hand. (Bukhari 2977, Muslim 372)"
"32302","(32302) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was given five things that no prophet before me had given me: I was sent. To the red and the black, and I was supported with terror for a month’s journey, and the land was made for me a purification and a place of worship, and the spoils were made lawful for me, but no It was permissible for a prophet who was before me, and I was given intercession, for there is no prophet who did not ask for his intercession, and I delayed my intercession: I made it for one who dies not associating anything with God."
"32303","(32303) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Masoud ibn Malik, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was helped by youth, and Aad was destroyed by the hornet. (Bukhari 1035. Muslim 17)"
"32304","(32304) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah: He heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was given Unless any of the prophets were given this, we said: O Messenger of God! What is it? He said: I was victorious through terror, I was given the keys of the earth, I was named Ahmed, the dust was made pure for me, and my nation was made the best of nations. (Ahmad 98 and Bazzar 656)"
"32305","(32305) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, who said: Ka'b said: The first one to take the door of Paradise by the throat and have it opened for him is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he recited a verse. From the Torah: The last of us are the first, the last are the first."
"32306","(32306) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfy, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: We have been favored over people by three things: the entire earth has been made for us a place of mosque, and its soil has been made for us when there is no We find the water pure, and these verses were given from a treasure house under the throne from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah, it was not given from Him. No one before me, and no one after me will be given that."
"32307","(32307) Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Mandal, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: I went out in search of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and found him praying, so I waited for him until he prayed, and he said: I have been given. It is the fifth night, such as no prophet was given before me: I was aided by terror, so the enemy would be terrified by a month’s march, and I was sent to the Red Sea. And the lions, and the earth was made for me a sanctuary and a place of mosque, and spoils were made permissible for me but they were not permissible for anyone before me, and it was said: Ask and it will be given to you. So I hid it, for it will come from among you who does not associate partners with God."
"32308","(32308) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: I am the first to intercede in the jinn, and he said: None of the prophets has spoken the truth as much as you have spoken the truth, and indeed, among the prophets there is no prophet. Of his nation, he believed him except one man. (Muslim 330, Ahmad 140)"
"32309","(32309) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised place} He said: He will make him sit on the throne."
"32310","(32310) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair: {And indeed, he is with us. For Zulfi} He said: The mention of getting close to him."
"32311","(32311) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I entered Paradise and, lo, I am in a flowing river, its edges are tents of pearls, so I hit the clay with my hand, and when it catches it I exhale. He said: So I said To Gabriel: What is this? He said: This is Al-Kawthar which God Almighty has given you. (Ahmad 1031, Ibn Hibban 6472)"
"32312","(32312) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us. He greeted us in front of us when he fell asleep, then he raised his head smiling, and we said: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God? He said: A surah has just been revealed to me, so he recited, In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar. Pray to your Lord and sacrifice. Indeed, that is your choice. Al-Abatr} Then he said: Do you know what Al-Kawthar is? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: For it is a river and my Lord has promised me, upon it is much good, and it is a basin that you can visit. On the Day of Resurrection, my nation will be as numerous as the stars. Then the servant will be overwhelmed by them and I will say: My Lord, he is one of my companions. He says: No, you do not know what happened after you. (Muslim 53. Ahmad 102)"
"32313","(32313) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Hakim’s daughter, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, do you have a basin? He said: Yes, and I love the one whom your people return to me. (Ahmed 409)"
"32314","(32314) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muhajir bin Al-Mismar, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, who said: I wrote to Jabir bin Samura: Tell me about something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he wrote to me: I heard him say: I Overflowing into the pelvis. (Muslim 1453. Ahmad 89)"
"32315","(32315) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Al-Sanabih, he said: I heard him say: I heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: I will leave you at the basin. (Bukhari 7335. Ahmed 236)"
"32316","(32316) Abu Asama and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs ibn Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is nothing between my grave and the pulpit of Rawdah. Garden of Paradise, and my pulpit is on my lap."
"32317","(32317) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings be upon him: I will leave you at the basin. (Bukhari 65751 Muslim 1796)"
"32318","(32318) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace on this pulpit, saying: Indeed, you have a predecessor upon Al-Kawthar.\n(Muslim 1795. Ahmad 297)"
"32319","(32319) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise, two edges of which are made of gold, and its stream is on rubies and pearls, its soil is It is sweeter than musk, and its water is sweeter than honey and whiter than snow. (Tirmidhi 3361. Dharmi 2837)"
"32320","(32320) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, on the authority of Jundub, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: I will leave you at the basin. (Muslim 1792. Ahmad 313)"
"32321","(32321) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: In front of you is a basin as between Jarbaa and Adharh. (Muslim 34. Abu Dawud 4712)"
"32322","(32322) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He came out The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day while we were in the mosque and he was tying his head with a rag due to the illness he died. Then he turned towards the pulpit, so we followed him, and he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he is standing at the Basin at the end of the night. \n(Darimi 77. Abu Ali 1150)"
"32323","(32323) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: People will come to my basin and mingle without you. (Bukhari 6576 and Ahmed 473)"
"32324","(32324) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us and said: I will leave you at the basin."
"32325","(32325) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will leave you at the basin. Whoever comes to me will drink from it, and whoever drinks from it will not. He is never thirsty. (Bukhari 65850 Muslim 1793)"
"32326","(32326) Zayd ibn Harun told us, his people informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Usaid ibn al-Hudair, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You will see my traces after me, so be patient until you meet me at the basin.\n(Bukhari 3792, Ahmed 351)"
"32327","(32327) Affan told us, Wahib told us, Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar: After me you will meet a legacy, so be patient until You will meet me at the basin. (Bukhari 4330 and Muslim 738)"
"32328","(32328) Affan narrated to us, Wahib narrated to us, Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, On the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I am at the basin waiting for someone to come to the basin.\n(Muslim 1794, Abu Ali 4437)"
"32329","(32329) Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: I said: O Messenger of God, what is the vessel for the basin? He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, your intention is greater than the number of stars in the sky and their planets in the dark night. Al-Musahiyah, whoever drinks from it will not thirst. Its width is as long as the distance between Amman and its descendants. Its water is whiter than Milk is sweeter than honey. (Muslim 1798 and Ahmad 149)"
"32330","(32330) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha al-Amri, on the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am at the depths of my cistern, defending the people from it, to the people of the right. Indeed, I will strike them with a stick until they refuse. He said: Then a prophet was asked. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about the saa’ of the basin? He said: There is not a month or so between these two places of my stay and Amman. Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked. May God bless him and grant him peace. About his drink? He said: Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. He pours into it a spout of ink, or two ink from the jinn. One is paper and the other is gold. (Muslim 1799. Ahmad 275)"
"32331","(32331) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra: That the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Men from among those who accompanied me and saw me would come to the basin to the point that when they were raised up to me, they would mingle without me. So I will say: Lord of my companions. So they will say: You do not know what they did after you. (Ahmed 48)"
"32332","(32332) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of One day, God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was eating meat, and she raised the arm to him, and she was admiring him, so he gasped at it, and then He said: I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection, and do you know why on the Day of Resurrection God will gather the first and the last in One level, and the caller will hear them, and sight will penetrate them, and the sun will set, and the people will be in anguish and distress beyond measure. They cannot bear it, but they cannot bear it, so some people say to others: Do you not see what has reached you? Do you not look for someone to intercede for you? To your Lord.\n Some people say to one another: Your father is Adam. Then they come to Adam and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind. God created you with His own hand. And He breathed into you of His Spirit, and commanded the angels, and they prostrated to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? Don't you see what we have reached? So he says to them: Indeed, my Lord has\n He was angry today with an anger that he had never been angry with before, and he will never be angry like him after him, and he forbade me from the tree. So I disobeyed him, myself, myself, go to someone else, go to Noah.\n Then they will come to Noah and say: O Noah, you are the first of the messengers to the people of the earth, and God has called you a grateful servant. Intercede for us with your Lord.Don't you see what we're in? Don't you see what we've reached? So He says to them: Indeed, my Lord has become angry today with an anger that He has never been angry with before, and He will never be angry with the like of Him after Him. And indeed, I had a supplication which I invoked upon my people, myself, myself. Go to others, go to Abraham \n Then they would go to Abraham and say: O Abraham, you are the Prophet of God and his friend from among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Don't you see where we are? Don't you see what we have achieved? Then Abraham will say to them: Indeed, my Lord has become angry today with an anger that He has never been angry with before, nor will He be angry with after Him. The like of him, and he mentioned his lies, my soul, my soul, go to someone else, go to Moses.\n So they would come to Moses and say: O Moses, you are the Messenger of God, and God has favored you with His message and His words over the people, intercede for us. To your Lord, do you not see what we are in? Don't you see what we have achieved? Then Moses will say to them: Indeed, my Lord has become angry today with an anger that He has never been angry with before, nor will He be angry with the like of after Him. And I killed a soul whom I was not commanded to kill, myself, myself, go to someone else, go to Jesus.\n Then they will come to Jesus and say: O Jesus, you are the Messenger of God, and you spoke to the people in the cradle, and you conveyed His word to Mary. And a spirit from Him, intercede for us with your Lord,Don't you see where we are? Don't you see what we have achieved? Then Jesus will say to them: Indeed, my Lord has become angry today with an anger that He has never been angry with before, nor will He be angry with after Him. A similar one - and he did not mention any sin - Myself, myself, go to someone else, go to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you.\n Then they come to me and say: O Muhammad, you are the Messenger of God and the Seal of the Prophets, and may God forgive you for your previous and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? Don't you see what we have achieved? So I go and come under the throne and fall prostrating to my Lord, then God will grant victory over me and will bless me with His praises, and the two were good. He was charged with something that had not been revealed to anyone before me. Then it was said: O Muhammad, raise your head. Ask and it will be given to you. Intercede and your intercession will be granted, so I will be raised. My head and I say: O Lord of my nation, O Lord of my nation, several times, and it will be said: O Muhammad, enter the jinn from your nation, one without reckoning. Upon them is the right of the gates of Paradise, and they are partners with people in other gates.\n Then he said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, what is between the two doors is the place of the Paradise, just as it was between Mecca and Hijra. Or as between Mecca and Busra. (Bukhari 3340, Muslim 184)"
"32333","(32333) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: The sun will be given a free sun on the Day of Resurrection. Ten years, then you will come close to the people’s skulls until you are close to two corners, and they will sweat until the sweat drips down to the ground, then It rises until the man gargles. Salman said: Until the man says: gargle. So when they see what they are in, some of them say: To some: Do you not see what you are in? Go to your father Adam and let him intercede for you with your Lord. Then they will go to Adam and say: O our father, you are the one whom God created with His own hand and breathed into you of His Spirit and made you dwell in His Paradise. Arise and intercede for us with our Lord. You see what we are in, so he says: I am not there and I am not like that, so where are the doers? So they say: To whom do you command us? He says: Bring a servant whom God has made thankful.\n Then they would go to Noah and say: O Prophet of God, you are the one whom God has made thankful, and you have seen what we are in. Arise and intercede for us. So he says: I am not there and I am not that, so where is the subject? They say: To whom do you command us? He says: Go to the friend of the Most Gracious, Abraham. So they will come to Abraham and say: O friend of the Most Gracious, you may see what we are in, so intercede on our behalf to our Lord. He will say: I am not. There you are, but you are not there.So where are the verbs? They say: To whom do you command us? He says: Give Moses a servant whom God has chosen for his message and his words.\n Then they would come to Moses and say: You may see what we are in, so intercede on our behalf with our Lord. Then he would say: I am not there, and I am not in that place. So where are the verbs? They say: To whom do you command us? Then he says: Bring the word of God and his spirit to Jesus, son of Mary.\n Then they would come to Jesus and say: O Word of God and His Spirit, you may see what we are in, so intercede on our behalf with our Lord, and He will say: I am not there, and I am not that, so where is the verb? They say: To whom do you command us? So He says: Bring a servant through whom God has opened and sealed, and forgiven his previous and future sins, and he will come on this day. Safe\n Then they will come to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O Prophet of God, you are the one through whom God has opened and sealed, and He has forgiven you for your previous deeds. Your sin and what is coming, and you have come on this day safe, and you may see what we are in, so intercede on our behalf with our Lord, and He says: I Your friend, he goes out and is surrounded by people until he comes to the gate of Paradise, then he takes a gold ring in the gate. Then he knocks on the door, and it is said: Who is this? It is said: Muhammad. He said: Then it will be opened for him, and he will come until he stands before God, and he will ask for permission to prostrate, and the call will be given. And he prostrates to Him,Then he calls: O Muhammad! Raise your head, ask and it will be given to you, intercede and you will be granted intercession, and supplicate and it will be answered. He said: Then God will bestow upon him from praise, praise and glorification whatever It is not opened for any of the creatures. He said: Then he says: Lord of my nation, my nation. Then he asks for permission to prostrate and permission is given to him and he prostrates. Then God opens to him a way of praise, praise, and glorification that has not been opened to any of the creatures, and He calls: O Muhammad! O Muhammad! Raise your head, ask and it will be given to you, intercede and you will be granted intercession, and pray and you will be answered. So he raises his head and says: O Lord, my nation, my nation, two or three times.\n Salman said: He will intercede for everyone who has in his heart a grain of wheat’s weight of faith, or a barley’s weight of faith. Or the weight of a mustard seed of faith, for that is the Praiseworthy Station."
"32334","(32334) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ghalib, on the authority of Hudhayfah said: The master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 1782 and Ahmad 388)"
"32335","(32335) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The believers will gather on the Day of Resurrection and say: If only we had interceded with our Lord, and they will be inspired by that. So He relieved us from this place, and they would come to Adam and say to him: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, and God created you with His hand, and blew In you is His Spirit, and He taught you the names of everything, so intercede on our behalf with our Lord that He may relieve us from this place of ours. He said: I am not here with you. And he complains to them, or mentions the sin he committed, and his Lord is ashamed. But go to Noah, for he is the first Messenger. It was sent to the people of the earth, and they will come to Noah, and he will say: I am not here, and he will remember asking his Lord about what he has no knowledge of. Then his Lord will be ashamed, but go to Abraham, the friend of the Most Gracious. So they will come to him, and he will say: I am not here with you, but go to Moses. A servant to whom God spoke and gave him the Torah, and they come to him and he says: I am not here with you, and the killing of a soul is mentioned to them. Without a soul, then his Lord will be ashamed of that, but go to the servant of God and his Messenger and the word of God and his spirit, and they will come. Jesus says:\n I am not for you and I am not for you, but go to Muhammad, a servant. May God forgive his past and future sins.\n He said: Al-Hasan said: He said: So I will go and walk between two generations of believers. Al-Hasan’s words have ceased, so I will seek permission from my Lord. Then permission is given to me, and when I see my Lord I fall prostrating, then He will leave me as God wills, and it will be said or said: Raise. Your head, say and you will be heard, ask and it will be given to you, intercede and you will be granted intercession, so I will raise my head and praise Him with praise. You will teach me and I will intercede. Then He will impose a punishment for me and I will admit them to Paradise. Then I will return to it the second time. When I see my Lord and fall prostrating, He will leave me alone. God willed that He would leave me, then He would say something similar to His first statement: Say, and it will be heard, and ask, and it will be given to you, and intercede, and you will be interceded, so I raise my head. So praise Him with praise that you will teach me, and it will be said: Ask and it will be given to you, and intercede and it will be interceded, so the punishment will be determined for me, so I will admit you to the Garden, then I return to him on the fourth day and say: O Lord, only those who have been imprisoned by the Qur’an remain."
"32336","(32336) Malik bin Ismail told us, Yaqoub bin Abdullah Al-Qummi told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Hamid, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I am bound by your detention. Speak about it. Fire, and you will overcome me, thrusting into it like moths and grasshoppers, and I am about to send your detention and spare you - or upon me. - Al-Hawd, and you come to me together and dispersed. (Bazzar 204)"
"32337","(32337) Omar bin Saad, Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am leaving among you the two caliphs after me: the Book of God. My family, my family, and they will not separate until they return to the basin. (Ahmad 1821. Tabarani 4921)"
"32338","(32338) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: He sent for me Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad and I came to him and he said: What are the hadiths that you narrate in our language and narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace, we do not hear it in a book of his. He narrated that he had a basin, so he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to us about it. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and our promise to him. (Ahmad 336. Tabarani 5021)"
"32339","(32339) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: I have a basin as long as the Kaaba to the Holy House, white as milk, and its vessel is as many as the stars. Heavens, and I will be the most followed of the prophets on the Day of Resurrection. (Ibn Majah 4301. Abu Ali 1024)"
"32340","(32340) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Asim Al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka'b bin Ajra said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to me while we were sitting on a pillow made of human beings, and he said: It is They will be princes, so whoever enters upon them and believes their lies and helps them in their oppression is not of me and I am not of him. He does not refer to the basin, and whoever does not believe them in their lies and curses them for their injustice is of me and I am of him. It is located near the basin. (Tirmidhi 2259. Ahmad 243)"
"32341","(32341) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Zakaria narrated to us, Atiyya Al-Awfi narrated to us: that Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri narrated to him, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every prophet has been given a gift and he has fulfilled it, but I have hidden your gift. For the intercession of my nation.\n(Ahmad 20. Abu Ali 1010)"
"32342","(32342) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings be upon him: Noah will be called on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: Did you convey the message? He says: Yes, then his people are called and it is said: Did he convey the message to you? They say: No warner came to us, nor did anyone come to us. He said: Then it will be said to Noah: Who will bear witness for you? He says: Muhammad and his nation. He said: That is his saying {And thus We made you a just nation}. He said: The just middle. He said: Then they will be called and bear witness to him with the message. He said: Then I will bear witness against you after that. (Bukhari 3339. Tirmidhi 2961)"
"32343","(32343) Ali bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abdullah said: Indeed, God has taken Abraham is a friend, and indeed your companion is a friend of God. Indeed, Muhammad is the most honorable of creation before God. Then he recited: {Perhaps your Lord will send you A praiseworthy position}"
"32344","(32344) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: God said: {And the trumpet was blown, and whoever was in the heavens and whoever was on the earth was astonished} until His saying: {And when They will stand and watch. So I will be the first to raise his head. Then behold, Moses was taking one of the pillars of the Throne, and I do not know which one will be raised. His head was before mine, or he was among those whom God has excluded. (Bukhari 2411, Ibn Majah 4274)"
"32345","(32345) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Muriya, on the authority of Talha, the client of Quraysh, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are not one part of a hundred thousand of those who come to me at the basin. We said to Zaid: How old were you that day? He said: Between six hundred and seven hundred. (Abu Dawud 4713. Ahmad 369)"
"32346","(32346) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhayfi, who said: The basin is whiter than Milk, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, and sweeter than musk, its nature is as numerous as the stars in the sky, between Aila and Sana'a, whoever drinks from it will never be thirsty after that. (Ahmed 390)"
"32347","(32347) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And indeed, it is a reminder for you and for your people} It is said: Who is this man from? It is said: From the Arabs, and it is said: From which Arabs? So it is said: From the Quraysh: {And We have raised up your remembrance} I do not mention except that you mention: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger. God"
"32348","(32348) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Hasan: In his saying {Have We not opened your chest to you?}: Yes, Filled with wisdom and knowledge {And We have lifted from you your burden which has burdened your back}, He said: How heavy is the burden on the back {And We have raised up for you your remembrance} Yes, he is not mentioned unless I am mentioned with him."
"32349","(32349) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, On the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, I have names. I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, and I am the Eraser - God erases. In Me is disbelief, and I am the Gatherer. People will be gathered at my feet, and I am the One who will punish. A person said to him: What is the outcome? He said: There is no prophet after him.\n(Bukhari 3533. Muslim 1828)"
"32350","(32350) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhaifi, he said: The Messenger of Allah passed by me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, Al-Muqaffi, and Al-Hashir. (Tirmidhi 368 and Ibn Saad 104)"
"32351","(32351) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Moses said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us names, and some of them we have memorized. He said: I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, Al-Muqaffi, Al-Hashir, the Prophet of Repentance, and the Prophet of the Epic. (Ahmad 404, Ibn Saad 105)"
"32352","(32352) Al-Ala’ ibn Usaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Asma’, On the authority of Thawban, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God has angled the earth for Him, and I have seen its easts and its wests. And my nation’s dominion will reach what has been established for me, and I have been given the red and the white treasures. Hammad said: And I heard him once say: So I gave it to the kingdom of Persia and the Romans, and I asked my Lord for my nation not to destroy it. By His Sunnah with His common people, and He does not give authority over them to an enemy other than themselves. Muhammad, if you make a decree, it will not be rejected, and I give you a guarantee for your nation that I will not destroy it because of your Sunnah, nor will I give power to your people. There is an enemy against them other than themselves who deems their supremacy permissible, even if everyone from among their countries were to gather against them, or he said: whoever Its diameters (Muslim 2215. Abu Dawud 4249) Q."
"32353","(32353) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Amir bin Saad, on the authority of his father: That the Messenger One day, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he came from on high until when he passed the mosque of Banu Muawiyah, he said: He entered and bowed down. We performed two rak'ahs and we prayed with him, and he prayed to his Lord for a long time, then he turned to us and said: I asked my Lord for three, and He granted me. Two and he prevented me from doing one. I asked my Lord not to destroy my nation with the Sunnah, so He gave it to me, and I asked Him not to He will destroy my nation by drowning, so He gave it to me. I asked him not to put their share among them, so she responded to me."
"32354","(32354) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to the tribe of Banu Muawiyah. I followed his trail until he appeared on her, so he prayed eight rak'ahs of long prayer, then he left and said: O Hudhayfah, Is it too long for you? I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: I asked God for three, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to He appeared over my nation and he gave it to me, and I asked him not to destroy it with years, so he gave it to me, and I asked him not to destroy it with years. He does not share their share among them, so He prevented me."
"32355","(32355) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Mara, on the authority of Abd God, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was taken captive, he was taken to the Sidra of the Manta and he is in the heavens. Sixth: And to it will end what comes out of the earth, and some of it will be taken away, and to it will end what comes down. With it from above it, then it is taken from it {when the Sidrā overlays what it covers}. He said: a bed with it made of gold. He said: so it was given to him. Third: He was given the five daily prayers, He was given the last two rings of Surat Al-Baqarah, and He was forgiven from among His nation who does not associate partners with Allah. Inserts.\n(Muslim 279. Ahmad 387)"
"32356","(32356) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhafi: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was brought with Buraq, a long white animal that placed its hoof at its tip. He said: Why? He and Gabriel continued their journey until they came to the Holy House, and the gates of heaven were opened for them, and they saw the jinn. And Hell, Hudhayfah said: He did not pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. (Tirmidhi 3147 and Ahmad 394)"
"32357","(32357) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was taken captive. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was brought with an animal lower than a mule and higher than a donkey. Its hoof was placed at its tip. It was called: Al-Buraq. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a camel belonging to the polytheists, and it dispersed, and they said: O people, what is this? They said: We do not see anything, it is only a smell, until he came to the Holy House, and two vessels were brought, in one of which was wine and The other was milk, so he took the milk, and Gabriel said to him: You have been guided and your nation has been guided. Then he walked to Egypt."
"32358","(32358) Hadith narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, he said: Ibn Abbas said, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: That night I was taken captive, and in the morning in Mecca, I was terrified by my situation, and I knew that the people He lied, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat isolated and sad, then Abu Jahl passed by him and came until he sat next to him. So he said to him like one mocking: Was it from anything? He said: Yes, he said: What is it? He said: I was taken on a journey during the night. He said: Where to? He said: To the Holy House. He said: Then the morning was between our backs? He said: Yes, but he did not see that he was lying for fear that he would deny the hadith if he called his people to it. He said: Should I speak to your people? What did you tell me if I invited them to you? He said: Yes, he said: O people of Banu Ka'b bin Luayyim, come, he said: Then the gatherings dispersed, so they came until they were seated. To them, he said to him: Tell your people what you told me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He was taken captive by night. They said: Where to? He said: To the Holy House. They said: Then you appeared among us in the morning? He said: Yes, he said: Between applauding and placing his hand on his head in astonishment at the lie - he claimed -! They said to me: Can you grant us the mosque? He said: Among the people are those who traveled to that country and saw the mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So I went. I called them, and I continued to call them and I called them until I got confused about some of the adjectives, so he came to the mosque and I was looking at him. Until it was placed below the house of Aqeel - or the house of Aqal -, so I described it while I was looking at it, and he said: The people: As for the description, by God, it was correct. (Nasa’i 11285. Ahmad 309)"
"32359","(32359) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: While Gabriel was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he heard the opposite of Above him, he raised his head and said: A door in heaven has opened that has never been opened before. He said: Then an angel came to him and said: Give good tidings of two lights. You have been given what was not given to those before you: the Openers of the Book and the last of Surat Al-Baqarah. You have not read a letter of it without I gave it to you\n(Muslim 554, Hakim 558)"
"32360","(32360) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, he said: Abdullah bin Qays told me, he said: I was with Ibn Abi Barda one night, and Al-Harith bin Uqish entered upon us, and Al-Harith narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Of my nation there are those who will enter Paradise through your intercession, more than harm."
"32361","(32361) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Zakaria narrated to us, he said: Atiyya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: That the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Of my nation there are those who will intercede for a man and for his family, and they will enter Paradise through his intercession.\n(Tirmidhi 2440. Ahmad 63)"
"32362","(32362) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : I have been harmed for the sake of God and no one is harmed, and I have been harmed for the sake of God and no one is afraid, and a third of what is in between has come upon me. By day and by night, I and Bilal have no food that any man with a liver would eat except what he saw as Bilal’s armpit. (Ibn Majah 151, Ahmed 120)"
"32363","(32363) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Tahaman narrated to me, saying: Samak bin Tahaman narrated to me. Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I do not know of a stone in Mecca that greeted me before If I am sent, I know him now. (Muslim 1782. Tirmidhi 3624)"
"32364","(32364) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Musa bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, God appeared to me in the best of forms and asked me: What did the most exalted eminent dispute with? He said: So I said: My Lord, I have no knowledge of it. He said: Then he placed his hand between my shoulders until I found a piece of clothing between my breasts, or He placed them between my breasts until I found a piece of clothing between my shoulders. He did not ask me about anything but I informed him."
"32365","(32365) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Saad bin Saeed told us, he said: Anas bin Malik told me, he said: He sent me. Abu Talha went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to invite him. He said: So I came and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with the people. He said: He looked at me and I became ashamed, so I said: Answer Abu Talha. He said to the people: Get up. Abu Talha said: O Messenger of God, it is only I made something for you. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, touched it and invoked blessings upon it, and said: Enter a group of My companions were ten, and they ate until they were satisfied, and ten continued to enter and ten left, until not one of them remained. Unless he went in and ate until he was satisfied, then he prepared it, and behold, there was something like it when they ate from it.\n(Muslim 1412, Ahmad 218)"
"32366","(32366) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Ash-Shakhir, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub: A bowl of porridge was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was placed among the people’s hands. So they followed her until noon in the morning, while some people got up and others sat down, and a man said: Oh, Samurah, was she stretching out? Samarra said: What were we astonished by? It was only extended from here and he pointed with his hand to the heavens. (Tirmidhi 3425. Ahmad 18)"
"32367","(32367) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid bin Ayman, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Jabir bin Abdullah: Tell me. With a hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which I heard from him and which I narrated on your authority. Jabir said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of the ditch we dig, we stayed for three days without eating food or being able to eat it. There was a trench in the ditch, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, this is A dog had fallen into the ditch, so we sprinkled water on it. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up with his belly. He was tied up with a stone, so he took the pick or the mop, then he named three, then struck, and it came back as a whole hill.\n When I saw that from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: O Messenger of God, give me permission. So he gave me permission, so I came. My wife, so I said: Your mother is bereaved of you. I have seen something from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I cannot be patient with. So what? Do you have it? She said: I have a saa’ of barley and a bunch of grapes. He said: We ground the barley, slaughtered the bunches, skinned them, and put them in the burma. We kneaded the barley, then I returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and stayed for an hour, and I asked him for permission, and he gave me permission.So I came and saw that the dough had risen, so I ordered her to bake bread, and I set the pot on the dough, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I went to him and said: We have food for us, so if you decide to stay with me, you and one or two men with you, then I will do so."
"32368","(32368) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He died - or was martyred - Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram, so I sought help from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask his debtors to give up any of their debt, but they refused. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Go and classify your dates into different categories, then inform me. He said: So I did and I did. Al-Ajwa individually, and I classified it into different types, then I informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Then he came and sat on its top. Or in the midst of it, then he said: Eat for the people, so I ate for them until I fulfilled them, and these were dates, as if it had not diminished. Something about it (Bukhari 2127, Ahmed 313)"
"32369","(32369) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of Ishaq bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to me one day and said: Invite your companions for me, meaning the companions of the class. So I started following them, man by man, waking them up until I gathered them together. Then we came to the door of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we sought permission. So he gave us permission. Abu Hurairah said: And a sheet of paper was placed in our hands containing the size of a handful of barley. He said: So he placed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laid his hand on her and said: Take in the name of God. So we ate whatever we wanted, then we went away. Help us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when the scrolls were placed: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, he has not spent the night in The family of Muhammad is food other than anything you see, so it was said to Abu Hurairah: As much as it was when you finished. He said: The same as it was then. It was placed but there were traces of fingers on it. (Tabarani 2928)"
"32370","(32370) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Musa Al-Janni narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him say: A prophet said God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those sitting with him one day: Would you be pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Would you be pleased to be half the people of Paradise? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Verily, my nation on the Day of Resurrection will be two-thirds of the people of Paradise. The people on the Day of Resurrection will be One hundred and twenty rows, and my nation is from that, eighty rows.\n(Muslim 2000, Ahmed 453)"
"32371","(32371) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murra, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of Paradise are twenty and a hundred rows, this nation. Of these, there are eighty rows. (Tirmidhi 2546. Ahmad 347)"
"32372","(32372) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Imamah Al-Bailili saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: My Lord promised me that seventy thousand of my nation would be admitted to Paradise, with every thousand Seventy thousand, there is no reckoning upon them, nor punishment, and three times of the times of my Lord. (Tirmidhi 2437. Ahmed 250)"
"32373","(32373) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Al-Harith bin Husayrah narrated to us, he said: Al-Qasim narrated to us. Ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How? You and a quarter of Paradise, for you is a quarter, and for all people three quarters. He said: So they said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: So how about you and a third of it? They said: That is a lot. He said: How about you and half? They said: That is more? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection will be twenty and a hundred rows, you will be eighty rows.\n(Ahmad 453. Abu Ali 5337)"
"32374","(32374) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Badil told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abbad, on the authority of Ka’b, said: The people of Paradise are twenty and one hundred rows, eighty of this nation."
"32375","(32375) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When It reached the end of the tree, when its leaves were like the ears of an elephant, and when its leaves were like the ears of a camel, then when it was overgrown with It is God’s command that He did not cover it. It turned and resembled rubies. (Bukhari 3207, Ahmad 128)"
"32376","(32376) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: I have never smelled musk or amber. Sweeter than the scent of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I have never touched silk or silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 3561, Muslim 1814)"
"32377","(32377) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Dhiyāl ibn Harmālă, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: Accept us with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from a journey, until when we were pushed to one of the walls of Banu al-Najjar, behold, there was a camel in it - It means: raging - no one enters the wall without it being forced upon him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came until he came to the wall. So he called the camel and it came, placing its hilt on the ground until it puddled between its hands. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come. He snatched it and pushed it to his companions, then he turned to the people and said: There is nothing between the heavens and the earth that He does not know. I am the Messenger of God, not disobedient to the jinn or mankind. (Ahmad 310, Darmi 18)"
"32378","(32378) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdul God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I disavow every friend of his character, except that God has decided Your companion is a friend. Waki` said: Because of his vinegar. (Muslim 1856. Tirmidhi 3455)"
"32379","(32379) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, God has angels who travel on earth, informing me of His peace upon His nation."
"32380","(32380) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had no water, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: Ask someone who has some leftover water. He brought water and poured it into a vessel. Then he placed his palm in it and made the water come out. between his fingers, then he said: Hail the blessed bird, and blessings from God. He said: So we drank from it, Abdullah said. We used to listen to the praises of food while we were eating. (Bukhari 3579, Ahmed 401)"
"32381","(32381) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih bin Abdullah Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, he said: We traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I attended the prayer, and a man came with his bounty for healing. So he poured it into a cup and said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution. Then the people brought the rest of the birds and said: Wipe them off. They wiped themselves, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard them, and he said: On your messengers, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, placed his hand in the cup of water, then he said: Make the birds bathe. He said: Then Jabir bin Abdullah said: By the one who I saw water coming out from between the fingers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not even raise his hand. They all performed ablution, and the lions said: I have thought of it. He said: We were two hundred or more. \n(Bukhari 3576. Ahmed 292)"
"32382","(32382) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: I attended the prayer, and someone stood up. He was close to the mosque, so he performed ablution, and some people remained, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with a bowl made of stones. There was water in it, so he put his palm in the bowl, and the bowl was small. He spread his palm in it, so he joined his fingers and performed ablution. All the people. We said: How many were they? He said: Eighty men. (Bukhari 3575. Ahmed 106)"
"32383","(32383) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We descended on the day of Al-Hudaybiyah. We found its water that the first people had drunk, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat at the well, then called for a bucket of it. So he took some of it with his mouth, then poured into it and prayed to God, and its water increased until the people drank from it. (Bukhari 3577. Ahmed 290)"
"32384","(32384) Marwan narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’, he said: Imran bin Al-Hussein narrated to us, he said: We were with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was on a journey, and people complained to him that they were thirsty, so he called so-and-so and called Ali, and he said, “Go and seek water for us.” So they set off and met a woman who had two bazaars or two flats. He said: So they brought her to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for a vessel and emptied it from the mouths of the two troughs, or the two surfaces, then he leaned it down. He opened their mouths, and he released Al-Azali, and it was called to the people: Water and draw water. He said: So he gave water to whoever watered, and he drew to drink from whoever drew water. He said: And it was standing and looking at what was being done with its water. He said: By God, it was removed from it when it was removed, and indeed it appears to us. It is more filled than it was where it began. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By God, We have not provided you with anything. There is nothing in your water, but God gives us something to drink. (Bukhari 344, Muslim 476)"
"32385","(32385) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Amr bin Murrah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Salam narrated to us. He said: Abdullah said: Everything was given to your Prophet except the five keys. And He knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow.\n(Bukhari 1039. Ahmad 386)"
"32386","(32386) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am the master of the descendants of Adam, and I am the first for whom the earth will open, and I am the first to intercede and the first interceded (Tirmidhi 3611)"
"32387","(32387) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: This pulpit of mine is one of the pastures of Paradise that you may graze on. (Ahmad 450, Bayhaqi 247)"
"32388","(32388) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: I heard Hisham saying: Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I race the Arabs. (Ibn Saad 21)"
"32389","(32389) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: God chose Ishmael from the descendants of Abraham, and he chose from the sons of Ishmael, Banu Kinanah. And he chose Quraysh from the Banu Kinanah, and he chose from the Quraysh Banu Hashim, and he chose me from the Banu Hashim. \n(Muslim 1782. Tirmidhi 3606)"
"32390","(32390) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas, who said: Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting sad and some of the people of Mecca had beaten him. He said: So he said: What’s the matter with you? He said: He did these and these. He said: Would you like me to show you a sign? He said: Yes, then he looked at a tree beyond the valley, and said: Call that tree. So he called it and it started walking until it stood between His hand, then he said to her: Go back. She went back until she returned to her place, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is enough for me, it is enough for me. (Ahmad 1131 Darami 23)"
"32391","(32391) Qarad Abu Nuh narrated to us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father, He said: Abu Talib went out to the Levant, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and sheikhs from Quraysh went out with him. They landed and unfastened their packs, and the monk came out to them. Before that, they were passing by, but he did not come out to them, nor He turned around and said: They are dismounting, so he began to penetrate them until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he said: This is the Master of the Worlds, this is the Messenger of the Lord of the Worlds, this is God sent as a mercy to the worlds, so he said to him Sheikhs from Quraysh: What do you know? He said: When you approached Al-Aqaba, not a tree or a stone remained but it fell down in prostration, and they do not prostrate except to a Prophet. (Tirmidhi 3620)"
"32392","(32392) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The steps of my pulpit are places in Paradise. (Ahmad 289. Ibn Hibban 3749)"
"32393","(32393) Hushaym told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been given the summaries of the words, their openings, and their conclusions."
"32394","(32394) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one day. Then the wolves came and howled behind him, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, he said: These wolves have come to inform you. That you distribute to her of your wealth what is appropriate for her, or that you leave her alone so that she may rebel against you. They said: Leave her so that she may rebel against us.\n(Dharmi 22)"
"32395","(32395) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: He was asked: Was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he raises his hand? He said: Yes, the people complained about the gathering and said: O Messenger of God, the rain has failed, the land has become barren, and wealth has perished. He said: So he raised His hand until I saw his armpits, and there were no clouds in the sky, so we did not pray until the strong young man was near the house. He was about to return to his home, so he said: So our gathering was destroyed. He said: So they said: O Messenger of God, the houses were destroyed and confined. Al-Rukban, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, smiled at the haste of the chiefs of the son of Adam, and said: Oh God, protect us and protect us. On us, he said: Then the heavens became clear."
"32396","(32396) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Mughith ibn Sumayyah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: An updated Torah was sent down to me, in which is the light of wisdom and springs of knowledge, so that With it are blind eyes, uncircumcised hearts, and deaf ears, and it is the Most Merciful that bestows the Book. (Dharmi 3327)"
"32397","(32397) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I asked for intercession for my nation, and he said: Seventy thousand are yours. They will enter Paradise without reckoning. I said: Increase me. He said: For every thousand, seventy thousand. I said: Increase me. He said: For it is yours. Such and such and such, so Abu Bakr said: It is sufficient for us. Omar said: O Abu Bakr, leave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then Abu Bakr said: O Omar, we are only a handful of God’s handfuls. (Tirmidhi 2437. Ahmed 250)"
"32398","(32398) Ahmad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Khaled Zayd al-Asadi told us, he said: Aoun ibn Abi Juhayfy al-Sawa’i narrated to me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Aqeel, who said: We set off as a delegation and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and someone from among us said: O Messenger of God, have you not asked your Lord for a king? Like the kingship of Solomon. He laughed and said: Perhaps your companion in the sight of God is better than the kingship of Solomon. Indeed, God did not send a prophet except He gave him a supplication, and among them was he who took this worldly life and was given it, and among them was he who invoked it against his people when they disobeyed him. So they were destroyed, and indeed God gave me a supplication, so I hid it from my Lord in order to intercede for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"32399","(32399) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maymunah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Rifa’a al-Janni, who said: We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: My Lord has promised me that seventy thousand of my nation will enter the jinn without reckoning or torment. (Taalisi 1291, Ahmed 16)"
"32400","(32400) Hushaym told us, he said: Abdul-Malik informed me, he said: I heard Abu Ja`far narrating, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I have been given intercession and it is granted to him who does not associate anything with God."
"32401","(32401) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Issa narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla said: Ubayy bin Ka’b told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: My father, my Lord sent me to recite the Qur’an in one letter, so I responded to him to make it easy for my nation, so he responded to me to recite the Qur’an. On seven letters, and for every reply I returned to you a question that you asked of me. He said: I said: O God, forgive my nation, O God, forgive my nation. Forgive my nation, and I have delayed the third day until a day in which all creation, even Abraham, will desire me. (Muslim 562. Ahmad 127)"
"32402","(32402) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salla, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The people will gather in On one level, sight penetrates them, and the caller hears them, and a herald calls: O Muhammad, upon the heads of the first and the last, and he says May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: May God bless you and grant you peace, and goodness is in your hands. The Mahdi is the one whom you have guided. Blessed are you. And You are exalted, and from You and to You there is no refuge or refuge except to You. Glory be to You, Lord of the House. Blessed are our Lord and exalted be He. Hudhayfah: That is the Praiseworthy Place. (Nasa’i 11294. Tayalisi 414)"
"32403","(32403) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud al-Awdi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, in his saying: {Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy place}, he said: Al-Shafi’iyyah. (Tirmidhi 3137, Ahmad 441)"
"32404","(32404) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Farqad Al-Sabkhi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: A woman brought her son to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, this is his son. He was possessed by a madness that took him at our lunch and dinner, and he became malicious. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped his chest and said goodbye. Then it snarled, and it came out from its belly like a black puppy."
"32405","(32405) Yunus bin Muhammad and Affan told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering a sermon to a trunk, and when he took the pulpit, he turned to him, and the trunk bowed until He took him and embraced him, and he remained calm, and said: If I had not embraced him, he would have longed for the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmad 2661 Darami 39)"
"32406","(32406) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: They came to Sahl bin Saad and said: What is the pulpit of the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: There is no one left who is more knowledgeable about it than me. He said: It is like a jungle, and so-and-so - the servant of so-and-so - made it for the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was leaning against a stump in the mosque and praying. To him when he delivered a sermon. Then when he took the pulpit and sat on it at the end of the trunk, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him. So he made it firm - but in the hadith of Abu Hazim it is not: so he made it firm - until it settled. (Bukhari 448 Muslim 387)"
"32407","(32407) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Wahid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He delivered a speech to the trunk of a palm tree, and a woman from the Ansar said to him: O Messenger of God, I have a carpenter boy. Should I not command him? Will he create a platform for you? He said: Yes, so he took a pulpit, and when it was the day of the Friday prayer, he delivered a sermon from the pulpit. He said: The trunk that was standing He was like a boy. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This man cried when he lost his memory.\n(Bukhari 449. Ahmed 300)"
"32408","(32408) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Waddak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He (peace and blessings of God be upon him) was delivering a sermon to Jadhu’, then a Roman man came to him and said: I will make you a pulpit on which you can deliver the sermon. So he made a pulpit for him. This is what you see. When he stood up and addressed the young camel’s soul, Hanin the camel’s soul, to her two children, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down to him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, took him to him, and he remained at rest, so he ordered him to be buried and a dig made for him. (Darimi 37. Abu Ali 1062)"
"32409","(32409) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Like the previous hadith of Ibn Abbas. (Ibn Majah 1415. Ahmed 249)"
"32410","(32410) Suwayd bin Amr Al-Kalbi and Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had a night with us, and he spread out. Each one of us is the arm of his camel. She woke up one night and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, coming to her, not in front of her. Uhud, so I set off to ask for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw Muadh bin Jabal and Abdullah bin Qais standing. He said: I said: Where is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the top of the valley, and then there was something like the roar of a millstone. We only stayed for a while until... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: Indeed, the night came to me, coming from my Lord, so he gave me the choice to enter half of my nation. Jinnah and among the intercessors, and indeed I chose the intercession. He said: So we said: O Messenger of God, we seek you, God and the Companions, when you have made us Among those who are worthy of your intercession. He said: So you are among those who are worthy of my intercession. He said: Then We approached the people with hugs. He said: And behold, they were terrified. And they lost their Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Indeed, a night came to me, coming from my Lord, so He gave me the choice between entering. Half of my nation is the jinn and among the intercessors, and I chose the intercessors. They said: O Messenger of God, we seek you from God and the Companions, when You have made us among the people of your intercession. When they came upon him, he said: I bear witness from those present that my intercession is for those of your nation who have died, not He associates anything with God. (Ibn Khuzaymah 387)"
"32411","(32411) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: He passed by me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was driving my camel and I was among the last of the people, and he was falling ill, or had become ill, he said: What What's up? So I said: O Messenger of God: He is rising, or he has risen, so he took something that was in his hand and struck it, then said: Ride, so he I was detaining him until they caught me. (Muslim 1222. An-Nasa’i 6235)"
"32412","(32412) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdul told me Al-Aziz, on the authority of Ali bin Murra, who said: I saw three things from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that no one had seen. Before me, and no one will see her after me: I went out with him on a journey until, while we were on some way, we passed by a woman sitting She had a boy with her. She said: O Messenger of God, this son of mine has been afflicted with calamity, and an affliction has befallen us from him. He will be taken away today. I don't know how many times he said: Give it to me, so I took it to him, and he put it between him and his companions on the trip, then he gaped. Then he blew on it three times: In the name of God, I am the servant of God, the most humiliated enemy of God. He said: Then he handed it to her, then he said: We will meet him in He returned to this place, so tell us what he did. He said: So we went and came back, and we found her in that place with her. Three things, and he said: What did your boy do? She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we did not sense anything of it until the Hour, so gather these sheep. He said: Get down and take some of them. One and the rest were rejected.\n He said: I went out with him one day to the graveyard, and when we emerged, he said: Look, woe to you, do you see anything? Waren me? I said: O Messenger of God, I do not see anything hiding you except a tree, which I do not see as hiding you. He said: What is close to it? I said: A tree behind it, and it is like it or close to it. He said: Go to them and tell them that the Messenger of God has prayed. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to meet, by the permission of God Almighty. He said: So they gathered, so he went away for his need, then came back and said: Go to them and say to them: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has commanded you to return to each one of you. Its location\n He said: I was sitting with him one day when a camel came trotting until it hit its calf between its hands, then it left. He looked at him and said: Look, who is this camel? He had an affair, so I went out to look for his owner, and I found him belonging to a man from the Ansar, so I called him to him, and he said: What is the matter with your camel? This? He said: What is the matter with him? He said: I don't know, by God, what's the matter with him? We worked on him and sprinkled water on him until he was unable to water the water, so we made a vow yesterday. That we slaughter him and divide his meat. He said: Do not do that. He will give it to me or on his own behalf. He said: It is yours, O Messenger of God. So he gave it the name of truthfulness, then he sent with it."
"32413","(32413) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, he said: Ismail bin Abdul Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, He said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pass stools. Until he disappears and is not seen, so we camped in a clearing of land in which there were neither trees nor knowledge, and he said: O Jabir, put in it Idawtak Maa, then he set off with us, saying: So we set off so that we could not be seen, and behold, there were two trees, four cubits apart, so he said: Oh. Jabir, go to this tree and tell it: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says to you: Follow your companion until He sat behind you, and she returned to her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat behind them, then they returned to their place.\n So we rode while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Between us it was as if there were birds over our heads providing shade for us.” Then a woman appeared to us. She had a boy of hers with her, and she said: O Messenger of God, this son of mine is taken away by Satan many times every day, so he stopped by her. Then he took the boy and put him between him and the one who was leading the journey, then he said: The most despicable enemy of God. I am the Messenger of God in three. Then he pushed him away. Then, when we had completed our journey, we passed by that place, and the woman appeared to us, with a young boy and two rams with her. They drove them, and she said: O Messenger of God, accept these from me, for the one who sent you with the truth has not returned to him again, so he said: Take One of them, and they responded to the other.\n He said: Then we walked while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us, as if there were birds over our heads, providing shade. Then, when a camel called, When he was between the two satans, he fell down and prostrated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat down, then he said: Upon the people, who is the owner of this? Camel? Then, when a fatwa from the Ansar issued a fatwa to him, they said: He is for us, O Messenger of God. He said: What is the matter with him? They said: We had been with him for twenty years, and he was a generous person, so we wanted to slaughter him and divide him among them. Our servants, so she escaped from us. He said: Will you sell him? They said: No, but he is yours, O Messenger of God. He said: If not, then do good to him. His time will come."
"32414","(32414) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Amr bin al-Ahwas, On the authority of his mother, Umm Jundub, she said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, throwing pebbles at Jamarat Al-Aqaba from the bottom of the valley on the day Al-Nahr while riding an animal, then he departed and a woman from Khath’am followed him, and with her was a young boy who was afflicted with him, and she said: Messenger of God, this is my son and the rest of his family, and he is suffering from an affliction that does not speak. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he greeted: “Bring me some water.” He brought it, washed his hands, and rinsed his mouth. Then he gave it to her and said, “Give me some of it to drink.” And some of his sperm was poured upon him, and God sought healing for him. She said: Then I met the woman and said: If only she had granted me some of his sperm. She said: Only And this is why he was afflicted. So I met a woman who was about to squint and asked her about the boy. She said: He was healed and became of sound mind, not like people’s minds. (Abu Dawud 1961, Ahmed 503 BC)."
"32415","(32415) Aswad bin Amir told us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought me back one day behind him and he was captured. I had a story that I would not tell anyone, and it was something that amazes me, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he concealed There was a target, or a palm tree, to relieve his need. One day he entered the Ansar’s palm tree and saw a camel in it. When he saw it, The camel fell down and its eyes shed tears. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wiped his navels and his secrets and calmed down, so he said: Who is this for? The camel? Or who is the master of this camel? He said: The Ansari said: I am, O Messenger of God, and he said: Be good to him, for he complained to me that you starve him and make him tired. (Abu Dawud 2542, Ahmed 206)"
"32416","(32416) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders: A Jew in Aleppo belonged to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted a she-camel and said: Oh God, make him beautiful, so his hair turned black."
"32417","(32417) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Husayn bin Waqid told me, he said: Ibn Nahik told me, he said: I heard Amr bin Akhtab Abu Zayd Al-Ansari says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked for water and I brought him a cup. There were hairs on it, so he took them out and said: Oh God, make him beautiful, for I saw him when he was ninety-four years old, and what was in it? His head is a white cap.\n(Tirmidhi 3429. Ahmad 341)"
"32418","(32418) Mu’ali bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hamza, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Yusuf bin Suleiman, on the authority of his grandmother, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Hamq: He gave the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, drink milk, and he said: Oh God, grant him sustenance. In his youth, eighty years have passed since he has not seen a single white hair. (Musnad 864)"
"32419","(32419) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’di, on the authority of a man who narrated to him, on the authority of Umm Malik Al-Ansariyah said: Umm Malik brought a stick of ghee to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave orders. May God bless him and grant him peace. He squeezed it, then pushed it to her and she returned, and behold, it was full. So she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and she said: Was it revealed about anything, O Messenger of God? He said: What is that, Umm Malik? She said: You returned my gift to me. He said: So he called Bilal and asked him about that, and he said: By the one who He sent you with the truth. I squeezed her until I was ashamed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Congratulations to you, mother. What's wrong with you, this is a blessing. May God hasten your reward for you. Then he taught her to say ten times at the end of every prayer: Glory be to God. Praise be to God ten times, and God is greater ten times. (Ahmad 340. Tabarani 351)"
"32420","(32420) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid al-Fayshi, on the authority of his son To Khabab, she said: My father went out on a campaign during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was there. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He used to work with us and he would milk goats for us. He used to milk them in our vines and they would be full. When Khabbab came, He used to milk her, but he milked her again. (Ahmad 372. Ibn Saad 290)"
"32421","(32421) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {And when We took from the prophets their covenant, and from you and from Noah.\n(Ahmad 127, Ibn Hibban 6404)"
"32422","(32422) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Ma’an narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us one day and he was angry, and we saw A[corrupt] with him. Gabriel, he said: I have never seen a person who wept more and was more content than him. He said: Ask me, for by God you will not ask me about... Nothing except that I informed you about it. He said: Then a man got up to him and said: O Messenger of God, am I in Jinnah or in Hell? He said: No, but in Hell. He said: Then another one got up to him and said: O Messenger of God, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafiya. He said: Then another one came up to him and said: Should we perform Hajj every year? He said: If I had said it, it would have become obligatory, and if it had become obligatory, you would not have done it, and if you had not performed it, you would have been punished.\n He said: Then Omar bin Al-Khattab stood up and said: We are satisfied with God as our Lord, with Islam as our religion, and with Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as our Messenger. Messenger of God, we were the custodians of a covenant with the people of Jahiliya, so do not reveal our secrets, do not reveal our secrets, and pardon us, may God pardon you. He said: So he walked away from him, then he turned towards the wall and said: I have never seen good and evil like today. I saw heaven and hell. Without this wall. (Bukhari 931 Muslim 1832)"
"32423","(32423) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Gabriel was late for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was greatly alarmed, and Khadija said to him: I see that your Lord has troubled you because of what he sees of your distress. He said: So it was revealed: {And by the forenoon and by the night when it is silent, your Lord has not left you, nor has He diminished}"
"32424","(32424) Amr bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Asbat bin Nasr al-Hamdani, on the authority of Samak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the first prayer, then he went out to his family and I went out with him, and two sons met him. So he started wiping the cheeks of one of them, one by one, and said: As for me, he wiped my cheeks, and I found his hand feeling cool and smelly, as if he had taken it out. From your body is a perfumer. (Muslim 1814. Tabarani 1944)"
"32425","(32425) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Bishr, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about Al-Kawthar? He said: This is the abundant goodness that God has given him."
"32426","(32426) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: He is the Prophet and the best that God gave him"
"32427","(32427) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Falayt, on the authority of Jisra, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he prayed one night and repeated verses until morning, with which he bowed and with which he prostrated {Indeed You punish them, for they are your servants.} He said: I said: O Messenger of God, you continued to repeat these verses until the morning. He said: Indeed I asked my Lord for intercession for my nation, and this will be granted to him who does not associate anything with God. (Bayhaqi 13)"
"32428","(32428) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: When God revealed: “My father’s hands remained forbidden.” Lahab} Abu Lahab’s wife came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr was with him, so Abu Bakr said: The Prophet of God, that she will harm you, so he said: There will come a dispute between me and her. He said: She did not see him, so she said to Abu Bakr: Your friend came to us and said: By God, he does not speak poetry or say it. She said: You are a believer. He said: So I rushed back to him, and he said: Abu Bakr: O Messenger of God, she did not see you. He said: And he said: There is no longer an angel between me and her who conceals me until She went (Ibn Hibban 6511, Abu Ali 25)"
"32429","(32429) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: My example and the example of the two prophets is that of a man who built a house and completed it except for one brick, so I came and completed it. That is milk. (Muslim 1791. Ahmad 9)"
"32430","(32430) Affan narrated to us, he said: Sulaym bin Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Saeed bin Mina narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets is like a man who built a house, and he completed it and completed it except for one place. Milk, so people began to enter it and marvel at it and say: If it were not for the location of the milk, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said hello: I came to the place of bricks and sealed the prophets. (Bukhari 3534, Muslim 1791)"
"32431","(32431) Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidi, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: A man came to The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, I have come from a neighborhood where no shepherd comes to them, but no shepherd comes to them. So, pray to God for us, and he said: O God, give water to your country and your livestock, and spread your mercy. He said: Then he prayed and said: O God, give us rain. Helping, soothing, horrifying, good and bestowing, quick and not harmful, beneficial and not harmful. He said: It did not descend until it came to anyone in front of him. Of the faces except that he said: We have given rain and given us life. (Abu Dawud 1200; Ibn Majah 1270)"
"32432","(32432) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, who conveyed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I have been sent as a sealer and a conqueror, and the hadith has been summarized for me in brief, so do not let the polytheists destroy you.\n(Abdul Razzaq 20062)"
"32433","(32433) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: I was sent to complete good morals. (Ahmad 381, Hakim 613)"
"32434","(32434) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, he said: Zayd bin Qadamah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Muslim, he said: He said: The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace - or whomsoever God wills among them - said: O Messenger of God, we have not entrusted that we should separate from you in this world. If you had died, you would have been raised above us and we would not have seen you. Then God revealed: {And whoever obeys God and the Messenger - those are with those whom God has bestowed. Among them are the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and these are good companions. (Tabarani 12559)"
"32435","(32435) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, he said: Zayed told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, he said: When it was revealed This is the verse {The Messenger believed in what was sent down to him from his Lord}, Gabriel said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, God has The best of praise be upon you and your nation. Ask and it will be given to you. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited[corrupt] And he recited these verses until he concluded them with: {Allah does not burden a soul except within its capacity} until the end of the verse. (Tabari 153)"
"32436","(32436) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman Al-Alaf told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali: In his saying: {And he recites it A witness from Him}, he said: He is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, a witness from God. (Ibn Jarir 14)"
"32437","(32437) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out He and Abu Bakr arrived at Medina. Suraqih bin Malik followed them, and when he saw them he said: These are Quraysh that would have fled if they had returned to them. Quraysh gave her a ride, he said: Then his horse wrapped around them, he said: The horse became loose, he said: So pray to God to let her out, and not The closest of the two of you. He said: So she left and came back until he did that twice, or three times. He said: Damn it, miserable. Then he said: Do you have anything but provisions? And the lambs? They said: We do not want to, nor do we have any need for that. Save yourself from us. He said: I am sufficient for you both. (Ibn Saad 232)"
"32438","(32438) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Moses asked his Lord He asked: {And Moses chose from his people seventy men} until he reached {written with them in the Torah and the Gospel} so he was given to her. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bazzar 2213)"
"32439","(32439) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: He was in a shield. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a ram that was painted, and that was unfortunate for him, so in the morning God had taken it away."
"32440","(32440) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, he said: I mentioned The prophets are with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he was mentioned, he said: That is the friend of God. (Muslim 1855. Ahmad 377)"
"32441","(32441) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I will be the most followed of the prophets on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to knock on the door of Heaven\n(Muslim 1888, Abu Ali 3946)"
"32442","(32442) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people I am only a Mercy and a Guide. (Ibn Saad 1920 Darmi 15)"
"32443","(32443) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy, on the authority of his father He said: A man said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if I made all of your prayers a prayer upon you? He said: Then God is sufficient for you. He worries you about the affairs of this world and the hereafter."
"32444","(32444) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Pray upon me, for indeed, praying upon me is purification for you, and ask God for the means for me. They said: What is the means? Messenger of God? He said: The highest level in Paradise, only one man can attain it. I hope that I will be him."
"32445","(32445) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever prays one blessing upon me, may God’s prayers be upon him ten times."
"32446","(32446) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Amr, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays one blessing upon me, may God pray ten blessings upon him, and spares him Ten bad deeds."
"32447","(32447) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Musa bin Yaqoub al-Zam’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Kaysan told me, He said: Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al Hadad told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: The people closest to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who will pray the most for me. (Tirmidhi 484, Ibn Hibban 911)"
"32448","(32448) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Suleiman the client of Al-Hasan bin Ali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day and there was joy. His face, so they said: O Messenger of God, do we see happiness in your face? He said: The king came to me and said: O Muhammad, would you not be satisfied with the fact that no one from your nation prays upon you except that I pray upon him? Ten times, and no one from your nation will greet you except that I greet him ten times? He said: Yes."
"32449","(32449) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidy, who said: Qays ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi narrated to me. Sa`sa`a, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdul Rahman bin Awf: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: I prostrated in gratitude for what He has bestowed upon me among my nation: Whoever sends a blessing upon me, ten good deeds are recorded for him, and ten good deeds are omitted from him. Bad deeds."
"32450","(32450) Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, he said: A man from Banu Asad narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that he said: Whoever prays Upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ten good deeds were recorded for him, ten bad deeds were removed from him, and ten degrees were raised for him."
"32451","(32451) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays upon me, the angels will continue to pray upon him as long as He prays for me, so let the servant say it a little or a lot."
"32452","(32452) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Raqqashi, he said: An angel is entrusted with the one who sends blessings upon me. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to report it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that so-and-so from your nation prayed On you"
"32453","(32453) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who I was mentioned to him, but he forgot to pray for me and made a mistake on the way to Paradise on the Day of Resurrection. (Ibn Majah 908)"
"32454","(32454) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Badr bin Uthman, who said: I heard Ikrimah. He said: Al-Kawthar is what the Messenger of God gave him. May God’s blessings and peace be upon him, of goodness, prophethood, and Islam."
"32455","(32455) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Ata’, he said: {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar}, he said: a basin in Paradise. It was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"32456","(32456) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Badr bin Uthman, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: When it was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Quraysh said: Muhammad was amputated from among us, so they revealed: {Indeed, what will happen to you is the amputee}: The one who threw it at you is the amputee. (Tiberius 330)"
"32457","(32457) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya’la, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, who said: No. We prefer anyone over our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we do not prefer anyone over Abraham, the friend of God."
"32458","(32458) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not choose between the prophets. (Bukhari 6916 and Muslim 1845)"
"32459","(32459) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he recited it to him at the end of al-Baqarah until, when he had memorized it, he said: Recite it to me. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited it to him, and he made Gabriel says: That is for you, that is for you {Do not hold us accountable if we forget or make a mistake}. (Ibn Jarir 160)"
"32460","(32460) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: If you wish, We will give you the keys of the earth and its treasures, and that will not deprive you of anything in the Hereafter, and if you wish, we will gather them for you. In the Hereafter, he said: No, but rather gather them for me in the Hereafter, and then the following verse was revealed: {Blessed is He who, if He wills, will make for you better than that, gardens that you may flow with. Beneath it are rivers, and He will make for you palaces."
"32461","(32461) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud: He said: I was a young boy who tended sheep for Uqba bin Abi Mu’ait, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr - who had fled from the polytheists - and they said: O boy, do you have some milk to give us drink? I said: I am entrusted, and I am not your leg. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have any trunk on which he has not stepped? The stallion? I said: Yes, so I brought her to you, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, seized her, wiped the udder and said goodbye, and the udder was filled with water. Then Abu brought it to him. A virgin found a rock with a sinkhole - or a hole in it - so he milked in it, and he drank and Abu Bakr drank, then she drank, then he said to the udder: Reduce it, so he reduced it, and said: I came to him after that and said: Teach me this saying. He said: You are a learned boy."
"32462","(32462) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: It was for Omar. There was a right on a Jewish man, so he came to him looking for him and met him, and Omar said to him: No, by the one who chose Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted the humans. I will not separate from you while I ask you for something. The Jew said: God did not choose Muhammad over the humans, so he slapped him. Omar, and he said: Between you and me, Abu al-Qasim, and he said: Omar said: No, by the one who chose Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace over mankind. I said to him: God did not choose Muhammad above all mankind, so he reassured me, and he said: As for you, O Omar, I am satisfied with your smack, yes. A Jew, Adam is God’s friend, Abraham is God’s friend, Moses is God’s salvation, Jesus is God’s spirit, and I am God’s lover. Yes, O Jew, you call God by two names. He named my nation “Peace” and He called my nation “Muslims” and “The Believer” and He called my nation “believers.” Yes, O Jew. You asked for a day reserved for us, today is for us and tomorrow is for you, and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians. Yes, O Jews, you are the first and we are the first. others who preceded the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, the jinn was forbidden to the prophets until they entered it, and it was forbidden to the nations. Until your nation enters it."
"32463","(32463) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And he saw it. Another revelation}, he said: He saw his Lord. (Tirmidhi 3280)"
"32464","(32464) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told us, he said: A man from Banu Salman bin Saad told me, On the authority of his mother: That her maternal uncle Habib bin Fuwayk told her: That his father took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. His eyes were bright and he could not see anything with them. So he asked him: What happened to him? He said: I was training my horses, and my foot fell on a snake's egg, and my eyesight was injured, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ran out. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he saw. He said: I saw him inserting the thread into the needle, and he was eighty years old. And his eyes are gleaming."
"32465","(32465) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Umar Mawla Ghufari, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad, from Ali’s descendants, told me: When Ali described the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: It was not long and obscure, nor short and hesitant. He was one of the men, he had curly hair, but he was not curly, nor was he curly. He was a curly man, but he was not With Mutahim, or Al-Mukalathum, there was a roundness in the face, white with a reddish hue, it irritated the eyes, he was polite. The labia, the soles of the epiphyses and cleats, are bare, with a covering, bent with the palms and feet, and when he walks they are shriveled as if He walks slowly, and when he turns, he turns together, between his shoulders is the Seal of the Prophethood, and he is the Seal of the Prophets, the most generous of people. He was the most courageous of the people, the most sincere in his speech, the most fulfilling of the people’s obligation, the most generous of people, and the most generous to them. Whoever sees him in person loves him, and whoever acquaints with him loves him, and his address says: I have never seen anything like him before, nor After him \n(Ahmad 89 and Ibn Saad 410)"
"32466","(32466) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra, who said: It was in the legs of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Hamousha, and he would not laugh except with a smile, and when I looked, I would say: He has kohl on his eyes, not With the best (Abu Ali 7424)"
"32467","(32467) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ali: It is The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, described: He had a great visage, white with a red streak, a huge beard. The collar, the palms and feet are long, the hair is long, the hair is thick, the feet are curled. His walk was as if he was descending into a mountain, neither long nor short. I had never seen anything like it before him or after him. (Ibn Hibban 6311 and Ahmad 134)"
"32468","(32468) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simmak: He heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: It was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he had combed the front of his head and his beard, and when he applied oil, then combed it, it was not brown, and it was There is a lot of hair on the beard, and a man said: Is your face like a sword? He said: No, rather it was like the sun and the moon, round, and I saw the ring between his shoulders, like the white of a dove. It resembles his body. (Muslim 1823. Ahmad 104)"
"32469","(32469) Dhu narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid the Persian, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me during sleep during the time of Ibn Abbas upon insight. He said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Indeed, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In sleep, he said: Can you describe this man whom you saw? I said: Yes, I described to you a man between the two legs, whose body and flesh are dark in white, good-natured, with kohl-colored eyes. The beautiful circles of his face were filled with his beard from here to there - and he pointed with his hand to his temple - until... It almost filled his throat - Awf said: I do not know what this adjective was - so Ibn Abbas said: If only I had seen him in You cannot describe it more than this. (Ahmed 361)"
"32470","(32470) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not asked. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, never said anything and said: No. (Bukhari 6034, Muslim 1805)"
"32471","(32471) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present the letter to Gabriel during every Ramadan. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. From the night in which what is presented is morning, and it is more beautiful than the scent sent. No. He asks for something but gives it to him."
"32472","(32472) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas: that Abu Bakr was a companion The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled from Mecca to Medina, and Abu Bakr used to travel to the Levant. He said: He was known The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not known, so they used to say: O Abu Bakr, who is this boy among the people? Your hand, he said: This is the one who guides the path, he said, and when they approached Medina, they descended upon the heat, and sent to the Ansar. So they came. He said: I saw him on the day he entered Medina, but I have never seen a day better or brighter than the day he entered upon us. And I witnessed him on the day he died, and I have not seen a day more uglier or more unjust than the day he died, may the prayers of God be upon him. And His mercy and His pleasure be upon him.\n(Ahmad 122, Tirmidhi 3618)"
"32473","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(32473) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu`man, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us and said: The first of creation to be clothed in the garment of Abraham.\n(Muslim 2194. Tirmidhi 3167)"
"32474","(32474) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Abu Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr: {And Ibrahim, who He fulfilled} He said: He conveyed what he was commanded to do."
"32475","(32475) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The shelters are the supplications. He wants {Indeed, Abraham is his captain}"
"32476","(32476) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: O best of creation. He said: That is Abraham. (Muslim 1839. Abu Dawud 4639)"
"32477","(32477) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: People will be gathered naked and barefoot, and the first to be met with the garment of Abraham will be."
"32478","(32478) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: When Abraham, peace be upon him, finished building It was said to the Ancient House: “Call the people to perform the Hajj.” He said: My Lord, how can my voice reach? He said: Give permission and upon me is the delivery. Then Abraham, peace be upon him, said: O people, the Hajj to the Ancient House has been decreed upon you. He said: He heard it from the heavens to the earth. Don’t you see that people are coming from the ends of the earth seeking prayers?"
"32479","(32479) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah bin Ma’n narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Go Ibrahim the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in trouble and was not able to eat, so he passed by a red basket, took some of it, and then He returned to his family, and they said: What is this? He said: Red wheat. He said: So they opened it and found it to be red wheat. He said: And when he planted some of it, a spike of corn came out. Its root to its branch is an interwoven love."
"32480","(32480) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: When Abraham was shown the kingdom of heaven And on earth, he saw a servant committing an indecent act, so he supplicated for him and was destroyed, then he saw another servant who supplicated for him and was destroyed, so God said: Come down. My servant, My servants will not destroy you."
"32481","(32481) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: It was sent for Ibrahim, peace be upon him. Two hungry lions, he said: So they licked it and prostrated to it."
"32482","(32482) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malil, on the authority of Ali: Concerning his saying: {O universal fire Coolness and peace be upon Abraham. He said: Had he not said {and peace}, coldness and peace would have killed him."
"32483","(32483) Khalid ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Thabit, he said: Musa, the servant of Abu Bakra, narrated to me. He said: narrate to me. Saeed bin Jubayr said: When I saw Abraham, peace be upon him, in a dream, slaughtering Isaac, he walked with him for a month’s journey in the morning. One until the slaughterer brought maniy, and when God prevented him from slaughtering, he brought a ram and slaughtered it, then returned with it a month’s journey. In one soul, valleys and mountains were folded for him."
"32484","(32484) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Abu Sulayman, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: The fire has not burned Ibrahim except his trustworthy people."
"32485","(32485) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid. Ibn Umair, on the authority of his father, said: Moses said: O Lord: You mentioned Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, why did you give that to them? He said: Abraham did not treat me in any way except that he chose me, and Ishaq made his own sacrifice for me, so he is better than anyone else. And I never put Jacob through any calamity without it increasing his good opinion of me."
"32486","(32486) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Mujahid: {And he announced to the people the Hajj} He said: When Abraham was commanded To announce the call to Hajj, so he stood up and said: O people, answer your Lord. So they answered him: O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God, O God."
"32487","(32487) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And when Abraham was tested by his Lord With words that he completed. He said: He was tested with the verses that came after them."
"32488","(32488) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: {And when his Lord tested Abraham with words} He said: From them. Circumcision"
"32489","(32489) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And when his Lord tested him, With words} He said: No one was tested with this religion and established it except Abraham, peace be upon him."
"32490","(32490) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The first A word that Abraham said when he was thrown into the Fire: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs."
"32491","(32491) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed: Abraham was the first of the people to host a guest. And the first of people to be circumcised, and the first of people to trim his nails, trim his moustache, and use the sunshade."
"32492","(32492) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id: that Abraham, peace be upon him, was the first to see He turned gray hair and said: O Lord, what is this? He said: Dignity. He said: O Lord, increase my dignity."
"32493","(32493) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Othman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father: He said: The first person to deliver a sermon on the pulpit was Ibrahim Khalil, peace be upon him."
"32494","(32494) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {So We did not find therein anything other than a house of Muslims.} He said: Lot. Peace be upon him and his two daughters."
"32495","(32495) Abu Asama narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: Jundub said, he said Hadeeth: When the messengers were sent to the people of Lot to destroy them, it was said to them: Do not destroy them until they bear witness against them. Lot three times. He said: And their way was with Abraham, peace be upon him. He said: So they came to Abraham. He said: And when they gave him the good news of They gave him good tidings. He said: {When the terror had departed from Abraham and good tidings came to him, he would argue with us regarding the people of Lot.} He said: And it was that I was arguing with him. O you, he said: Have you considered that if there were fifty Muslims therein, would I destroy them? They said: No. He said: Have you seen if there were forty in it? He said: They said: No, until he came to ten, or five - Hamid doubted that - He said: They said: So they went to Lot and he He was working on his land. He said: He considered them to be human beings. He said: Then he approached them in secret until the evening came to his family.\n He said: So they walked with him, and he turned to them. He said: And you do not know what these people are doing? They said: What do they do? He said: There is no one among the people who is worse than you. He said: So they put on their clothing according to what he said, and they walked with him. He said: Then he said something like this. So he repeated something like this to them three times. He said: Then he took them to his family. He said: Then his old wife went away. The bad - to his people, and she said: Lot entertained men last night. I have never seen men with better faces than them, nor The best smell from them.\n He said: They came rushing to him until they pushed him at the door to the point that they almost defeated him. He said: Then he gave him shelter to an angel. One of them with his wing, and the lowest of them clapped it. He said: And Lot mounted the door and rose with it. He said: So he began to address them: {These are your daughters. I am purer for you, so fear God and do not disgrace me in my presence. Is there not among you a man of sound judgment? He said: They said: “You have known what we have.” There is any right in your daughters, and indeed, you know what we want. He said: And He said: “If only I had strength over you, or sheltered myself in a strong corner.” He said: They said: {O Lot, indeed, we are messengers of your Lord. They will never reach you.} He said: That was when he learned that they were messengers of God, then he read to his saying: {Is not the morning near?}\n He said: And an angel said: So he swung his wings like this - meaning: like a beating - and none of them fainted that night. Except blindness. He said: So they spent the night blind, awaiting the torment. He said: And he took his family. He said: Gabriel asked permission to enter. I destroyed them, so permission was given to him, and he took up the land that they were on. He said: So he took it until the people of the heavens of the world heard it. The grudge of their dogs, he said, then he turned to them, he said: So his wife heard him - he means: Lot, peace be upon him - the duty and With him, she turned around and the torment befell her. He said: And she pursued their journey with stones."
"32496","(32496) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Musa, peace be upon him, came out calling: Labbaika, he said: And the mountains of spirits will answer him."
"32497","(32497) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Saeed: A man from the Ansar heard a Jewish man while he was in the market, saying: By the one whom Moses chose over mankind. So he struck his face and said: How evil is it, Ali Abul-Qasim? Then the Jew went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Abu al-Qasim, so-and-so struck his face, so he sent So he called him and said: Why did you hit him in the face? He said: I passed by him in the market and I heard him say: By the one whom Moses chose to Humans, then I was seized with anger and hit him in the face. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not choose between Prophets, people will be shocked on the Day of Resurrection, so I raise my head, and behold, I am with Moses, taking one of the pillars of the Throne. I know who should be shocked among those who were shocked and recovered before me, or who was held accountable for his first shock, or who said: His first shock was enough for him."
"32498","(32498) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith. On the authority of Kaab, he said: God divided His words and vision between Moses and Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Moses spoke to him. Twice, and Muhammad saw him twice. (Hakim 575)"
"32499","(32499) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad - and he was one of most of the people. Or from the people who narrated, on the authority of the Children of Israel - he said: He narrated to us that the fragments whom Pharaoh named were among the Children of Israel. Six hundred thousand, and Pharaoh's lead was seven hundred thousand, each man of them on a horse, with a white sash on his head. And in his hand was a war, and he was behind them in blood. When Moses, peace be upon him, led the Children of Israel to the sea, she said: Children of Israel: Wherever you promised us, this sea is in our hands, and here Pharaoh and his soldiers have attacked us or behind us. So Musa, peace be upon him, said to the sea: Abu Khalid has broken down. He said: I will not break up for you, Musa. I am more advanced than you in character, or more powerful. He said: Then it was called: “Strike the sea with your staff,” so it struck “and it split.”\n Al-Jariri said: They were twelve tribes, and each tribe had its own way. When the first of Pharaoh’s soldiers reached On the sea, the horses feared the flames, and one of them appeared to a horse as a young horse, and it smelled its scent, so the horses began to follow it bravely, so when The last of Pharaoh's soldiers was completed in the sea. The last of the children of Israel came out of the sea and fell upon them, so the children of Israel said: He did not die. Pharaoh, and he was never going to die, so he said: No longer had he heard God denying his prophet, so he threw him on the coast. As if it were a red bull, seen by the children of Israel. (Ibn Jarir 19)"
"32500","(32500) His youth narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud: When Moses, peace be upon him, was captured by the Children of Israel, he informed Pharaoh, so he ordered a sheep to be slaughtered. Then he said: No, by God. It will not be finished skinning it until six hundred thousand Copts gather to me. He said: Then Moses, peace be upon him, set off until he reached The sea, so he said to him: Split. So he said: the sea: You were arrogant, O Moses. Did you ever separate for any of the descendants of Adam and he would part for you?\n He said: And with Moses, peace be upon him, was a man on a horse of his own, and that man said to him: Where was your command, O Prophet of God? He said: I was not commanded except in this manner. He said: So he swung his horse and swam with it and he came out, and said: Where were you commanded, O Prophet of God? He said: I was not commanded except with this face. He said: By God, I have not lied, nor have I been told a lie. He said: Then he broke into the second one and glorified it, then He came out and said: Where was your command, O Prophet of God? He said: I was not commanded except in this manner. He said: By God, I have not lied, nor have I been told a lie. He said: Then God revealed to Moses, peace be upon him: {To strike with your staff} So Moses struck with his staff {and it split, and each group was like a great mountain} like a great mountain, and it was Therein are twelve paths for twelve tribes, each tribe having a path of their own. When the companions of Moses went out and the companions of Pharaoh were completed The sea met them and drowned them."
"32501","(32501) On the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Jabir: {So whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth was struck by lightning, except whom God willed.} He said: Moses is among those whom God has excluded."
"32502","(32502) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amara ibn Abd, on the authority of Ali, He said: Moses and Aaron, peace be upon them, set out, and a hand and a hand went, and they came to a mountain in which there was a bed, and Aaron slept on it and was arrested. His soul, so Moses returned to his people, and they said: You killed him, you envied us for his character, or for his softness, or for his speech. Similar to this - doubt from Sufyan - he said: How can I kill him while his sons are with him? He said: So choose whomever you wish. He said: So choose ten from each tribe. He said: That is what He said: {And Moses chose his people seventy men} So they came to him and said: Who killed you, O Aaron? He said: No one killed me, but God caused me to die. They said: O Moses! You disobeyed after that. He said: Then the tremor seized them. Then he began to hesitate to the right and to the left and say: {If you wished, you could have destroyed them before. And shall I destroy you because of what the foolish among us have done? It is nothing but a trial against you. He said: So he called upon God, and He gave them life and made them prophets. Speak to them (Ibn Jarir 73)"
"32503","(32503) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, on the authority of `Umar ibn Al-Khattab, that when Moses, peace be upon him, reached the waters of Madyan, he found a group of people drinking water, so when they had finished, they returned the rock to Ali. The well, and only ten men could lift it, and then two women left.\n He said: What is wrong with you? So I told him, so he came to the stone and he lifted it up, then he did not draw but one sin until the sheep were seen and returned. The two women went to their father and told him, and Moses, peace be upon him, turned to the shade and said: {My Lord, indeed, for what You have sent down to me is good. poor}"
"32504","(32504) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When Moses came to his people and ordered them to pay zakat, Qarun gathered them together and said: This has come to you. With fasting and prayer and with the things you are able to do, are you willing to give him your money? They said: We cannot afford to give him our money, so what do you think? He said: I think that we should send to the oppressor of the Children of Israel and order her to throw it at the heads of the rabbis and the people because he wanted it. On herself, so they did so, and Moses, peace be upon him, spread the peace over the heads of the people, so he prayed to God over them, so God Almighty revealed to the earth If I obey Him, then Moses, peace be upon him, said to her: Take them. So she took them to their heels, and they started saying: O Moses. Moses said: Take them, so I took them to their knees. He said: So they started saying: O Moses, oh Moses. He said: Take them. So I took them to their custody, and they started saying, “O Moses, O Moses.” He said, “Take them.” So I took them to their necks. So they started saying: O Moses, oh Moses. He said: So I took them and hid them, so God Almighty revealed to Moses about him. Peace: O Moses, my servants asked you and pleaded with you, but you refused to answer them. By Your glory, if they called on me, I answered them. (Hakim 408)"
"32505","(32505) Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Qays, on the authority of Salma ibn Kuhayl: {And I cast upon you a burden of From Me} He said: I have endeared you to My servants."
"32506","(32506) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And We brought him near in salvation} until he heard the squeak of the pen."
"32507","(32507) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked Which of the two terms did Moses, peace be upon him, decide? He said: He fulfilled them and completed them."
"32508","(32508) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He was asked: Which of the two terms did Moses decide? He said: He completed them and the last of them. (Hamidi 535, Bazar 2246)"
"32509","(32509) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Manyal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: In His saying: {Do not be like those who annoyed Moses, but God cleared him of what they said, and he was honorable in the sight of God} He said: His people said to him: He turned away, he said: So he went out one day to wash himself, and put his clothes on a rock, and the rock came out holding his clothes tight. He went out and followed her naked until she brought him to the gatherings of the children of Israel. He said: They saw him not turning away. He said: That's it. His saying {So God cleared him of what they said, and he was honorable with God}"
"32510","(32510) Abu Asama told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Khalas bin Amr and Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: In His saying: {O you who have believed, do not be like those who annoyed Moses, but God cleared him of what they said, and he was with God. And well} He said: Among those who harmed him was that a group of the Children of Israel said: Moses would not hide this veil from us except from A blemish on one’s skin: either leprosy, or disease, or blindness, and God wanted to clear him of what they said: He said: And indeed, Moses Peace be upon him, one day alone, he placed his garment on a stone, then he went in to wash himself, and when he finished, he put on his garment. To take it apart from the stone with his garment, so Moses, peace be upon him, took his staff in his wake and started saying: My garment, oh stone! My dress, oh stone! Until he came to a group of the Children of Israel and saw him naked, and behold, he was like the best-mannered man, so God cleared him of what They say, he said: The stone stood up and took his garment and put it on, and Moses began striking the stone with his staff. By God, there is now in the stone Moses' strike left scars, whether three, four, or five. (Ahmad 514, Tabari 51)"
"32511","(32511) Abu Asama told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When you subjected the wind to Suleiman bin Dawud, peace be upon him He would come in the morning from Jerusalem and visit Fazira, then go and spend the night in Kabul."
"32512","(32512) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Dirar bin Murra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Sulaiman was Six hundred thousand chairs will be placed for it."
"32513","(32513) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Suleiman bin Dawood, peace be upon him, used to place six hundred thousand chairs for him, and then the nobles of mankind would come so that they could sit. From what is next to the right, then the nobles of the jinn will come until they sit from what is next to the left, then he calls the birds and they shade them, then He calls for the wind and it carries them, so he travels in one morning the journey of a month, while one day he He was walking through a clearing of earth and needed water, so he called the hoopoe and it came and pecked the earth and reached the place of water, then it came. The devils seize that water, so they flay it just as a human skin is flayed, and they extract water from it.\n He said: Then Nafi’ ibn al-Azraq said to him: Stop, Waqaf. Did you see what you said, the hoopoe comes and pecks the earth and strikes a place? How can he see this when he does not see the trap? It comes to him until it falls on his neck. So Ibn Abbas said to him: Woe to you, destiny has prevented sight."
"32514","(32514) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: Solomon’s throne was being placed On the wind and the chairs of whoever he wanted, among the jinn and mankind. He needed water, but they did not know its location. He checked the birds at that time and did not He found the hoopoe and threatened him, and his torment was plucking him and basking him in the sun. He said: When he came, the birds met him and they said: He threatened you. Solomon, and he said: Did he make an exception? They said: Yes, unless you bring an excuse, and his excuse was that he brought news of his companion from Sheba. He said: So Solomon wrote to them: {Indeed, it is from Solomon, and it is in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Do not you rise above me and come to me in submission}"
"32515","(32515) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Karim, who said: I heard Mujahid say: When he said: {I will bring it to you Before you get up from your place} This, he said: I want to hasten more than this, {The one who has knowledge of the Book said, I will bring it to you Before your limb returns to you.} He said: Then the throne emerged from a tunnel from the earth."
"32516","(32516) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {Before you rise from your position} He said: The sitting place of a man in which he sits until he leaves it."
"32517","(32517) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit ibn Amara, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ma`abad al-Zamani, who said: {In the Name of God, Most Gracious} was not revealed. The Most Merciful} in any part of the Qur’an except in Surah An-Naml {Indeed, it is from Solomon, and it is in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful}"
"32518","(32518) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr: {Before he returns to you. Your limb} He said: He raised his limb and did not return to it until he looked at the throne between his hands."
"32519","(32519) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih: {And indeed, I am sending it to them with a gift} He said: It was I gave her bricks of gold."
"32520","(32520) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Her name Bilqis bint Dhu Shara, and she was a poetic woman."
"32521","(32521) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid: That his companion was Saba’. She was a poetic fairy."
"32522","(32522) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And I I am sent to them with a gift.} He said: I was sent with gold, or bricks of gold. When they came, behold, the walls of the city were made of Gold, and that is His saying: {Will you provide me with wealth, for what God has given you is better than what He has given you} the verse."
"32523","(32523) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Hamid bin Abdul Rahman speaking, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: He said - meaning God Almighty -: It is not necessary. A servant may say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matthew. (Bukhari 3416, Muslim 166)"
"32524","(32524) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, who said: He said - God Almighty means: No servant can say: I am better than Yunus bin Matta. Praise God in the darkness. (Tahawi 1013)"
"32525","(32525) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: No one can say, “I am better than Yunus ibn Matthew.” (Bukhari 3412, Ahmed 390)"
"32526","(32526) Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: A cousin narrated to me. Your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: It is not for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta. (Bukhari 7539, Abu Dawud 4636)"
"32527","(32527) Ubaid Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: Abdul told us Allah ibn Masoud in Bayt al-Mal, on the authority of Yunus, said: Yunus had promised his people punishment and told them that it would He came to them for three days, and they separated each of his parents from her two children, then they left and came to God and asked for forgiveness. So God spared them the torment, and the next morning Yunus was waiting for the torment, but he did not see anything. He was one who lied and it was not for him. Clearly, he was killed, so he set off in anger until he came to some people in a ship, and they carried him and recognized him. When he entered the ship, they stagnated, and the ships stopped. It moves right and left. They said: What is the matter with your ship? They said: We do not know. Yunus said: In it there is a servant more distant than his Lord, and it will not travel until you meet Him. They said: As for you? O Prophet of God, no, by God, we will never meet you.\n So Yunus said to them: So they cast lots, and whoever casts lots, let him cast lots. So Yunus cast lots for them, but they refused to invite him, so they said: Whoever casts three Several times and he fell, and Yunus knocked on them three times and he fell, and he had been entrusted with the whale, so when he fell, it swallowed him and took him in. To the depths of the earth, then Yunus, peace be upon him, heard the glorification of the pebbles {so he called out in the darkness: There is no god but You. Glory be to You. Indeed, I was of The wrongdoers} three injustices,The darkness of the belly of the whale, the darkness of the sea, and the darkness of the night. He said: {So We cast him naked while he was sick.} He said: Like a curled-up chick, it has no feathers, and God made a pumpkin tree grow over it for shade. And he afflicted with it, and it withered, and he wept over it when it withered, so God revealed to it: You weep over a tree. Be patient and do not cry for a hundred thousand or more whom you wanted to destroy.\n So he went out and saw a boy tending sheep. He said: Who are you from, boy? He said: From the people of Yunus. He said: So when you return Go to them and tell them that you have met Yunus. He said: Then the boy said: If you are Yunus, then you may know that he is the one who lied and did not There is clear evidence that he will be killed, so who will bear witness on his behalf? Then Yunus said to him: This tree will bear witness for you, and this Al-Baqa’, and the boy said: An ointment, and Yunus said to them: If this boy comes as well, then they will bear witness to him. They said: Yes, so he returned. The boy went to his people, and he had brothers and he was in a state of protection for him, so he came to the king and said: I met Yunus while he was reciting. Peace be upon you. So the king ordered him to be killed, and they said to him: He has clear evidence. So he sent with him and they went to the tree. And Al-Baqa’, so the boy said to them: I adjure you by God. Did Yunus speak to you? They said: Yes,So the people returned terrified, saying: The trees and the earth bear witness to him, so they went to the king and told him what they had seen.\n Abdullah said: So the king approached him, took the boy by the hand, made him sit in his seat, and said: You are more deserving of this place. From me\n Abdullah said: So that boy stayed in charge of them for forty years."
"32528","(32528) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: Yunus stayed in the belly of the whale for forty. One day"
"32529","(32529) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem: {So he called out in the darkness.} He said: A whale within a whale and its darkness. The sea"
"32530","(32530) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I heard him say: {So he called out in the darkness} He said: Darkness is the night, Darkness is the sea, and Darkness is the fish."
"32531","(32531) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Al-Harith, he said: When The whale bit him and threw him to the ground. He heard her praising God, so she excited him to praise him."
"32532","(32532) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shibl bin Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Abu Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Maryam said: Whenever Jesus and I were alone, he would talk to me and I would talk to him, and whenever he kept me busy, he would talk to me and I would talk to him. A person swam in my stomach while I was listening to him."
"32533","(32533) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shibl narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Jesus, peace be upon him, did not speak except the verses that he spoke until he reached the age of childhood."
"32534","(32534) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, who said: Only three people spoke during the birth: Jesus, peace be upon him, the companion of Joseph, and the companion of Jurayj."
"32535","(32535) Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And indeed, For knowledge of the one who seeks.} He said: The emergence of Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him."
"32536","(32536) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Sheikh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: {To make it prevail over all religion} He said: The exit of Jesus, peace be upon him."
"32537","32537) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: When God wanted to raise Jesus, peace be upon him, to the heavens, he went out to his companions - who were twelve men - from a spring in house and its top was dripping with water, so he said to them: Is there not one of you who will disbelieve in me twelve times after believing in me? Then he said: Which of you will have my likeness cast upon him and be killed in my place and be with me in my rank? Then a young man who spoke to them stood up and said: I, so Jesus said: Sit, then he repeated it to them, so the young man stood up, and Jesus said: Sit, then He repeated it to them, so the young man got up and said: I. He said: Yes, you are that one. He said: Then the likeness of Jesus was cast on him.\n He said: And Jesus, peace be upon him, was raised from a rose that was in the House to the heavens. He said: The request came from the Jews, so they took So they killed him, then crucified him, and some of them disbelieved in him twelve times after they had believed in him, so they separated into three groups. He said: Then one group said: God was in us as He willed, then He ascended to the heavens, and these are the Jacobites. And another group said: It was Among us is the Son of God, then God raised him up to Himself, and those Nestorians, and one group said: The servant of God and the Messenger of God was among us. God willing, then God raised him and these Muslims to Himself.\n Then the two infidel women demonstrated against the Muslim woman, and they fought her and killed her. Islam remained obliterated until God sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, so God revealed to him: {So a group of the Children of Israel believed} meaning: the group that believed in the time of Jesus. {And a group disbelieved} meaning: the group that disbelieved in the time of Jesus {So We supported those who believed} in the time of Jesus {over Their enemy} by making Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prevail over their religion over the religion of the disbelievers {so they became victorious}. (Nasa’i 11591)"
"32538","(32538) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Jesus was the son of Maryam. He, peace be upon him, did not take dinner for lunch or lunch for dinner, and he used to say: “Indeed, with each day he received his sustenance,” and he used to wear hair. He eats trees and sleeps wherever he is in the evening."
"32539","(32539) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, who said: A woman passed by Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him. She said: Blessed is the womb of your burden, and the breast that suckled you. Then Jesus, peace be upon him, said: Blessed is he who reads the Qur’an and follows what is in it."
"32540","(32540) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yaqoub, he said: Jesus bin Maryam said: Do not be too much. Speech other than the remembrance of God, and your hearts harden, for a hard heart is far from God, but you do not know, do not look into it. the sins of your servants as if you were lords, and look at your sins as if you were slaves, for people are but two men: afflicted. And he is well, so have mercy on the people of calamity, and thank God for his well-being."
"32541","(32541) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, who raised him to Jesus, saying: He said: To his companions, take the mosques. dwellings, and take homes as dwelling places, and escape from this world in peace, and eat of wild herbs, and the Amish add to it: And drink from the water of Qarah."
"32542","(32542) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Musayyab, on the authority of a man who narrated to him, who said: The disciples said to Isa Ibn Maryam, peace be upon her: What do you eat? He said: Barley bread. They said: What are you wearing? He said: Wool. They said: What does it spread out on? He said: The earth. They said: All of this is severe. He said: You will not attain the kingdom of the heavens and the earth until you achieve this pleasure. Or he said: upon your desires."
"32543","(32543) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, he said: I heard him mentioned, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: In his saying: {Indeed, you and what you worship besides Allah are the number of Hell; you will enter it.} He said: So mention Jesus. And Ezra: They were both worshippers, and these verses were revealed after them: {Indeed, those of us who preceded Those are far away from it. He said: Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him."
"32544","(32544) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Misra Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: I asked Ka'b about raising Idris to a high place? He said: As for Idris being raised to a high position, he was a pious servant, and his good deeds would be raised to him as they are raised to the people of the earth. The people of his time. He said: The king was astonished at his work, so he asked his Lord for permission. He said: My Lord, give permission. I will go to this servant of yours, and I will visit him. So he gave him permission, and he came down and said: O Idris, give good news, for your work will be raised. The righteous is that which is not raised for the people of the earth. He said: And what did he teach you? He said: I am a king. He said: Even if I am a king. He said: I am at the gate where your work goes up.\n He said: Will you not intercede on my behalf with the Angel of Death, so that he may be delayed for my sake, so that I may increase in gratitude and worship? The angel said to him: God does not delay a soul when its time has come. He said: I know, but it is better for my soul. So the angel carried him. On his wings, he ascended with him to the heavens and said: O Angel of Death, this is a pious servant and a prophet, to whom countless good deeds will be raised. It will be raised up for the people of the earth, and I liked that, so I sought permission from my Lord, and when I gave him the good news of that, he asked me to intercede for him. To you, it will be delayed for his sake, and his gratitude and worship of God will increase. He said: Who is this? He said: Idris, so he looked at the book he had until he came across his name, and said: By God, nothing remains of Idris, so he erased it and died. His place"
"32545","(32545) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: {And We raised him to a high place} and he said: In the heavens. Fourth"
"32546","(32546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: In the fourth heaven."
"32547","(32547) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Hud, peace be upon him, was immortalized in His people, and he was sitting among his people, and a cloud of clouds came over them, and they said: {This is a storm that will rain for us} and he said: Hud is upon him. Peace: {Rather, it is as much as you hastened about it; an odor in which is a painful punishment} So she started to throw the tent and bring the absent man."
"32548","(32548) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: David, peace be upon him, used to address the people and He has a wicker basket in his hand, and when he is finished, he gives her some of it and sells it."
"32549","(32549) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When the sin befell David, it was only Your sin is that when he saw her, he ordered her to be separated and did not approach her. Then the two opponents came to him and took cover in the sanctuary, so when He saw them and stood up to them and said: Leave me. What brought you to me? They said: We are only speaking to you in a simple manner, {Indeed, this is my brother who has ninety-nine ewes, and I have one female ewe} and he... He wants to take it from me. He said: Then David, peace be upon him, said: By God, he has more right to have his sperm broken than this one. This - meaning from his nose to his chest - so the man said: This is what David did.\n So David, peace be upon him, knew that he was only meant for that, and he knew his sin, so he prostrated himself for forty and forty days. One night, his sin was written on his hand, and he looked at it so that he would not neglect until the herbs grew. His tears covered his head, and after forty days he called: The forehead was sore and the eyes were frozen, and David did not return. He had committed a sin and called: Are you hungry and should you be fed? Or are you naked and clothed? Or an oppressed person and you will be helped? He said: He loved so much that he attacked the herds that surrounded him when he did not mention his sin, and then he was forgiven. If he had On the Day of Resurrection, his Lord will say to him: Be in front of me. He will say: O Lord, my sin is my sin. So He will say to him: Be behind me. So he says: O Lord, my sin is my sin. So he says to him: Take my feet, so he takes his feet."
"32550","(32550) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, he said: We were informed that David, the Prophet of God, rewarded Blessings be upon his households and upon his wives and children. Not a single hour of the night or day came without a person standing from the family of David. He prayed, so I taught them these verses: {Do the family of David with gratitude, and few of My servants are grateful}"
"32551","(32551) Affan narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah bin Abdul Karim narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to us: That David the Prophet, peace be upon him, narrated to us. He said: My God, even if every verse of mine had two tongues, Glory be to You night and day, You would not have fulfilled the due of Your blessings. Ali"
"32552","(32552) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: The two adversaries entered upon Dawud. Peace be upon him, and each one of them took the head of his companion."
"32553","(32553) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: It was only the temptation of David. The sight"
"32554","(32554) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadlili, he said: What David, peace be upon him, raised his head to the heavens until he died."
"32555","(32555) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qays, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: That David, peace be upon him, said: O Lord, the children of Israel are asking you With Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, so make me, O Lord, a fourth among them. Then God revealed to him: O David, indeed Abraham He was thrown into the Fire because of me, but he was patient. That was a calamity that did not befall you, and Isaac gave his life because of me, so he was patient. That is a calamity that did not befall you, and indeed, You took away his beloved Jacob until his eyes became bright, so he was patient. That was a calamity that did not befall you. NS (Bazzar 1307. Tabari 23)"
"32556","(32556) Ali bin Zaid said: His successor told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: that David told himself that he was afflicted with Atasim, and it was said to him: You will be tested and you know the day on which you will be tested, so take heed, so it was said to him: This day. in which you were tested. So he took the Psalms and placed it in his lap, closed the door of the mihrab, and sat upright at the door, and said: No. Call the call to prayer for anyone today.\n While he was reciting the Psalms, a golden bird came, like the best of all birds, of every color, and began to fly. In his hands, he approached him and was able to take it, so he took it with his hand so that he could take it, so he asked him from behind him. So the Zabur closed and he got up to take it. It flew and fell on the window of the mihrab. We also came to it to take it and it fell. On his own, so he looked over it to see where it had fallen, and he saw the woman at her blessing, taking a bath after her menstruation, so when She saw his shadow, moved her head, and covered her body with her hair, so David said to the one who was appointed: Go and tell so-and-so that she will come. So he came to her and said to her: The Prophet of God is calling on you. She said: What do I have to do with the Prophet of God? If he has a need, let him come to me. As for me, I will not come to him. So Al-Mansaf came to him and told him what she said, so he came to her: She closed the door without him and said: What is the matter with you, David?Do you not know that whoever did this, you stoned him and admonished him, and he returned.\n Her husband was a warrior in the cause of God, so David, peace be upon him, wrote to the commander of the battle: Look for Uriah and put him in the army. He carried the coffin - and the people who carried the coffin were: either it would be opened for them, or they would be killed - so he presented him while carrying the coffin and he was killed, so when her waiting period was completed He proposed to her, and she stipulated that if she gave birth to a boy, he would make him a caliph after him. She appointed fifty of his sons as witnesses over him. Israel and wrote a decree against him about that, but he did not realize that his temptation was a temptation, until she gave birth to Solomon and he became a young man, so he took control of The two kings were on the mihrab, and it was among their affairs what God related, and David fell down prostrating, so God forgave him and he repented, and God repented. Aliyah\n So they divorced her, and Solomon fled and sent him away. While he was with her, he was on a journey with her - and he was in the direction of the people - when he came. Some of his boys were playing and they started saying: Oh, there is no religion, oh, there is no religion. Then David stood up and said: What is the matter with this man who is called “No?” religion, and he said: Solomon, while he was in the neighborhood of the people: but if he had asked me about this, I would have informed him of his matter, so it was said: To Dawud: Solomon said such-and-such, so he summoned him and said: What is the matter with this boy who was named La-Din? He said: I will teach you the knowledge of that.So Solomon asked about his father, how was his situation? It was said to him: His father was on a journey with his friends, and he had a lot of money, so they wanted to kill him, so he advised them. He said: I left my wife with child, so if she gives birth to a boy, tell her that she calls him “no religion.” So Solomon sent to his companions, So they came, and he was alone with one of them, and he did not stop until they acknowledged it, and he was alone with the others, and he did not stop with them until they all acknowledged, so he raised them up. To David, he killed them, and he had some sympathy for him.\n She was a devout woman from the children of Israel, and she had become a virgin, and she had two beautiful maids, and she had become a virgin. A woman does not want men, so one of the two slave girls said to the other: This affliction has been upon us for a long time, but this one has not She wants men, and we would still be as evil as we were to her. If we had exposed her, she would have been stoned. We would have gone to the men, and they would have taken the egg water. So they came to her while she was prostrating, and they uncovered her garment and sprinkled white water on her anus and cried out: She has committed a mistake. And whoever among them committed adultery was subject to stoning, so the white water on her clothes was brought to David, peace be upon him, and he wanted to stone her, so he said Solomon: If he had asked me, I would have told him. So it was said to David: Solomon said such-and-such, so he called him.He said: What is the matter with this? What's the matter with her? He said: Bring me fire, for if it is the water of the men, it will disperse, and if it is the water of the whites, it will come together, so bring fire and put it on. So he gathered to protect her from stoning, and showed him some kindness and loved him.\n Then after that, there were the owners of the field and the owners of the field, and David, peace be upon him, ruled that the owners of the field should know about the sheep, so they went out. The shepherds went out with the dogs, and Solomon said: How was the matter among you? So they informed him, and he said: If I had been in charge of their affairs, I would have judged between them other than this decision. So it was said to David: Indeed, Solomon He says such-and-such, so he summoned her and said: How do you make up for it? So he said: I will give the sheep to the owners of the field this year, and they will have their children, their offspring, their fodder, and their benefits for the year. And these people sow like their own tillage, so when the tillage that was over them reached its ripeness, he took that tillage and gave it to them. These sheep, he said: so he was kind to them. \n Hammad said: I heard Thabit saying: He is Uriah."
"32557","(32557) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: God revealed to David, peace be upon him, that: Say to the oppressors: Do not mention me, for it is my right to remind those who He reminded me, and if he mentioned them I cursed them."
"32558","(32558) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: David, peace be upon him, died suddenly on Saturday. He was hibernating, so the birds used to seek shade over him."
"32559","(32559) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Al-Muhallab Abu Kudayna narrated to us, on the authority of Ata, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {O mountains of Ubayy are with him} He said: Praise You."
"32560","(32560) Muhammad bin Bishr and Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman: {O mountains Obi with him} He said: Glory be to Him."
"32561","(32561) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He cried because of his sin until he became agitated. He was surrounded by tears."
"32562","(32562) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra: {Aubi} said: Glory be to Him."
"32563","(32563) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {We have not made He said: No one was named after him."
"32564","(32564) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The same."
"32565","(32565) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Suleiman al-Abdi, on the authority of a man among them called: Mahdi, on the authority of Ikrimah: {And We gave him wisdom as a child} He said: pulp."
"32566","(32566) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid: {And We gave him wisdom when he was a child} He said: The Qur’an."
"32567","(32567) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour ibn Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, who said: Ibn Umar and Ibn al-Zubayr entered the mosque. He was crucified. They said: These are Asma. He said: So he came to her and reminded her and admonished her, and said to her: The corpse is not anything. But souls are with God, so be patient and seek reward. She said: And what prevents me from being patient, and the head of Yahya bin Zakariya was given as a gift. To one of the prostitutes of the Children of Israel."
"32568","(32568) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Yahya ibn Zakariya was not killed except in A prostitute, she said to her companion: I will not be satisfied with you until you bring me his head. He said: So he slaughtered it and brought him his head. In a basin"
"32569","(32569) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid: Concerning his saying: {We had not previously made for it any name.} He said: something like it in Virtue"
"32570","(32570) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: There is no one except that he made a mistake, or was concerned about his mistake, not Yahya ibn Zakariya. Then he recited: {and master and confinement}, then He raised something from the ground, then said: He had nothing with him except something like this."
"32571","(32571) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa`id: {And master and chaste} He said: The Forbearing."
"32572","(32572) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no one who has not made a mistake, or is about to make a mistake, except Yahya ibn Zechariah\n(Ahmad 2958, Abu Ali 2538)"
"32573","(32573) He told us in his youth, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid: {We had not before given to him any name.} He said: Almost like"
"32574","(32574) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Dhul-Qarnayn Prophet"
"32575","(32575) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He was the king of the earth."
"32576","(32576) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Ali, who said: He was a righteous man, he advised God and He advised him. So he was struck on his right horn and died, so God revived him. Then he was struck on his left horn and died, so God revived him, and among you. Like him"
"32577","(32577) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Tufail, he said: He was asked Ali on the authority of Dhul-Qarnayn? He said: He was neither a prophet nor a king, but he was a worshiper who advised God and He advised him, so he called his people to God and he was beaten. His right horn, and he died, and God revived him. Then he called his people to God, and his left horn was struck, and he died, and God revived him. So he was named Dhul-Qarnayn."
"32578","(32578) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Habib ibn Hamaz, who said: It was said to Ali: How did Dhul-Qarnayn reach the East and the West? He said: The clouds were subjected to him, the light was extended to him, and the means were extended to him. Then he said: Shall I increase for you? He said: It is sufficient for me."
"32579","(32579) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: No one ruled the entire earth except four: two Muslims. And two disbelievers. As for the two Muslims: Sulaiman bin Dawud and Dhul-Qarnayn, and as for the two disbelievers, Bakht Nasr, and the one who performed Hajj. Abraham in his Lord."
"32580","(32580) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Joseph was thrown into the pit when he was seventeen years old. years, and he was in slavery, in prison, and in kingship for eighty years, then he was reunited and lived after that for three years. And twenty years."
"32581","(32581) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Rabi’ al-Jurashi, who said: Al-Hasan’s oath Two halves, so Joseph and his mother were given half for good behaviour, and half for the rest of creation."
"32582","(32582) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Who is the most generous of people? He said: The most devout of God. They said: Not. This is what we ask you about. He said: So the most honorable of people was Yusuf, the Prophet of God, the son of the Prophet of God. The son of the Prophet of God, the son of Khalil God, may God’s prayers be upon them.\n(Bukhari 3374, Muslim 1846)"
"32583","(32583) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Joseph was given the portion of goodness."
"32584","(32584) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He was given Joseph, peace be upon him, and his mother are a third of good character."
"32585","(32585) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Abdullah bin Abbas came to Ibn Salam. He said: I want to ask you about three things. He said: Are you asking me while you are reading the Qur’an? He said: Yes, he said: Fasl, he said: Tell me about Tuba, what was it? And what happened to Uzair? And about Solomon, why did he miss the hoopoe?\n He said: As for Tuba’, he was an Arab man. He prevailed over the people and took captive a young man from among the rabbis, so he brought them in and spoke to them. And they spoke to him, and his people said: Indeed, Tuba’ has abandoned your religion and followed the fatwa. So Tuba’ said to the fatwa: You may hear what he said. These people said: Between us and them is the fire that burns the liar and saves the truthful from it. They said: Yes. Tuba’ said. For the girl: Enter it. He said: So they picked up their Qur’an and entered it, and it opened for them until they cut it. Then he said to his people : They entered it, and when they entered it, fire engulfed their faces, so they retreated! He said: Let us enter it. He said: So they entered it and it opened for them, until when they got in the middle of it it surrounded them and burned them. He said: Tuba’ converted to Islam and was a righteous man.\n As for Uzair: When the Holy House was destroyed and the teachings of knowledge were being taught and the Torah was torn apart, it was wandering wild in the mountains, and it was being destroyed. A spring from which he drank. He said: One day he returned to it, and behold, a woman appeared to him. When he saw her, he recoiled. Thirst came to her, and when she was crying, he said: What makes you cry? She said: I cry for my son. He said: Was your son blessed? She said: No, he said: He was creating? She said: No. He said: So do not cry over him. She said: Who are you? Do you want your people? Enter this spring, for you will find them. He said: So he entered it. He said: Every time he entered it, his knowledge increased until it was over. To his people, and God has returned his knowledge to him, so he revived for them the Torah and revived for them knowledge. He said: This is Uzir.\n As for Suleiman: He went down a while on a journey and did not know what was beyond the water, so he asked who knew his knowledge? They said: The hoopoe, so he inspected it there."
"32586","(32586) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abd God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I disavow every friend of his character, except that God has decided Your companion is a friend, and if I had taken a friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a friend, except that Waki’ said: From his companion."
"32587","(32587) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said in the grandfather: As for what the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If I had taken this mother as a friend, I would have taken him as a father.\n(Bukhari 3456. Dharmi 2910)"
"32588","(32588) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The people of the highest degrees will see whoever is below them just as you see the star rising on the horizon from the horizons of the heavens. And Abu Bakr and Omar were among them, and they were blessed. (Tirmidhi 3458, Ahmed 27)"
"32589","(32589) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Fulayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Salem Abul Nadr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Hunayn and Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed the people, and he said: The people entrusted me with the companionship and wealth of Abu Bakr, and if I had taken one of the people as a friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but his brothers Islam and its affection. There is not a door left in the mosque that will not be blocked except the door of Abu Bakr.\n(Bukhari 3904, Muslim 1855)"
"32590","(32590) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: No wealth has benefited me. Abu Bakr’s wealth has not benefited me. He said: Then Abu Bakr cried and said: Is there anything wrong with me and my wealth? Thank you, O Messenger of God. (Tirmidhi 3661, Ahmed 253)"
"32591","(32591) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, that a Bedouin among them said: I witnessed He performed the morning prayer with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One day, he turned to the people and said: I saw people from your nation. Yesterday they weighed, and Abu Bakr was weighed and he won, then Omar was weighed and he won. (Ahmed 63)"
"32592","(32592) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Bakr narrated to him, he said: I said: To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were in the cave: If one of them were to look at his feet, we would see under his feet. He said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two, God is the third? (Tirmidhi 3096. Ahmad 4)"
"32593","(32593) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Salem, who said: I said to Ibn al-Hanafiyyah: Abu Bakr was the first of the people to convert to Islam. He said: No, I said: From whom did Abu Bakr rise? He was the best of them in Islam when he converted to Islam until he joined God."
"32594","(32594) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have mercy. My nation Abu Bakr."
"32595","(32595) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, described a day Paradise, and what is in it of honor, and he said, among others, that there are birds in it like a flock, so Abu Bakr said: Oh. Messenger of God, those birds are soft, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Abu Bakr, whoever eats from them is softer. From it, by God, O Abu Bakr, I hope that you will be among those who eat from it. (Ahmed 221)"
"32596","(32596) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of his father, who said: A man said to Omar bin Al-Khattab: What I saw someone like you. He said: Did you see Abu Bakr? He said: No. He said: If you had said yes, I saw him, I would have hurt you."
"32597","(32597) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar said: Because I come forward. It would be more beloved to me to be beheaded than to advance against a people among whom is Abu Bakr."
"32598","(32598) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Omar bin Asid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: We used to say in the time of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The best of people are Abu Bakr and Omar. (Ahmed 26)"
"32599","(32599) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suhayl, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We used to count while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman, then we remained silent. (Abu Dawud 4603. Ahmed 14)"
"32600","(32600) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The love of Abu Bakr, Omar, and his acquaintance. Their virtues from the Sunnah"
"32601","(32601) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Siyah, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, in his saying: {So God sent down His tranquility upon him} He said: upon Abu Bakr. He said: As for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, it was Peace be upon him before that."
"32602","(32602) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Bakr was freed from the one who was being tortured. In God there are seven: Aamir bin Fuhayra, Bilal, Zunairah, Umm Abbas, Al-Nahdiyyah and her daughter, and the two female slaves of Banu Amr bin Hopeful"
"32603","(32603) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, that Omar said: I do not hear of anyone who preferred me over Abu Bakr except Forty lashes."
"32604","(32604) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, he said: Abu Muadh told me, on the authority of Khattab, or my father. Al-Khattab, on the authority of Ali, said: While I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Abu Bakr and Omar came and said: O Ali, these two are masters like all the people of Paradise, except for those who are among the prophets, so do not tell them about them. (Tirmidhi 366. Ibn Majah 95)"
"32605","(32605) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of a servant of Rabi’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfy, said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I do not know what was decreed. As long as I remain among you, follow the example of those after me. He referred to Abu Bakr and Omar. (Tirmidhi 3799 and Ahmad 3985)"
"32606","(32606) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, he said: It is written in the first book: the example of my father. Virgin like rain, wherever it falls it is beneficial."
"32607","(32607) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. The excellent man is Abu Bakr, the excellent man is Omar, the excellent man is Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, the excellent man is Amr ibn al-Jamuh, and the excellent man is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. (Tirmidhi 3795, Ahmad 419)"
"32608","(32608) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jami’, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: I said to my father: Who is good? The people after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Abu Bakr. He said: I said: Then who? He said: Then Omar. He said: I said: Then you. He said: Your father is a man of the Muslims. (Bukhari 3671, Abu Dawud 4605)"
"32609","(32609) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sadaqi bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: I heard my grandfather Riyah bin Al-Harith mentioning; He witnessed Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, and he was in Al-Kufa in the Great Mosque, and they were all on the right side. And to the north, until a man from the people of Medina came, called Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, and the raiders welcomed him. He made him sit at his feet on the bed, and while he was still there, a man from the people of Kufa entered, called Qais. Ibn Alqamiya, so he faced Al-Mughirah and cursed and cursed, and Al-Madani said to him: O Mughir ibn Shu’ab, who is insulting this person? He said: He cursed Ali bin Abi Talib. He said to him twice: O Mughir bin Shu’ab, oh Mughir bin Shu’ab, should I not listen to the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They are taken captive in your presence. Do not deny it, and do not change it, for I bear witness against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, according to what my ears have heard and what my heart has understood, for I will never narrate a lie about him after him, so they will ask me. On the authority of him, if you meet him, he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Omar is in Paradise, Othman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise. The jinn, Talhah is in the jinn, Zubair is in the jinn, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf is in the jinn, and Sa`d is in the jinn. Paradise, and the last ninth, if I wanted to name it, I would have named it. He said: Then the people of the mosque came out and called upon him by God: The companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who is the ninth? He said: You called me to God, and God is Great. I am the ninth of the believers, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the tenth. Then They followed it, and by God there is no witness that a man among them witnessed one day in the path of God, with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, covering his face with dust is better than the deeds of any of you, even if it lasts as long as Noah.\n(Abu Dawud 4618 and Ibn Majah 133)"
"32610","(32610) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, in The jinn is a bird like a fortuneteller. A man comes and gets some of it, then goes away as if nothing was missing from it. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, that bird is soft. He said: Whoever eats it is softer than it, but you are among those who eat it. He eats it."
"32611","(32611) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, he said: I bear witness against nine people that they are in Paradise, and if I bore witness against the tenth, you would be truthful. He said: I said: And what is that? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with Hira’, Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, and Saad bin Malik, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Stand firm, for there is no one over you except a prophet. Or a friend, or a witness. He said: I said: From the tenth. He said: I. (Abu Dawud 4616. Ibn Hibban 6996)"
"32612","(32612) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, that Aisha looked at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. She said, “O Master of the Arabs.” He said: “I am the master of the descendants of Adam, and I am not proud, and your father is the master of all the Arabs.”"
"32613","(32613) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Juhayf, who said: Ali said: The best of this nation yet. Her prophet is Abu Bakr, and after Abu Bakr is Omar. If I wanted to tell you about the third, I could do so. (Ahmed 106)"
"32614","(32614) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Juhayfy, on the authority of Ali, the same. (Ibn Abi Asim 1202)"
"32615","(32615) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: I walked with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the wife of a man from the Ansar. He said: I spread palm roots for him, and I slaughtered We heard something, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let us enter a man from the people of Paradise, so Abu Bakr entered, then he said: A man from the people of Paradise will enter. Omar entered, then he said: A man from the people of Paradise will enter, then he said: Oh God, if you wish. You made him Ali, so he entered Ali."
"32616","(32616) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, he said: Al-Hurr bin Sayyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Akhnas Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Omar is in Paradise, Ali and Othman are in Paradise, Talha is in Paradise, and Zubair is in Paradise. And Abd al-Rahman bin Awf is in the jinn, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas is in the jinn, and if I wished, I could have named it the ninth. (An-Nasa’i 8210. Ahmed 188)"
"32617","(32617) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib said: It was said to me and to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq on the day of Badr: With one of you was Gabriel, and with the other. Mikael and Israfil are a great king who witnesses the battle, or stands in the ranks. (Ahmad 147, Ibn Saad 175)"
"32618","(32618) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Sari ibn Yahya, on the authority of Bastam ibn Muslim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Amr bin Al-Aas greeted a group in which Abu Bakr and Omar were present. When they came, Abu Bakr and Omar complained about Omar, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No one will conspire against you after me."
"32619","(32619) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar said: I wished to be from Paradise where I see Abu Bakr."
"32620","(32620) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man said to Omar: O the best of people, and he said: I am I am not the best of people. He said: By God, I have never seen a man better than you. He said: Have you not seen Abu Bakr? He said: No. He said: If you had said: Yes, I would have punished you. He said, and Omar said: (Oh God) between me and Abu Bakr, a day from my father. A virgin is better than the family of Omar."
"32621","(32621) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qays, he said: Amr said: Which of the people is most beloved to you? Messenger of God? He said: Why? He said: Let us love whom you love. He said: The most beloved of people to me is Aisha. He said: I am not asking you about women, I am asking you about men. He said: One time: her father, and another time he said: Abu Bakr. (Bukhari 3662, Hakim 12)"
"32622","(32622) Zaid told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Abu Dhudhail, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: There is no one who has been safer with us than Abu Bakr, and if I had taken a friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but My brother, my companion, and my religion, and your companion has been taken as a friend, meaning himself."
"32623","(32623) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Badr bin Othman, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Marwan, on the authority of Abu Aisha, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us one morning and said: I just saw it as if I had been given The keys and the scales. As for the keys, these are the keys. I have been placed on a palm, and my nation has been placed on a palm, so I have passed. With them, then Abu Bakr was brought and he prevailed, then Omar was brought and he prevailed, then Uthman was brought and he succeeded, then it was raised, he said: so he said to him Man: Where are we? He said: Where you have placed yourselves."
"32624","(32624) Qabisa narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, On the authority of his father, he said: We sent a delegation to Muawiyah. He said: He was not as impressed with the delegation as he was with us, so he said: O Abu Bakra, Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: She was amazed at the vision when he was being asked about her, so I heard him say: I saw a balance sent down from the sky and I was weighed in it, I and Abu Bakr, so I preferred to Abu Bakr, then Abu Bakr was weighed against Omar, and Abu Bakr preferred, then Omar and Uthman were weighed, and Omar preferred to Uthman. Then the scales were raised to the heavens, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Caliphate and prophethood, then God will give you the kingdom. Whoever He wills, He said: Then insert us into our cages and bring us out."
"32625","(32625) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Two men mentioned Uthman, and one of them said: He killed a martyr. Then the other man clung to it and brought it to Ali. He said: This man claims that Uthman ibn Affan killed a martyr. He said: Did you say that? He said: Yes, do you not remember the day I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar and Othman were with him? So I asked The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, and I asked Abu Bakr and he gave me, and I asked Omar and he gave me, and I asked Othman So he gave me, and I said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to bless me. He said: What is yours will not be blessed for you when He has given you? A prophet, a truthful, and two witnesses. Then Ali said: Leave him, leave him, leave him. (Abu Ali 1598)"
"32626","(32626) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, that he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this nation after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Abu Bakr and Omar bin Al-Khattab."
"32627","(32627) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd bin Yathai’, he said: It was Abu Bakr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace on the Day of Badr, at Al-Arish. (Tabari 190)"
"32628","(32628) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Every person of good deeds has a gate from the gates of Paradise from which they will be called. With that action, there is a chapter for those who fast, and it is called Al-Rayyan. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, is there anyone who will call upon him? All of those doors. He said: Yes, and I hope that you are one of them, O Abu Bakr."
"32629","(32629) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah al-Majishūn, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundādir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Omar said: Abu Bakr is our master and he freed our master, meaning Bilal. (Bukhari 3754)"
"32630","(32630) Yazeed told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I imitated this verse, and Abu Bakr judged it.\nAnd the whiteness of the clouds gives water to the orphans, protection for the widows.\n Abu Bakr said: That is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"32631","(32631) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ghudayf bin Al-Harith, a man from Oh, on the authority of Abu Dharr, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God has placed the truth on the tongue of Omar.\n(Abu Dawud 6955, Ahmed 165)"
"32632","(32632) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Salem told us, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was shown sleeping as if I was taking off a bucket. Bakr was at the heart of Qalib, then Abu Bakr came and committed a sin, or two sins, and he committed a weak sin, and may God forgive him. Then Omar ibn al-Khattab came and asked for water, so it turned west. I have never seen a genius among the people break out of his shame until the people narrated and attacked him. With rottenness."
"32633","(32633) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: While I was watering at a well, Ibn Abi Quhafiya came and removed one or two sins. He was weak, and God will forgive him. Then Omar came and attacked until it became impossible for him to move, and he struck the people with clay, but they did not I saw a genius slandering you. (Bukhari 3644, Muslim 1860)"
"32634","(32634) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, that a Bedouin among them said: I witnessed the morning prayer with One day, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to the people and said: I saw people from my nation yesterday. They weighed, and Abu Bakr won, and he won, then Omar was weighed, and he won."
"32635","(32635) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, among those who passed away were men who had narrated news other than prophethood. If there is anyone among my nation Of them, then Omar. (Muslim 1864. Tirmidhi 3693)"
"32636","(32636) Abdullah bin Idris, Waki’ and Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abdullah said: What We have been dearer to you since Omar converted to Islam. (Bukhari 3684, Hakim 84)"
"32637","(32637) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani and Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: Ali said: We were not We reject the fact that the sakinah speaks with the tongue of Omar."
"32638","(32638) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, Abdullah said: When the righteous are mentioned, they will live. Welcome to my life"
"32639","(32639) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: Abdullah said: When the righteous are mentioned, greetings."
"32640","(32440) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Wasil Al-Ahdab, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Omar was a fortified fortress of Islam, from which Islam entered and did not leave. So when Omar was killed The fortress is broken, so Islam leaves it and does not enter it."
"32641","(32641) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Umm Ayman said when Omar was killed today and that is Islam."
"32642","(32442) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A man met a devil. On some of the roads of Medina, they took a path and Satan was struck, so Abdullah was asked and he said: Who do you think he is except Omar? (Bayhaqi 123)"
"32643","(32443) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Omar saw The opinion with which the Qur’an was revealed."
"32644","(32444) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, he said: Abdullah said: We did not quarrel with the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, an angel speaks in the language of Omar."
"32645","(32645) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We used to talk, or we used to talk, that The devils were chained up during the time of Omar, so when he was afflicted they were released."
"32646","(32446) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abdullah said: I never saw Omar except as if he was In his eyes there is a kingdom to protect him."
"32647","(32647) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Abdullah said: The people of The family is among the Arabs. No calamity has ever befallen them. The family of the family has no bad life."
"32648","(32648) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abu Talha said on the day Omar died: What The people of a household are present, and there is no one who has departed without calamity having come upon them."
"32649","(32649) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Jaham bin Abi Al-Jaham, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has put the truth on the tongue of Omar and in his heart.\n(Ibn Hibban 6889)"
"32650","(32650) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, he said: Abd al-Malik said: Qubaisa bin Jabir told me, he said: What I saw a man who was more knowledgeable about God, but had never read the Book of God, nor was he more knowledgeable about God’s religion than in my life."
"32651","(32651) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, he said: Abdullah said: I do not think that there is any Muslim family that did not experience the grief of Omar on the day Omar was stricken except a bad family. Indeed, Omar was... He taught us the most knowledgeable about God, made us read the Book of God, and made us understand the religion of God."
"32652","(32652) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: So The righteous were mentioned, so he greeted Umar. Indeed, his Islam was a victory, and his rule was a conquest, and God knows best on earth. Nothing, except that it has been found, has been lost for a lifetime, even a biting bitten. By God, I think that there is a kingdom in your eyes, guiding you and guiding you. I swear to God, I think that Satan would hesitate to talk about Islam and Omar would respond to him, and I swear to God, if I knew that a dog He loves Omar because I love him."
"32653","(32653) Abd al-Malik ibn Misra narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab, on the authority of Mus’ab. Ibn Saad, on the authority of Muadh Ibn Jabal, he said: Omar is in Paradise, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw what he saw in his sleep. And in its awakening, it is true. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: While I was in Paradise, I saw it. He turned around and said: Who is this for? It was said: By Omar bin Al-Khattab. (Ahmad 245. Ibn Hibban 6884)"
"32654","(32654) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: I entered Paradise. Then, when I saw a palace of gold, I said: Who is this for? They said: To a young man from Quraysh, so I thought it was me, so I said: To whom is he? They said: For Omar. (Ahmad 1798, Ibn Hibban 6887)"
"32655","(32655) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Omar, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I entered Paradise, and behold, within it was a palace of gold. I admired its beauty, so I asked: Who is this for? It was said to me: For Omar, but nothing prevented me from entering him except because I knew of your jealousy, O Abu Hafs. So Omar cried and said: O Abu Hafs. Messenger of God, am I jealous of you?! (Bukhari 3242, Ahmed 339)"
"32656","(32656) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who heard Jabir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I entered Paradise, and I saw in it a house, or a palace, and I heard a voice, so I said: Who is this for? It was said: Omar’s, so I wanted to enter it. Then I mentioned your jealousy, and Omar cried and said: O Messenger of God, should I be jealous of you?! (Muslim 1862. Ahmad 309)"
"32657","(32657) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of His father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I passed by a palace made of gold, lofty, square, and I said: Whose palace is this? It was said: To a man from the Arabs, so I said: I am an Arab. Whose palace is this? They said: To a man from the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: I am Muhammad. Whose palace is this? They said: Omar bin Al-Khattab. (Tirmidhi 3689. Ahmad 354)"
"32658","(32658) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, who said: Abdullah bin Buraida narrated to me, on the authority of his father, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I think Satan will separate from you, O Omar! (Tirmidhi 3690, Ahmad 353)"
"32659","(32659) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr {and the righteous of the believers}, he said: Omar."
"32660","(32660) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalaf bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abul-Safar, who said: A vision was seen on Ali, and it was spreading a lot. He said: It was said to him: You often wear this cloak, so he said: It is the clothing of my friend, companion, and friend. And my particular one is Omar. Omar advised God, and God advised him, and then he cried."
"32661","(32661) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Omar continues He was diligent and diligent from the time he was arrested until he died."
"32662","(32662) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have never taken a path except that Satan has taken a path other than him, he said to Omar.\n(Bukhari 3294, Muslim 22)"
"32663","(32663) Abu Osama narrated to us, he said: He narrated to me as a whisper, he said: Abdullah bin Shaqiq narrated to me, he said: Al-Aqra’ narrated to me. He doubted as if in a whisper: I do not know who called the muezzin, or someone else. He said: Omar sent for the bishop and said: He will ask him and I will. He stood over them, shaded from the sun, and said to him: Do you find us in your letter? He said: Your description and your deeds. He said: But you do not find us? He said: I find you to be a horn of iron. He said: Then Omar broke into his face and said: An iron horn? He said: Very trustworthy, and it was as if he was happy about that. He said: What will you find after me? He said: An honest caliph who prefers his relatives. He said: Omar said: May God have mercy on Ibn Affan. He said: What will you find after him? He said: A crack of iron. He said: And there was something in Omar’s hand that would upset him. He said: So he threw it away and said: O Dafra’ah - twice, or three times. He said: Do not say that, O Commander of the Faithful, for he is a Muslim caliph and a righteous man, but he will be appointed caliph while the sword is drawn. And the blood is draining. He said: Then he turned to me and said: The prayer. (Abu Dawud 4615)"
"32664","(32644) Affan told us, he said, Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jarami told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Samarra bin Jundub narrated that a man said: O Messenger of God! I saw as if a bucket had been lowered from the sky, then Abu Bakr came and took some of her Iraqi women and drank a drink, and in it was double, then Omar came. So he took her Iraqis and drank until he swallowed. Then Othman came and took her Iraqis and drank until he swallowed."
"32665","(32665) Abu Muawiyah told us on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of the owner of the house, he said: He was Omar’s food storer, he said: A drought struck people during the time of Omar, so a man came to the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, seek rain. For your nation, for they have been destroyed. Then the man came in a dream and it was said to him: Come to Omar and greet him, and tell him that you upright, and say to him: On you is the wise one, upon you is the wise one. So Omar came and informed him, and Omar wept, then said: O Lord, there is no harm. Except what you are unable to do."
"32666","(32666) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah said: If the knowledge of Arab biology were placed in It is enough and the knowledge of Omar was placed in a hand so that the knowledge of Omar prevailed over them."
"32667","(32667) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim, who said: The people of Najran came to Ali and said: O Amir. Believers, your letter is in your hand and your intercession is on your tongue. Omar expelled us from our land and returned us to it. Then Ali said to them: And that is the ruling. Indeed, Omar was wise in the matter, and I would not change anything that Omar did. Al-A’mash said. They used to say: If only he had Ali Omar has something to take advantage of this."
"32668","(32668) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: When Ali presented the Kufa, he said: What I came to untie the knot of Omar."
"32669","(32669) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, on the authority of al-Saqr ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha: The jinn cried for Omar three days before he was killed, and she said:\n After the most distant person was killed in the city, the earth became louder and his bones vibrated.\n May God reward him better than Amir, and may God’s hand be blessed in that torn blood.\n Whoever strives, or rides on the wings of an ostrich, to realize what you did yesterday will precede you.\n She settled matters and then left with a hole in her sleeve that was not cleared.\n And I was not afraid that his death would be like the palm of my green-eyed spontaneum."
"32670","(32670) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Two men came to Abdullah, and he said: One of them said: O Abu Abdul-Rahman, how do you recite this verse? So Abdullah said to him: Who recited it to you? He said: Abu Hakim Al-Muzani, and he said to the other: Who told you to read? He said: Omar taught me to read, he said: Read as Omar taught you, then he cried until his tears fell on the pebbles, then he said: Omar was A fortress fortified according to Islam. One can enter it but not leave it. When Omar died, the fort was cut short, so he could leave it but not enter it. Therein"
"32671","(32671) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, that there was a canal in his hand that he walked on. And he used to often say: By God, if I had wanted this qanat of mine to speak, it would have spoken, if Omar ibn al-Khattab were a weighing scale. There was no length of hair in it."
"32672","(32672) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: Omar and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba spoke. A woman, so they married the raider and left Omar, or he said: They sent back Omar. He said: Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He has They left, or returned, the best of this nation."
"32673","(32673) Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Hasan might have mentioned Omar, and he said: By God, it was not. The first of them to embrace Islam, nor the best of them to spend in the way of God, but he defeated the people through asceticism in this world and strictness in matters. God, and he does not fear God’s blame."
"32674","(32674) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab. He said: We were talking about the calmness descending on the tongue of Omar. (Tabarani 8202)"
"32675","(32675) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, he said: Saad said: By God, what He was the oldest of us in Islam, but I know by what virtue he excelled us. He was the most prosperous in this world, meaning Omar ibn al-Khattab."
"32676","(32676) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Zubaid, who said: When Abu Bakr’s death came, he sent for Omar. To appoint him as successor. He said: Then the people said: You have left us harsh and harsh. If we had ruled, he would have been harsher and harsher. What will you say to your Lord then? You came to him while you were a successor over us. He said: Do you fear me by my Lord? I say: Oh God, I have enjoined upon them the best of your family."
"32677","(32677) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Marouf bin Abi Marouf Al-Mawsili, who said: When Omar was injured We heard a voice:\n\nMay he who weeps over Islam, for he is about to be destroyed, and the covenant has not yet come.\nYou have managed the world, and He has planned its good things, and He has filled it with one who is certain of the promise."
"32678","(32678) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: He entered Ibn Abbas on Omar when he was stabbed, and he said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, if your Islam was a victory, and if your emirate was a conquest By God, you have filled the earth with justice to the point that two men would dispute and come to your command. Omar said: Sit me down. So they sat him down. He said: He responded to your words. He said: He responded to him. He said: So bear witness to me with these words on the day you meet him. He said: Yes, he said: This was explained by Omar and Farah."
"32679","(32679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama bin Wardan, who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: To his companions: Who among you attended a funeral? Omar said: I. He said: Whoever visits a sick person among you? Omar said: I. Omar said: Whoever gives alms? He said: Omar: I. He said: Who among you is fasting in the morning? Omar said: I. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is obligatory and obligatory."
"32680","(32680) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mus’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar passed by a messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he and Aisha were eating a camel, so he called him and placed his hand with their hands. Then his hand hit Aisha’s hand, and he said: Oh, if he had obeyed this and her companions, no eyes would have seen them, and that is Before the verse of the Hijab, he said: Then the verse of the Hijab was revealed. (Bukhari 1053. An-Nasa’i 11419)"
"32681","(32681) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali came to Omar while he was under cover, and he said: What There is no one on the face of the earth who is more beloved to me than this evening, to meet God with his record."
"32682","(32682) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that Gabriel said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: Convey peace to Omar and tell him that his satisfaction is wisdom and his anger is glory. (Ibn Adi 261)"
"32683","(32683) Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-Salt ibn Bahram told us, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Hakam, that Abu Bakr, when he became heavy, He looked up at the people from a window and said: O people, I have made a covenant. Will you accept it? Then the people stood up and said: We were satisfied, so Ali stood up and said: We are not satisfied unless it is Omar bin Al-Khattab, and it was Omar."
"32684","(32684) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, who said: I heard Hudhayfah say: During the time of Omar, Islam was only like a man approaching, only getting closer and closer. When Omar was killed, it was like a man heading forward, only getting closer. Except later."
"32685","(32685) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shimr, he said: It is as if the knowledge of the people was tucked in a hole with The knowledge of life."
"32686","(32686) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Omar bin Jawan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, he said: We presented Medina, so Othman came and it was said: This is Othman, so a militia wearing a yellow robe with which he had covered his head entered. He said: Here we are. Ali, they said: Yes, he said: This is Talhah, they said: Yes, he said: Al-Zubayr, they said: Yes, he said: This is Saad, They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He bought the property of the son of so-and-so, may God forgive him, so I bought it for twenty thousand, or twenty-five thousand, so I went to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I said: I have bought it. He said: Place it in our mosque and I will reward it for you. He said: So they said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god. Do you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who will buy May God forgive him, so I bought her for such-and-such, then I came to him and said: I have bought her, and he said: Make her water. for the Muslims and reward you. He said: They said: Oh God, yes. He said: I adjure you by God, there is no god but Him. Do you know that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked into the faces of the people and said: Whoever prepares these people will be forgiven by God, meaning The army of hardship, so I defeated them so that they were not missing a head or a helmet. They said: Oh God, yes. He said: He said: Oh God, I bear witness. Three. (Ahmad 70 and Ibn Hibban 6920)"
"32687","(32687) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Khams bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: Haram narrated to me. Ibn Al-Harith and Asama Ibn Khurraym, who were fighting battles, told me a story, and neither of them felt that his companion He told me on the authority of Al-Bahazi, who said: While we were with the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day on the road From the roads of Medina, and he said: How will you deal with a trial that will erupt in the ends of the earth as if they were cows? They said: So what shall we do? O Messenger of God, he said: This and his companions are upon you. He said: So I hastened to feel compassion for the man, and said: This is my Prophet. God said: This is Othman. (Ahmad 33. Ibn Hibban 6914)"
"32688","(32688) Ismail Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ajra that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He mentioned a tribulation and brought it near. Then a masked man passed by and said: This and his companions will be on the right path at that time. So the man went, took him by the shoulders and turned his face to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This. He said: Yes, then it is Othman. (Ibn Majah 1111 and Ahmad 243)"
"32689","(32689) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: When Uthman was killed, the preachers of Ilya Then a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Murā ibn Ka’b, rose up from the last of them and said: If it were not for a hadith. I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as I stood. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a temptation, I think. He said: So he approached her, and a masked man passed by, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: This and his companions will be upon the truth from that time. So she went off, grabbed his shoulders, and turned with his face to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: This is it. He said: Yes, then it is Othman. (Ahmed 235)"
"32690","(32690) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sadaqi bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: I heard my grandfather Riyah bin Al-Harith narrate, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Othman is in Paradise."
"32691","(32691) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The most sincere of my nation is Othman."
"32692","(32692) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, that a man from Quraysh called Thumamah was on the authority of Sana'a. When he came to him when he killed Uthman, he wept for a long time. When he woke up, he said: Today the prophecy has been taken away, or he said: A difference. Prophecy became kingship and tyranny. Whoever conquers something eats it."
"32693","(32693) Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, who said: Aisha said: Othman was the one who comforted them and brought them to the womb."
"32694","(32694) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his commanders, that Uthman carried a thousand camels in the army of hardship, minus seventy. He filled it with horses."
"32695","(32695) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan, who said: Abdullah said when Othman was appointed successor: What Turn us away from its highest level, that which is above it."
"32696","(32696) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, who said: I heard Abdullah say when Othman was pledged allegiance: We did not turn away from the highest of the above."
"32697","(32697) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, he said: He said Ibn Abbas: If the people had gathered to kill Uthman, they would have stoned him just as the people of Lot were stoned."
"32698","(32698) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, that a man called Jajaha took up a stick. It was in the hand of Othman, so he broke it with his knee, and from that place he threw it to eat."
"32699","(32699) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Abi Habib, who said: Ka’b said: As if Look at this man, and in his hand are two flames of fire, meaning he fought Uthman and killed him."
"32700","(32700) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Qais told us, he said: Abu Salalah, his servant, told us Othman said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness: I wished to have some of my companions with me, so Aisha said: Shall I call Abu Bakr for you? She said: So she remained silent, so I knew that he did not want it, so I said: Should I pray for you Omar? She remained silent, and I knew that he did not want it. I said: Should I pray for you, Ali? She remained silent, and I knew that he did not want him. I said: Shall I invite Othman bin Affan for you? He said: Yes, so I invited him, and when he came, he motioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to keep your distance, so he came and sat next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to say to him, “And the color of Othman has changed.” Qays said: So Abu Sallah told me, he said: On the day of the resurrection, Othman was told: Do not fight, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He delivered a covenant to me, and I will be patient with him. Abu Sahlā said: So they saw that it was that gathering. (Ibn Saad 66. Ahmed 52)"
"32701","(32701) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, who said: I heard Uthman say: The greatest of you in singing in my eyes is the one who restrains his weapons and his hands."
"32702","(32702) Affan told us, he said: Wahib and Hammad told us, they said: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding his saying: {Is He equal to Him and whoever enjoins justice and is on a straight path} He said: He is Othman bin Affan."
"32703","(32703) Affan told us, he said: Sa’id bin Zaid told us, he said: Asim bin Bahdaliya told us, he said: Abu Wael told us, On the authority of Aisha, she said: Othman was writing Abu Bakr’s will, she said: Then he fainted, so he hastened and wrote: Omar bin Al-Khattab. When he woke up, Abu Bakr said to him: Who did you write to? He said: Omar bin Al-Khattab. He said: You wrote what I wanted, what I commanded you to do. With it, even if you wrote yourself down, you would be worthy of it."
"32704","(32704) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Kulayb bin Wael, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Malika, He said: A man asked Ibn Umar about Uthman. He said: He witnessed Badr. He said: No. He said: Did he witness the Battle of al-Ridwan? He said: No. He said: So, did he turn away on the day the two groups met? He said: Yes. He said: Then the man went and it was said to Ibn Umar: This man claims that you insulted Othman, he said: They turned him back to him, he said: They turned him back to him, and he said to him: Did you understand what I said to you? He said: Yes, he said: Did you ask me? Othman witnessed Badr, so I told you: No, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, Othman is in your need and his need. Your Messenger, so he struck him with his arrow, and you asked me if he witnessed the sale of Al-Ridwan. He said: So I said to you: No, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He sent a delegation to the parties to bid farewell and greet us, but they refused, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He pledged allegiance to him and said: Oh God, Othman is in need of you and the need of your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he wiped with one of his hands. On the other hand, he pledged allegiance to him, and you asked me whether Othman had assumed power on the day the two groups met. He said: So I said: Yes, and indeed it is God. He said: {Indeed, those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met, Satan caused them to slip only because of part of what they had earned, and indeed God had pardoned them} So go and do your best. (Abu Dawud 2720. Tabarani 125)"
"32705","(32705) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, who said: A man asked Ibn Omar, on the authority of Othman, so he mentioned his best deeds, then he said: Perhaps that will make you bad, so he said: Yes, so he said: May God force your soul."
"32706","(32706) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Hamid, he said: Abdul said: Allah Ibn Uqaym: I will never help in killing a caliph after Uthman. He said: Then he was told: And I helped with his blood. He said: I am preparing Mentioning his faults is an aid to his bloodshed."
"32707","(32707) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amir say: When the people began to attack Ali Othman, my father got up and prayed during the night, then he fell asleep. He said: He was told: Get up and ask God to protect you from the temptation from which He had been protected. His righteous servants. He said: Then he got up and fell ill. He said: He was not seen outside until he died."
"32708","(32708) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah bin Salih narrated to me, saying: Rabi’ bin Yazid narrated to me. Al-Dimashqi said: Abdullah bin Qais told us that Al-Numan heard Al-Numan bin Bashir that Muawiyah bin Abi had sent him Sufyan sent a letter to Aisha, so he pushed it to her, and she said to him: Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes. She said: One day I and Hafsah were with him. He said: If only we had a man who would talk to us. I said: Oh. Messenger of God, I will send to Abu Bakr and he will come and speak to us. He said: Then I remained silent, then Hafsa said: O Messenger of God, I will send To Omar and he spoke to us, but she remained silent. She said: He called a man and insisted on coming to him rather than us, so he left. Then Othman came and faced him. So I heard him say: O Uthman, God may give you a shirt, but if they want you to take it off, do not take it off three times. I said: O Mother of the Believers, where have you been regarding this hadith? She said: I forgot it as if I had never heard it before. \n(Ibn Majah 112 and Ahmad 149)"
"32709","(32709) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah informed me, on the authority of Iyas bin Salama, on the authority of his father that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to Uthman, one of his hands over the other, so the people said: Congratulations to my father. Abdullah circumambulated the Kaaba safely, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he had stayed for such and such a year, he would not have circumambulated. Until I roam. (Tabarani 144)"
"32710","(32710) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Salem, he said: Abdullah bin said: Omar: You blamed Othman for things that you would not have done if Omar had done them."
"32711","(32711) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Hilal ibn Waki`, on the authority of Uthman’s wife, she said: Uthman fell asleep, and when he woke up, he said: The people are killing me, so I said: No, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar. He said: They said: Break your fast with us. The night, or they said: You break your fast with us the night."
"32712","(32712) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Taman narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of his grandfather. Abu Habib, he said: I entered the house of Othman while he was besieged, and I heard Abu Hurairah say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: After me, you will encounter trials and disagreement. He said: Then someone said to him: What do you command me? He said: It is upon you. With the prince and his companions, and he struck Othman on the shoulder. (Hakim 99)"
"32713","(32713) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: Whenever Abu Hurairah mentioned killing Uthman, he would cry. It is as if I hear him saying: Haha, haha, wailing. (Ibn Saad 81)"
"32714","(32714) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, he said: She said when Uthman was killed You left it like a garment pure from filth, then you brought it near and slaughtered it as a ram is slaughtered. Was this not the case before? This, he said: Then Masruq said to her: This is what you did. You wrote to some people ordering them to go out. He said: So Aisha said: No. And in Him the believers believe and the disbelievers disbelieve in Him, I did not write to them black and white until I sat in My council. This, Al-Amash said: They believed that it was written on her tongue."
"32715","(32715) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, he said: I heard Ali making a speech saying: {Indeed, those to whom good deeds preceded among us are those far away from it} Othman said. Some of them"
"32716","(32716) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Uqba ibn Aws al-Sadusi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar said: There will be twelve caliphs in this nation: Abu Bakr, you have named him correctly, and Omar bin Al-Khattab. A horn of iron, you got its name right, and Othman bin Affan Dhul-Nourin was given two sureties of mercy. He was killed unjustly, you got it right. His name"
"32717","(32717) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of a scholar, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla entered upon al-Hajjaj and said: To those sitting with him: If you want to look at a man cursing the Commander of the Faithful Othman, then this is with you, meaning Abdul Rahman, Then Abdul Rahman said: May God forbid, O Prince, that I should curse Othman, for he would detain me. There is a verse in the Book about that. God, God said: {For the poor immigrants who were expelled from their homes and their wealth, seeking bounty from God and satisfaction. And they help Allah and His Messenger. Those are the truthful.” So Othman was one of them."
"32718","(32718) Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Ibn Layyaa told me, he said: Yazid bin Amr Al-Ma’afiri told me, He said: I heard Abu Thawr al-Fahmi saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Udays al-Balawi came and was one of those who pledged allegiance under the tree and went up. The pulpit thanked God and praised him, then he mentioned Othman, and Abu Thawr said: So I entered upon Othman while he was besieged, so I said: So-and-so mentioned such-and-such, so Othman said: And from where did you hide from God? Ten: Indeed, I am the fourth of Islam, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his daughter, then his daughter, and she pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with this hand. I did not touch the right hand with it, nor did I sing, nor did I wish, nor did I drink alcohol during my time, nor did I become a Muslim. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever buys this zinqa and adds it to the mosque will have a house. In Paradise, so I bought it and added it to the mosque. (Ibn Abi Asim 1308)"
"32719","(32719) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Milhan narrated to me, he said: It was mentioned by Ibn Omar Othman, and Omar, then Ibn Omar said: Have you seen that if you had two camels, one of them strong and the other weak, would you kill them? The weak"
"32720","(32720) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mus’ar, on the authority of Abu Salman, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, about Uthman, and Mis’ar said: He either said: You count him, or he said: We count him as one of our choices."
"32721","(32721) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Imran bin Umair, on the authority of Kulthum, who said: I heard Ibn Masoud say: What I love that you shot Othman with an arrow. Mas’ar said: I see that he wanted to kill him, and I do not have gold like anyone’s."
"32722","(32722) Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted Uthman and said to Uthman: May God forgive you for what you have put forward, what you have delayed, what you have concealed, what you have declared, what you have concealed, what you have revealed, and what you have revealed. He will exist until the Day of Resurrection.\n Abu Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:"
"32723","(32723) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Abu Aoun narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, he said: He mentioned Othman, and Al-Hassan bin Ali said: This is the Commander of the Faithful, he is coming to you now and informing you. He said: Then Ali came and said: It was Othman was one of those who {believed and did righteous deeds, then feared Him, and believed, then feared Him, and did good, and God loves those who do good.} until he completed The verse"
"32724","(32724) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Nafi’ bin Abd said: Al-Harith: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered one of the walls of the city, and said to him: Hold you at the door, so he came until... He sat on the stand and dangled his feet into the well, then the door was knocked on. I said: Who is this? He said: Abu Bakr. I said: O Messenger of God, this is Abu Bakr. He said: Give him permission and give him good tidings of Paradise. He said: So I gave permission. And I gave him good tidings of Paradise, so he came and sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the stand and dangled his feet into the well. Then the door was knocked on, and I said: Who is this? He said: Omar. I said: O Messenger of God, this is Omar? He said: Give him permission and give him good tidings. In Paradise, he said: So I gave him permission and gave him good news of Paradise, so he came and sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the stand and he showed him He put his feet in the well, then the door was knocked on, and I said: Who is this? He said: Othman. I said: O Messenger of God, this is Othman? He said: I gave him permission and gave him good tidings of Paradise with affliction. He said: So I gave him permission and gave him good tidings of Paradise, so he entered and sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his feet in the well. (Abu Dawud 5146, Ahmed 5146)"
"32725","(32725) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When Omar presented his daughter On Othman, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not guide Othman to someone who is better than her, and should I guide her to someone who is better than her? He is better for her than Othman. He said: So the Messenger of God married her and Othman married his daughter. (Hakim 106)"
"32726","(32726) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he was mentioned to Uthman, and a man said: They They revile him, and he said: Oh, they revile a man who entered upon the Negus among a group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. So each of them gave temptation to others. They said: What is the temptation that they gave him? He said: No one would enter upon him except him. He nodded to him, but Othman refused, so he said: What prevented you from prostrating as your companions prostrated? He said: I would not prostrate to anyone. Instead of God Almighty."
"32727","(32727) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Ali ibn Abu Talib, he said: By the one who separated the love and healed the soul, this is the covenant of the unlettered Prophet to me that no one will love me except a believer, and no No one hates me except a hypocrite. (Ahmad 95. Ibn Hibban 6924)"
"32728","(32728) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever I am his guardian is my guardian. (Ahmad 3500 Bazar 2535)"
"32729","(32729) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Umm Musa, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: By the one by whom I swear If Ali was the closest person to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: We promised the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The day he was arrested in Aisha’s house, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, started morning after lunch saying: Did he come to Ali? Repeatedly, she said: I think he was sent on a pilgrimage. She said: Then he came after that, so we thought that he had a need for him, so we left the house, so we sat at the door, and I was one of the closest to them from the door, so Ali leaned down on me and made his left side and he spoke to me, then That day was spent, and he was the closest person to him in his covenant. Women's 7108. Tabarani 887)"
"32730","(32730) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar, and he said: Tell me, On the authority of Ali, he said: If you want to ask about Ali, look at his place from the place of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. His abode, and this is the abode of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Indeed, I hate him. He said: So God hates you."
"32731","(32731) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to the people of Yemen to judge between them, and I said: O Messenger of God, I do not He taught me about the decree, he said: Then he struck my chest with his hand and said: O God, guide his heart and guide his tongue, so I did not doubt it. A decision was made between two people until I sat in these two sessions."
"32732","(32732) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, they said: No. He said: Tell us about yourself. He said: If I asked, I was given, and if I remained silent, I began. (Nasa’i 8505)"
"32733","(32733) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr Ibn Hind Al-Jamali, on the authority of Ali, who said: I was If I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would give me, and if I remained silent they would give me something. (Tirmidhi 3722, Hakim 125)"
"32734","(32734) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Habashi ibn Junada, who said: I said to him: O Abu Ishaq, where? I saw him. He said: He stood over us in our gathering and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Ali is from him and I am From Him, and no one can take care of me except Ali. (Tirmidhi 3719. Ibn Majah 119)"
"32735","(32735) Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: We were In Al-Juhfa, Ghadir Khumm, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out against us and took Ali by the hand and said: Who are you? His master, Ali is his master."
"32736","(32736) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Riyah bin Al-Harith, who said: “Ali was sitting in Al-Rahbih when he A man came to him after traveling and said: Peace be upon you, my master. He said: Who is this? They said: This is Abu Ayyub. Al-Ansari, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master.\n(Tabarani 4052)"
"32737","(32737) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: He succeeded The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked Ali bin Abi Talib in his invasion of Tabuk, and he said: O Messenger of God, you will leave me behind in the matter of women. And the two boys. He said: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?\n(Bukhari 4416. Muslim 31)"
"32738","(32738) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Saad narrating on the authority of Saad, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said to Ali: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me in the same position as Aaron was to Moses?\n(Bukhari 37061 Muslim 1871)"
"32739","(32739) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Al-Jinni, he said: Fatima, the son of Ali, narrated to me, she said: Asma Ibn Umays told me, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying to Ali: You are from me in your place. Aaron is from Moses, except that there is no prophet after me. (Nasa’i 8143 and Ahmad 438)"
"32740","(32740) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Ali: You are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after you."
"32741","(32741) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Saad, who said: Muawiyah presented in Some of his arguments, and Saad came to him, and they mentioned Ali, and Mu’awiyah got angry at him, and Saad got angry, and said: You say this to a man, I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says he has three qualities, because having one of them is more beloved to me than the world, and what In it: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master, and I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. God, peace and blessings be upon him, says: You are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: I will give the opinion to a man who loves God and His Messenger (Muslim 1871, Tirmidhi 2999)"
"32742","(32742) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hasira, he said: Abu Sulaiman Al-Janni narrated to me, Meaning Zayd bin Wahhab, he said: I heard Ali on the pulpit saying: I am the servant of God, and the brother of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. No one said it before me, and no one will say it after me except a liar and slanderer."
"32743","(32743) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, Al-Manhal, and Isa, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Ali used to go out in the winter wearing a loincloth and two light robes, and in the summer in So I asked my father, So I said: The people have seen something in the Commander of the Faithful that they disapproved of. He said: What is that? He said: He goes out in the intense heat in The stuffed cloak and the heavy dress, and he does not care about that, and goes out in the extreme cold in the two light clothes. And the two angels did not care about that and did not fear the cold. Did you hear anything about that? They ordered me to ask you: She asked him if she had prayed with him, so he prayed with him, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, the people have missed something about you. He said: What is it? He said: You go out in extreme heat in a stuffed abaya or a heavy garment, and you go out in extreme cold in two light garments. And in the two nights, you did not care about that, and you did not fear the cold. He said: And you were not with us, O Abu Layla, in Khaybar. He said: I said: Yes, by God, I have been with you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Bakr, so he marched with the people and was defeated. Until he returned to him, and he sent Omar, and he defeated the people until he reached him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will give you the opinion of a man who loves God and His Messenger and whom God and His Messenger love, for whom God will grant victory, who is not escaping, so he sent So he invited me, and I came to him while I was in my eyes and could not see anything. He spit in my eyes and said: O God, protect him from the heat and the cold. He said: Neither heat nor cold has harmed me yet. (Ahmed 99)"
"32744","(32744) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O people of Quraysh, God will surely send against you a man from among you whose heart God has tested for faith. He will strike you, or behead you. Abu Bakr said: I am he, O Messenger of God. He said: No, so Omar said: I am he. O Messenger of God, he said: No, but he is a shoe maker, and he gave Ali his shoes so he could clean them. (Tirmidhi 2460, Ahmed 155)"
"32745","(32745) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: We were sitting in the mosque when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and sat next to us, touching our heads. The bird, none of us spoke, so he said: There is a man among you who fights the people over the interpretation of the Qur’an just as you were fought over its revelation. Then Abu Bakr stood up and said: I am he, O Messenger of God. He said: No. Then Omar stood up and said: I am him, O Messenger of God. He said: No, but he The shoemaker in the room said: Then Ali came out to us, and he had with him the sandals of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he repaired them.\n(Ahmad 31, Hakim 122)"
"32746","(32746) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Ali, indeed you Treasure in Paradise, and indeed you are the possessor of its two horns, so do not follow one look with another, for the first is only yours and the last is not yours."
"32747","(32747) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Salih, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, he said: I heard Ali says: I am the servant of God, and the brother of His Messenger, and I am the greatest truthful. No one will say this after me except a liar and slanderer, and he has I prayed seven years before the people."
"32748","(32748) Shababhi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Habib al-‘Arniy, on the authority of Ali, he said: I am the first man He prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 141. Ibn Saad 21)"
"32749","(32749) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Jabr, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awf, and he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he departed to Taif and besieged it for nineteen days. Or eighteen, but he did not open it, then he departed in spirit, or in the morning and came down, then he migrated, then he said: Who are the people? I am generous to you and I enjoin you to do good to my family, and your destination is the basin, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, that you may establish prayer. And you will be given the zakat, or I will send to you a man from me, or like myself, and he will strike the necks of those who fight them and take them captive. Their descendants, he said: Then the people saw that it was Abu Bakr, or Omar, so he took Ali by the hand and said: This is it.\n(Bazzar 1050 and Hakim 120)"
"32750","(32750) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abi Fakhita, he said: Tell me Bayra bin Yarim, on the authority of Ali, said: A garment tied with silk was presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Either he lined it with silk or woven it, so he sent it to me, and I came to him and said: What should I do with it? He put it on, and he said: No, it was not I accept for you what I hate for myself."
"32751","(32751) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Fakhita, he said: Ja’adah bin Bira, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Abdul Rahim."
"32752","(32752) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiya bin Ka’b, on the authority of Ali, who said when he died Abu Talib: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, your uncle, the misguided sheikh, has died. He said: So he said: Go and bury him, then do not say anything until you come to me. He said: So I bury him, then I came to him and he commanded me, so I washed, then He supplicated for me with supplications that I would not like to have, including anything on earth."
"32753","(32753) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani ibn Hani, on the authority of Ali, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: You are of me and I am of you. (Abu Dawud 2274, Ahmed 98)"
"32754","(32754) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zaid bin Yatha’i, who said: It has reached Ali that people are saying about him, He said: Then he ascended the pulpit and said: I call upon a man to call upon God, and I call upon him only from among the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. He heard from the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he did not stand up, so he stood up six times, and six of those people led Saeed bin Wahhab, so they said: We testify. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever I am his master, Ali is his master. Oh God, befriend whomever is his friend and oppose whomever. He used to\n(Ahmad 1022, Bazzar 2541)"
"32755","(32755) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zayd al-Awdi, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Hurairah entered the mosque. So we gathered to him, and a young man stood up to him and said: I adjure you by God. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Who I was his master, so Ali is his master. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him. He said: Yes, so the young man said: I am innocent of you. I bear witness that you have been hostile to those who are loyal to you, and you have been loyal to those who are hostile to you.” He said, “The people treated him with pebbles.” (Bazzar 2531, Abu Ali 6392)"
"32756","(32756) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Amiri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. A delegation from the Sarh family from Yemen greeted them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “You must perform prayers and pay zakat, and you must listen.” And you will obey, or I will send to you a man like myself who will fight you and take your descendants captive. Oh God, me, or Like myself, then he took Ali's hand. (Ahmed 1024)"
"32757","(32757) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, who said: Al-Hasan bin Ali gave a speech when Ali was killed. He said: O people of Kufa, or O people of Iraq, there was among you a man who was killed during the night, or was wounded. Today, the ancients have not preceded him in knowledge, nor will the others surpass him. Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to On his journey, Gabriel was on his right, and Mikael was on his left, and he will not return until God grants victory to him."
"32758","(32758) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Murah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: It was mentioned to him what people said about Ali, and he said: We sat with him, we ate him, we drank him, and we stood up to him. deeds. I did not hear him say anything of what they say. It is enough for you to say: The cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and was circumcised, and he witnessed the Battle of Al-Ridwan, and he witnessed the Battle of Badr."
"32759","(32759) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Minin, and he is Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will convey my opinion to a man who loves God and His Messenger. He said: Then the people became arrogant, and he said: How is Ali? They said: He complained about his eyes. So he called him and he spit on his palms and wiped them with them. He appointed Ali, then handed over the opinion to him, and God granted victory to him that day. (Muslim 1871, Ahmad 384)"
"32760","(32760) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: While the Prophet was praying May God bless him and grant him peace. A group of his companions was with him, so he sent to his wives but did not find anything with any of them. While they were doing that, Ali came upon a dusty barn, on his shoulders, close to a saa’ of dates, which he had made with his own hands. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Welcome to the pregnant woman and the one being carried, then he made him sit down and shook the dirt off his head, then he said: He welcomed Abu Turab, so he brought him closer, and they ate until they were satisfied, then he sent to his wives, to each one of them, in a group."
"32761","(32761) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He handed over the flag to Ali, and he said: We will hand it over to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. He said: He spit in his eyes and was ashen. He said: He prayed for him and news was opened for him. (Abdul Razzaq 10395)"
"32762","(32762) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Umar bin Asid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Ali bin Abu Talib had three qualities because having one of them is dearer to me than red camels: He gave him his daughter in marriage and she bore him, and he provided The doors except his door, and he gave him the war on the Day of Khaybar."
"32763","(32763) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Iyas bin Salamah told me, he said: My father told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to Ali, and he said: I will give the opinion to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. He said: I brought him leading him, white-haired. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spat. He greeted him in his eyes, then gave him the banner, and the conquest was at his hand. (Muslim 1433. Ahmad 51)"
"32764","(32764) Abu Bakr bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Saeed, on the authority of Juma bin Umair, who said: I entered upon Aisha. And my mother and my aunt. We asked her: How was Ali with him? She said: You are asking me about a man who lowered his hand from the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a place where no one has ever been, and his soul flowed into his hand, and he wiped his face with it and died. It was said: Where will you bury him? Ali said: There is no spot on earth more beloved to God than a spot where his Prophet was killed, so we buried him. (Abu Ali 4845)"
"32765","(32765) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Shayba, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shayba, she said: Aisha said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out in the morning wearing a black hair cap, so Al-Hasan came and let him in. with him, then Hussein came and let him in with him, then Fatimah came and he let her in, then Ali came and he let him in, then he said: {It is only God desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you with a thorough purification}"
"32766","(32766) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Ammar, who said: I entered upon a group of people, and there were some people with them. So they mentioned Ali and insulted him, so he insulted him with them, so he said: Shall I not tell you what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes, He said: I came to Fatima and asked her about Ali, and she said: He went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sat down, and the Messenger of God came. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and with him were Ali, Hassan, and Hussein, each one of them taking him by the hand until he entered and brought Ali closer. And Fatima made them sit between his hands, and Hasan and Husayn made each one of them sit on his thigh, then he wrapped them around them. His garment, or he said: a garment, then he recited these verses: {Allah only desires to remove uncleanness from you, O People of the House}, then He said: Oh God, these are my household, and my household has more right. (Ahmad 1071. Tabarani 160)"
"32767","(32767) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Atiyya, Abu Al-Mu’adhil Al-Taffawi, on the authority of his father, he said: You informed me. Umm Salamah reported that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with her in her house one day, so she came to the servant and said: Ali and Fatima with the cloak, and he said: Step aside for me, on behalf of my household. So I stepped aside towards the house, and Ali entered. And Fatima, Hassan, and Hussein, so he placed them in his lap, and he took Ali with one of his hands and hugged him to him, and took So he comforted them with his other hand, held them close to him and kissed them, and covered them with black khamis, then said: Oh God, no. To Hell, I and my household. She said: So I called him, and I said: And I, O Messenger of God. He said: And you. (Ahmad 2961. Tabarani 939)"
"32768","(32768) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubaira bin Yarim said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Ali stand up as a preacher and address the people, and he said: O people, a man left you yesterday. The ancients preceded him, and the others will not overtake him. Indeed, it was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was sent. So he gives him the opinion and does not return until God grants victory to him, Gabriel on his right and Mikael on his left. He left neither white nor yellow, except seven hundred dirhams left over from his giving, with which he wanted to buy a servant. (Ahmed 1994, Bazzar 2574)"
"32769","(32769) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Hamza, the client of the Ansar, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam, he said: The first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali. Amr Ibn Murra said: So I went to Ibrahim. So I mentioned that to him, but he denied it and said: Abu Bakr. (Ahmad 368, Tayalisi 678)"
"32770","32770) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabaliya, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not fight He gave his weapons to Ali or his names."
"32771","(32771) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Masoud bin Saad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Maqil, On the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar Al-Aslami, on the authority of Amr bin Shas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He You have harmed me. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, I do not like to harm you. He said: Whoever harms Ali has harmed me.\n(Bazzar 2561, Ahmed 483)"
"32772","(32772) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, who said: I said to Ata’: He was among the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is there anyone more knowledgeable than Ali? He said: No, by God, I do not know him!"
"32773","(32773) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Habashi, who said: Al-Hasan bin Ali after the death of Ali, and he said: A man left you yesterday whom the ancients did not precede in knowledge, and the others have not overtaken him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give him the opinion, but he would not leave until God granted him victory. (Ahmed 199)"
"32774","(32774) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabab, on the authority of Anas, who said: Ali and I went out with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the walls of the city, so we passed by a garden, and Ali said: How beautiful this garden is! The Messenger of God, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your garden in Paradise[corrupt] With seven gardens, all of which Ali says: How beautiful is this garden, O Messenger of God, and he says: Your garden is in Heaven is better than this. (Tabarani 11084)"
"32775","(32775) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of A scholar, on the authority of Salman, said: The first of this nation to welcome its Prophet, its first to Islam was Ali bin Abi Talib."
"32776","(32776) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, he said: She said to me Umm Salama: O Abu Abdullah, will the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, be reviled among you, and then you will not change? He said: I said: And who He curses the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: He curses me and those who love him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He loves him. (Ahmad 323; Abu Ali 6977)"
"32777","(32777) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Fudail, on the authority of Abu Nasr, on the authority of Masawar al-Himyari, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: No believer will hate Ali, nor will a hypocrite love him.\n(Ahmad 292. Tabarani 885)"
"32778","(32778) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Ali, he said: Our example in this nation is like the shroud of Noah and the kebab of Hattah among the Children of Israel."
"32779","(32779) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Quram, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Ali said: He does not love us. A hypocrite, and let no believer hate us."
"32780","(32780) Abu Usamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Talha narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Hakam Al-Azdi, narrating His hadith is that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali: You will encounter a hardship after me. He said: O Messenger of God, in the peace of My religion. He said: Yes, in peace from your religion. (Hakim 140)"
"32781","(32781) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa’, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. He said: We camped at Ghadir Khumm. He said: So we were called to him: Prayer. He gathered and sat for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, under a tree and prayed the noon prayer. He took Ali by the hand and said: Aren’t you Do you know that I have more right to the believers than to themselves? They said: Yes. He said: Do you not know that I have more right to every believer than to them? Himself. They said: Yes. He said: Then he took Ali’s hand and said: Oh God, whomever I am his master, Ali is his master. Oh God, whoever By Allah, he returned to whoever was hostile to him, he said: Then Omar met him after that, and said: Congratulations to you, Ibn Abi Talib, in the morning. And you have become the master of every believing man, male and female. (Nasa’i 8473. Ahmad 281)"
"32782","(32782) Abu Al-Jawab told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent two armies, one of which was Ali bin Abi Talib, and the other was Khalid bin Al-Walid. He said: If there is a real fight against the people, and Ali opens a fortress and takes a female slave for himself, then Khaled wrote with his equal, so when The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read the letter and said: What do you say about a man who loves God and His Messenger and God loves him? And His Messenger. (Tirmidhi 1704, Ahmad 356)"
"32783","(32783) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyya bin Saad, saying: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and he An old man, and his eyebrows fell over his eyes, said: So I said: Tell us about this man, Ali bin Abi Talib. He said: He raised his eyebrows with his hand, then said: He is one of the best of human beings."
"32784","(32784) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Yazid Al-Rashk narrated to me, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a convoy and appointed a superior over them, and he did something to me. They denied it, so four of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, agreed to mention their matter to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And when they came from a journey, they would start with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they would greet him and look at him, then They departed to their camps. He said: When the convoy arrived, they greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of the four stood up. He said: O Messenger of God, did you not see that Ali did such-and-such, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him? He knew the anger on his face, so he said: Whatever you want from Ali, whatever you want from Ali, Ali is from me and I am from Ali, and Ali The guardian of every believer after me. (Abu Dawud 829. Ahmad 437)"
"32785","(32785) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, saying: Shaqiq bin Abi Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr bin Khalid bin narrated to us. Arfatiya, he said: I came to Saad bin Malik in Medina, and he said: It was mentioned to me that you insult Ali. He said: We did it, he said: Perhaps you have insulted him. He said: I said: God forbid. He said: Do not curse him. If the saw were placed on my side, I would have cursed Ali. I never insulted him, after what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Ali 773)"
"32786","(32786) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Maimunah, she said: When The group was when it was said to Maimunah ibn Al-Harith: O Mother of the Believers, and she said: You must give up Ibn Abi Talib, by God. He did not go astray, nor did he go astray. (Tabarani 12. Hakim 141)"
"32787","(32787) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: {You have made the pilgrims’ water-carriers and the caretakers of the Sacred Mosque} he said: It was revealed about Ali and Abbas. (Abdul Razzaq 269)"
"32788","(32788) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Ali said: No one has done it. Before me, and no one will use it after me. I had a dinar, so I sold it for ten dirhams, so when I talked to the Messenger of God, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I gave in charity a dirham until it ran out, then he recited these verses: {O you who have believed! Messenger, so present your disputes truthfully before me. (Ibn Jarir 20)"
"32789","(32789) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah Al-Ashja’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mugheerah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ali bin Alqamiya Al-Anmari, on the authority of Ali, he said: When this was revealed The verse: {O you who have believed, when you debate with the Messenger, then present your disputes with truthfulness before Me}. He said: The Messenger of God said to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: What do you see? A dinar. I said: They cannot bear it. He said: How much? You said: A barley. He said: It is too much. He said: So the verse was revealed: {Have you the fear that you will present alms before yourselves for your disputes}? \n(Tirmidhi 3300 and Ibn Hibban 6942)"
"32790","(32790) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Harun, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when Nafi’ bin Al-Azraq came to him and he stood up. On his head, and he said: By God, I hate Ali. He said: Then Ibn Umar raised his head to him and said: God hates you, you hate A man whose precedence is better than this world and what is in it."
"32791","(32791) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he said: There have been many virtues in Ali, such that if one of them were to be divided among the people, it would be more than enough for them."
"32792","(32792) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Dinar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qur’a, he said: It was me and Al-Hasan. We were sitting and talking, when Al-Hasan mentioned Ali, and said: He showed them the way, and established the religion for them when they had gone astray."
"32793","(32793) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zaid, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Ali is in Paradise. (Abu Dawud 4617, Ahmed 188)"
"32794","(32794) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Fatima said: O Messenger of God, You have given me in marriage to a man with broad legs, a large stomach, and dark eyes. He said: I have married you to the most peaceful of my nation and the most forbearing of them. And the most knowledgeable of them.\n(Abdul Razzaq 9783)"
"32795","(32795) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Buraidah, said: I went on a campaign with Ali to Yemen, and I saw that he was dry, so when I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I mentioned Ali and I looked at him, and the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed, and he said: Aren’t you Who has more right to the believers than they themselves? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. (Ahmad 3471 Hakim 110)"
"32796","(32796) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi, who said: Ali said: Some people will love me until they enter Hell for my love, and some people will hate me until they enter Hell because of my hatred."
"32797","(32797) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abi Habra, who said: I heard Ali say: He will destroy you in two men: the one who loves me excessively and the one who hates me excessively."
"32798","(32798) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent With his acquittal, he went with Abu Bakr to Mecca, so he summoned him and sent Ali, and he said: Only a man from Ahl al-Bayt can convey it.\n(Tirmidhi 3090, Ahmad 212)"
"32799","(32799) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Hakim, on the authority of Abu Maryam, who said: I heard Ali saying: May God destroy me. Two men: one who loves me excessively and one who hates me excessively."
"32800","(32800) Abu Al-Jawab narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Zayd bin Yatha’i, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The sons of Wali’ah will be destroyed, or I will send to them a man like myself, and he will go on with them.” My command, so he kills the fighter and takes captive the offspring. (Nasa’i 8457, Ahmad 966)"
"32801","(32801) Muttalib bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, he said: Ali ascended the pulpit and said: O God, curse everyone who hates us. He said: And every one who loves us is precious."
"32802","(32802) Muttalib bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Laith, he said: I entered upon Abu Ja`far, and he mentioned his sins and what he feared. He said: So he cried, then he said: Jabir told me that Ali carried the door on the Day of Khaybar until the Muslims went up and opened it, and that he was tried and did not Only forty men will carry it. (Bayhaqi 212)"
"32803","(32803) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Waqid bin Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: O people, watch over Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his family. (Bukhari 3751)"
"32804","(32804) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Ali: You are my brother and companion."
"32805","(32805) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Makin, on the authority of his maternal uncle, Abu Umayyah, that Ali passed by a house in order to build a house, so it fell. He broke a brick, or broke a brick, so he prayed to God not to complete its construction. He said: No brick was placed in it. Milk"
"32806","(32806) Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were with Abu Ja`far in the mosque and a boy was looking at my father. Ja'far was crying. Abu Ja'far said to him: What makes you cry? He said: From your love. He said: I looked where God looked and chose whom God chose."
"32807","(32807) Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, he said: I heard her say: My father, by God, to whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents on the day of Uhud. (Ahmad 1301)"
"32808","(32808) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ali bin Abi A student said: I did not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ransom anyone with his parents except Saad. I heard him say: On the day of Uhud: Accuse Sa’d, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. (Bukhari 2905, Muslim 1876)"
"32809","(32809) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I heard Sa’d Ibn Abi Waqqas narrates that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents to him on the day of Uhud.\n(Bukhari 3725. Tirmidhi 2830)"
"32810","(32810) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I heard Sa`d say: I was the first Arab man to throw stones. With an arrow in the way of God in battle and during battle. (Bukhari 3728, Muslim 2278)"
"32811","(32811) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Balaj, who said: I heard Mus’ab bin Sa’d narrate that Sa’d was a servant’s servant. He wanted something from him, so he said: I don’t have anything to give you, and he went for dinars and put them on his sandals, so he called Saad. Ali and her sandals were stolen."
"32812","(32812) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of Mus`ab ibn Sa`d, on the authority of his father that He heard a man praying for Ali, so he prayed for her, but she stumbled upon him and killed him."
"32813","(32813) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fear the supplications of Saad\n(Ibn Saad 142)"
"32814","(32814) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Al-Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zaid, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Sa’d is in Paradise."
"32815","(32815) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, that Abdullah told him that Aisha was She talks about the fact that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stayed up one night while he was beside you. She said: So I said: O Messenger of God What is the matter with you? He said: I wish a righteous man from my nation could guard me at night. He said: While we were like that, I heard a voice The weapon. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who is this? He said: I am Saad bin Malik. He said: He did not bring you. I said: I came. I will guard you, O Messenger of God. He said: I heard the snoring of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his sleep.\n(Bukhari 2885. Muslim 40)"
"32816","(32816) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, he said: I saw to the right of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to his left, on the day of Uhud, two men wearing white clothes. I have not seen them before or after, meaning Gabriel and Michael. (Muslim 1802. Ibn Hibban 6987)"
"32817","(32817) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, who said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab saying: Sa’d was Ibn Abi Waqqas was the strongest of the Muslims on the Day of Uhud."
"32818","(32818) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Utbah, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman, he said: The first Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him."
"32819","(32819) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I saw the hand of Talha ibn Ubaid Allah Shala’, and he protected her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud. (Bukhari 4063. Ibn Majah 128)"
"32820","(32820) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaid Allah bin Ishaq bin Talha, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, he said: I saw twenty-four wounds on his sword, which he inflicted with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"32821","(32821) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zaid, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Talhah is in Paradise."
"32822","(32822) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of his uncle Isa bin Talha, that a Bedouin came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him about those who had lost their lives, but he turned away from them. Then he asked him, but he turned away from them. He said: Talhah bin Ubaid Allah entered from the door of the mosque wearing two green garments, and said: This is one of those who made the decree. We love you\n(Tirmidhi 3203 and Ibn Saad 218)"
"32823","(32823) Omar bin Bishr told us, he said: Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya bin Abbad told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Zubair, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say that on that day: It means the day of Uhud: Talhah is obligatory, meaning the day of Uhud. (Tirmidhi 1692, Hakim 25)"
"32824","(32824) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, that Talhah stood up to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted with his hand, and it struck and his finger was paralyzed."
"32825","(32825) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: Plural for li The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his parents on the day of Qurayz, and he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. (Nasa’i 10030. Ibn Hibban 6984)"
"32826","(32826) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundakir, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Al-Zubayr is the son of my cousin and a disciple from your nation. (Nasa’i 8212 and Ahmad 413)"
"32827","(32827) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zaid, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Zubair is in Paradise."
"32828","(32828) Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, who said: He who saw Al-Zubayr narrated to me. Ibn Al-Awwam and his chest are like springs from stabbing and shooting."
"32829","(32829) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, who said: The first man to draw a sword in God Al-Zubair, my blast was blown: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was taken, and Al-Zubair came out and cut people with his sword, and the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace in the highest place of Mecca. He said: What is the matter with you, Zubayr? He said: I was told that you were captured. He said: So he prayed for him. He prayed for him and his sword."
"32830","(32830) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said On the Day of the Trench: Who is a man who will go and bring me the news of Banu Qurayz? So Al-Zubayr rode and brought him their news. Then he came back and said: Three times: Who will bring me their news? He said: Al-Zubair: Yes. He said: And he pluralized for Al-Zubair his parents. He said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, and he said to Al-Zubair: Every prophet has a disciple, and the disciples are Al-Zubair and the son of my cousin. (Tirmidhi 3745. Ahmad 307)"
"32831","(32831) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair. (Tirmidhi 3744, Ahmed 89)"
"32832","(32832) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Bahi, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, he said: She said to me: Your parents were among Those who responded to God and the Messenger after the affliction had afflicted them. (Muslim 1881)"
"32833","(32833) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: He heard Ibn Omar is a man who says: I am the son of a disciple of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ibn Omar said: If you are from the family of Al-Zubayr Otherwise, no. (Tabarani 225)"
"32834","(32834) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: He was not with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr. Other than two horses, one of them is on Al-Zubayr. (Ibn Saad 103)"
"32835","(32835) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zayd. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Abdul Rahman bin Awf is in Paradise."
"32836","(32836) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, that Ali and Amr bin Al-Aas came to the grave of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf mentioned that one of them said: Go, Ibn Awf, for she has attained her purity and preceded her race, and he said The other: Go, Ibn Awf, for you have gone with your belly, and you have not expressed any concern about it. (Ahmad 1255, Hakim 308)"
"32837","(32837) Ghandar narrated to us on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard my father narrating that he heard Amr bin Al-Aas. He said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf died, he said: Ibn Awf went with your belly, you did not grieve any of it."
"32838","(32838) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein used to ride on the backs of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, and the people began to bow to them, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They will call them my father and my mother. Whoever loves me, let him love these two. (Ibn Hibban 6970, Tabarani 2644)"
"32839","(32839) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, means: Oh God, I love them, so love them. It means good and good. (Ahmad 531, Abu Ali 6187)"
"32840","(32840) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. He said: He said, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, means: Al-Hassan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. (Tirmidhi 3768 and Ahmad 64)"
"32841","(32841) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Misra al-Nahdi, on the authority of al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I prayed Maghrib with him, then he stood up and prayed until He prayed the evening prayer, then he went out and I followed him, and he said: An angel came to me and asked his Lord’s permission to greet me and give me good tidings that good And Al-Hussein is the master of the youth of the people of Paradise."
"32842","(32842) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, raised Al-Hasan bin Ali was with him on the pulpit, and he said: This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will reconcile two groups of Muslims through him.\n(Bukhari 2704)"
"32843","(32843) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Al-Hasan And Al-Hussein is the master of the youth of the people of Paradise. (Tabarani 2599)"
"32844","(32844) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Ali Al-Amiri; That Hassan and Hussein came seeking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he joined them to him, and said: The boy Stingy and cowardly. (Ibn Majah 3661 and Ahmad 172)"
"32845","(32845) Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Subih the client of Umm Salama, on the authority of Zaid bin Numbers is that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Fatima, Ali, Hassan, and Hussein: I am at war with those who fought you, and he said hello. To those who are at peace with you. (Ibn Majah 145 and Ibn Hibban 6977)"
"32846","(32846) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zam’i narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Zaid. Ibn Al-Muhajir, he said: Muslim Ibn Abi Sahl Al-Nabbal informed me, he said: Hassan Ibn Asama Ibn Zaid informed me, he said: Abu Osama told me, he said: I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night for some need, he said: and he left. And it contained something that I did not know what it was, so when I finished my need, I said: What is this that you are including? Then he looked and saw Hasan and Hussein on his knees, and said: These are my sons and your daughter’s sons. Oh God, you know that I love them. So he loved them.\n(Tirmidhi 3769. Ibn Hibban 6967)"
"32847","(32847) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took me and Al-Hasan and said: Oh God, I love them, so love them. (Bukhari 3735. Tabarani 2642)"
"32848","(32848) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to curse The people of Najran took the hand of Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, and Fatima was walking behind them. (Hakim 593)"
"32849","(32849) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I named my son. These are in the name of the two sons of Aaron: Shabbar and Shabair. (Hakim 168. Tabarani 2778)"
"32850","(32850) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, heard Al-Hassan, or Al-Hussein, crying, so he got up in fear and said: The boy has bewitched me. I have risen to him, and how wise is he?"
"32851","(32851) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He took me and Al-Hassan and said: Oh God, I love them both, so love them."
"32852","(32852) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Zuhair ibn al-Aqmar. He said: While Al-Hasan bin Ali was giving a sermon, a man of the lion, Adam Twal, stood up and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted him and placed him in his grave, saying: Whoever loves me, let him love him, let him convey the news to the witness who is absent. (Bukhari 312, Ahmad 366)"
"32853","(32853) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving us a sermon, when Hasan and Hussein came, wearing red shirts. They walked and stumbled and got up, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down and took them and placed them in his hands. Then he said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth: (Your wealth and your children are only temptations.) I saw these two, but I was not patient. Then he began to I got engaged"
"32854","(32854) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Mahdi bin Maimun narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub, On the authority of Ibn Abi Naam, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Omar when a man came to him and asked him about mosquito blood? Ibn Omar said to him: Who are you from? He said: A man from the people of Iraq. Ibn Omar said: Look, they are asking me about the blood of mosquitoes, and they killed the son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: They are my fragrance from this world. (Bukhari 5994. Ahmad 93)"
"32855","(32855) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim informed me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub. On the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was called to pray, and he went out while he was pregnant. Hassan, or Hussein, so he placed him on his side and prostrated between the two of them in prayer, prostrating for a long time. My father said: So it was raised. My head was among the people, and suddenly the boy was on the back of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I lowered my head and prostrated, so when he saluted The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The people said to him: O Messenger of God, I have prostrated in your prayer as often as I have ever done. You prostrate to it. Was that what was revealed to you? He said: No, but my son left me on a journey, so I thought I would hasten him until he relieved himself. (Ahmad 493, Hakim 626)"
"32856","(32856) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He carried Al-Hasan bin Ali to his freedmen and said: Oh God, I love him, so love him. His people said: So I said to Adi: Good. He said: Yes. (Bukhari 3749. Ahmed 283)"
"32857","(32857) Ja`far ibn Aoun narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Abi Muzard al-Madini informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Harry, he said: Two eyes saw and two ears heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was holding Hasan’s hand, or Hussein, while he was saying: It was a relief for Buqa’s eyes. He said: So the boy put his feet on the feet of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then He raises him and places him on his chest, then says: Open your mouth. He said: Then he kisses him, then says: Oh God, I love him. So he loved him. (Bukhari 249. Tabarani 2452)"
"32858","(32858) Muttalib bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, he said: Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn clashed, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Hussein, and Fatima said: As if he is more beloved to you? He said: No, but Gabriel says: He is Hussein. (Ibn Adi 1678)"
"32859","(32859) Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed on good deeds. And Al-Hussein, and he was carrying them to one of the Ansar’s gatherings, and they said: O Messenger of God, what a good mount you are. He said: And what a good way to ride. The two passengers (Tabarani 3999)"
"32860","(32860) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Ali Al-Amiri said that he went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to a meal for which they had invited him, and then Hussein was playing with The boys were on the road, so he presented himself before the people, then he extended his hand and the boy began to flee. He passed by here and here, and the Messenger of God made He, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made you laugh until the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took him and put one of his hands under him. his chin and the other under his nape, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed his head and placed his mouth on his mouth and he kissed him. He said: Hussein is from me and I am from Hussein. God loves whoever loves Hussein. Hussein is one of the tribes. \n(Tirmidhi 3775 and Ibn Hibban 807)"
"32861","(32861) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amer, who said: I was informed that the Prophet prayed God, peace and blessings be upon him, sent to Ja’far’s wife to send me to Banu Ja’far. He said: So he brought them, and he said: Oh God, Ja’far. He has presented to you the best reward, so leave behind his descendants as good as you have ever left behind any of your righteous servants (Ahmad 1690)"
"32862","(32862) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amir, who said: When Ja`far came from the land of Ethiopia, he met Omar bin Al-Khattab went to Asma bint Umays. He said to her: We preceded you in migration and we are better than you. She said: I will not return. Until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God, I met Omar and he claimed that he was better. From us and that they preceded us in emigrating, so he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Rather, you emigrated twice. He said Ismail: Saeed bin Abi Barda told me, he said: At that time she said to Omar: It is not like that, we were being driven to the land of Haters and enemies, while you were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He exhorted the ignorant of you and fed the hungry of you."
"32863","(32863) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, he said: Abu told us Misra is that when he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he killed Ja’far and Zaid, and Abdullah bin Rawahi mentioned. He commanded them and said: O God, forgive Zaid three times. O God, forgive Ja’far and Abdullah bin Rawahih."
"32864","(32864) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbah bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, On the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shown it in sleep, and he saw Ja’far, an angel with two wings. Covered in blood, Zaid was facing him on the bed, and Ibn Rawahhi was sitting with them as if they were turning away from him."
"32865","(32865) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubira ibn Yarim, and Hani’, On the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ja’far: My character and his character resemble you."
"32866","(32866) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted Ja`far and said to him: My character and yours resemble me."
"32867","(32867) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted Ja`far and said to him: My character and yours resemble me. (Bukhari 2699. Tirmidhi 3765)"
"32868","(32868) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: As for you, O Jafar, you resemble me and my character."
"32869","(32869) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, that Jafar bin Abi Talib was killed on the day he was brought to Balqa’. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, replace Jafar with the best of what you have left behind any of your servants. The righteous"
"32870","(32870) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came when Khaybar was conquered, and he was told: Ja`far has come from the Negus, so he said: I do not know which one, should I be happy with Ja`far's arrival, or? With the conquest of Khaybar, then he met him, joined him, and kissed him."
"32871","(32871) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Amir, that Ali married Asma, his son Umays, and he bragged about it. Her two sons, Muhammad ibn Ja`far and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, said: Each of them said: I am more honorable than you, and my father is better than you. Your father, so Ali said to her: Judge between them, and she said: I have never seen a young man among the Arabs better than Ja’far, and I have never seen Both of them were better than Abu Bakr. Ali said to her: You have not left anything for us, and if you had said anything other than this, I would have hated you. She said: : By God, there are three of whom you are the meanest of choice. (Ibn Saad 285)"
"32872","(32872) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, that Hamza used to fight on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with two swords and says: I am the lion of God and the lion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Hakim 192)"
"32873","(32873) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud and Hanzala ibn al-Rahib was killed. The one whom the angels purified on the Day of Uhud. (Bayhaqi 15)"
"32874","(32874) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: When Hamza bin Abd was injured Al-Muttalib and Musab bin Umair on the day of Uhud, when they saw the goodness they saw, said: I wish our brothers knew what we have befallen. It is good that they increase their desire. Then God said: I will inform you. Then God revealed: {And do not think that those who were killed in In the way of God are the dead; rather, they are alive with their Lord and are provided with.} According to His word, {And God will not waste the reward of the believers}."
"32875","(32875) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Abdul-Muttalib bin narrated to me Rabi`a bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib said that Al-Abbas entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was with him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever angers you? He said: O Messenger of God: What do we have with the Quraysh? When they meet, they meet with faces giving good tidings. And when they meet us, they meet us with something other than that. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became so angry that his face turned red and even There was a vein between his eyes, and when he was angry he would turn away, but when it was concealed from him, he said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, he will not enter. The heart of a man of faith until he loves you for the sake of God and His Messenger, then he said: O people, whoever harms Al-Abbas has harmed me. A man is like his father. (Tirmidhi 3785. Ahmed 207)"
"32876","(32876) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : Take care of Al-Abbas, for he is the remnant of my fathers, and a man’s paternal uncle is like his father."
"32877","(32877) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha Muslim bin Subaih, who said: Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, we will see the faces of a people and the events that I have inflicted on them. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They will not be harmed. So that they love you for the sake of God and for my kinship. I hope for the benefit of my intercession, and the Banu Abd al-Muttalib do not hope for it. (Tabarani 12228)"
"32878","(32878) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said to Al-Abbas: Come here, for you are a relative. (Ibn Saad 26)"
"32879","(32879) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Amer, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out, and with him was Abbas. Al-Abbas was of the opinion, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O uncle, if you see a mistake in me, correct it with me.”\n(Ibn Abi Asim 349)"
"32880","(32880) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to me, on the authority of Shuaib bin Yasar, on the authority of Ikrimah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Ibn Abbas, made him sit in his lap, wiped his head and prayed for him. With knowledge (Ibn Abi Asim 279)"
"32881","(32881) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Yasar, he said: A white bird came and entered Ibn Abbas was shrouded when he was brought in, and then he was not seen again. (Tabarani 10581, Hakim 544)"
"32882","(32882) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of a man called Abu Kulthum, who said: I heard Ibn al-Hanafiyyah saying at Ibn Abbas’s funeral: Today the lord of knowledge died."
"32883","(32883) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: If Ibn Abbas had caught up with you Our teeth have never been seen by any man."
"32884","(32884) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: Yes, the interpreter of the Qur’an, Ibn Abbas"
"32885","(32885) Abdullah bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, that Kurayb told him On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for me to increase my God knows and understands. (Ahmed 330)"
"32886","(32886) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, who said: Al-Abbas entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him but did not see anyone with him, so his son said to him: I saw a man with him. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, Ibn Your uncle said that he saw a man with you, and Abdullah said: Yes, by the One who sent down the Book to you. He said: That is Gabriel.\n(Taalisi 2708, Ahmed 294)"
"32887","(32887) Suleiman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: I was in the house of Maimunah Ibn Al-Harith, and I prayed for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He prepared it, and he said: Who put this on? And Maimoonah said: Abdullah, and he said: Oh God, make him understand the religion and teach him. Interpretation (Ahmed 238)"
"32888","(32888) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar asked the companions of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about something. He said: So he asked me and I told him. He said: Are you too afraid to bring something like what he brought? This is the boy whose head is not in order."
"32889","(32889) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazeed, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Your permission is to lift the veil, and You hear my darkness until it exhausts you. (Muslim 1708. Ibn Majah 139)"
"32890","(32890) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik Ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, He said: Abdullah used to cover the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he washed himself, and wake him up when he slept, and walk with him on earth. A monster (Ibn Saad 153)"
"32891","(32891) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Amiri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad Al-Kinani, he said: Ibn Masoud was the owner of the wasad and the siwak. (Ibn Saad 153)"
"32892","(32892) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah used to dress the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He handed over his sandals and walked in front of him. (Ibn Saad 153)"
"32893","(32893) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If I had left without consulting him, I would have appointed Ibn Umm Abd as my successor. (Tirmidhi 3809. Ahmad 76)"
"32894","(32894) Abu Asama told us, he said: Zaidah told me, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zirr, he said: He made the people They laugh at what the wind does to Abdullah. It is enough for him. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is heavier in the sight of God. On the Day of Resurrection, it will be a weighing scale from one. (Abu Dawud 355. Ahmad 320)"
"32895","(32895) Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Badr, on the authority of Tamim ibn Huthlam, he said: I sat with the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr and Omar, and I did not see anyone who increased in this world, nor I desire the Hereafter, and I do not like to be in the slaughterhouse on the Day of Resurrection than you, O Abdullah bin Masoud."
"32896","(32896) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I am satisfied for my nation as Ibn Umm Abd was satisfied for it. (Hakim 318. Tabarani 8458)"
"32897","(32897) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Umm Musa, she said: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded May God bless him and grant him peace. He told Ibn Masoud to climb a tree and bring him some of it, so his companions looked at his tents. And they laughed at her, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What makes you laugh at Abdullah’s man in the scales? Heavier than anyone.\n(Ahmad 114; Abu Ali 591)"
"32898","(32898) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of His father, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said, “You have seen me as the sixth person on the surface of the earth to be a Muslim other than us.”\n(Ibn Hibban 62. Hakim 313)"
"32899","(32899) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever is pleased to read the Qur’an in a clear manner as it was revealed, let him recite it in the same manner as Ibn Umm Abd."
"32900","(32900) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The preserved among the companions of Muhammad knew May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Ibn Masoud is the closest to God and his companion on the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmed 395)"
"32901","(32901) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Khalid, he said: I came to Omar and he preferred The people of the Levant are ahead of us regarding the reward, so we said to him, and he said: O people of Kufa, are you afraid that I have favored the people of the Levant? The reward is up to you because of their hardship. I preferred you to Ibn Umm Abd."
"32902","(32902) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Abdullah came one day, and Umar He was sitting, and he said: He is a scholar, full of jurisprudence."
"32903","(32903) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib, who said: The letter of Umar was read to us: As for what follows, I have sent to you Ammar ibn Yasir as an emir, and Abdullah ibn Masoud as a teacher and a minister, and they are both among the nobles from Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I preferred you to Ibn Umm Abd over myself."
"32904","(32904) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, they said: Tell us on the authority of Abdullah. He said: He taught the Qur’an and the Sunnah, and that is sufficient knowledge."
"32905","(32905) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Salih ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah (They said to those who were given knowledge, “What did he say above?”) He is Abdullah bin Masoud."
"32906","(32906) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: Abdullah was likened to By the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his guidance, guidance, and blessings."
"32907","(32907) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Hubba bin Juwayn, he said: We were sitting with Ali and he reminded us. Some of Abdullah’s words, and the people praised him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, we have never seen a man with better morals, nor more compassionate. He was more learned, more pious, and had better companions than Ibn Masoud. Then Ali said: I implore you, by God, that it is truthfulness from your hearts. They said: Yes, he said: Oh God, I bear witness to you that I say the same as what they said, and better."
"32908","(32908) Ali told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: I heard Abu Musa He says: For a gathering in which I used to sit, Abdullah is more trustworthy than the work of his Sunnah."
"32909","(32909) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani ibn Hani, on the authority of Ali, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Ammar came to ask for permission, and he said: Give him permission to welcome the perfumed perfume.\n(Ibn Hibban 7075 and Ahmad 130)"
"32910","(32910) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Ammar was filled with faith until his days."
"32911","(32911) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Laila Al-Kindi, he said: Khabbab came To Omar, he said: Bring him closer, for no one is more deserving of this gathering than you except Ammar. So Khabab made marks on his back of what he had tortured him with. The polytheists."
"32912","(32912) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Ibn Sumayyah: He is not given a choice between two things except that he chooses the more guided of them. (Ahmad 389. Hakim 388)"
"32913","(32913) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: What is the matter with them and with Ammar? He calls them to Paradise and they call him to Hell. And so is the habit of The wretched and immoral people.\n(Ahmed 1598)"
"32914","(32914) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abi Al-Bakhtari, he said: He was asked Ali, on the authority of Ammar, said: A believer forgets, and if you remind him, he remembers, and faith has entered his hearing and sight, and he remembers what God willing, from his body."
"32915","(32915) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Ali, he said They said to him: Tell us about the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Tell us about Ammar. He said: A believer has forgotten, even if I reminded him of it."
"32916","(32916) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Hudhayl, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought. He greeted him, and it was said to him: A mountain fell on him and he died. He said: Ammar did not die. (Ibn Saad 254, Ahmed 1597)"
"32917","(32917) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Abi Zayed narrated to us, on the authority of the muezzin, that he heard Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ammar was filled with faith to the point of mishash, and he was among those who were forbidden to the Fire. (Ibn Asakir 43)"
"32918","(32918) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, on the authority of Salma ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Alqamah. On the authority of Khalid bin Al-Walid, he said: There was a conversation between me and Ammar, and Ammar went off to complain about me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was complaining about me, and Ammar did not add anything to him except harshness. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent, and Ammar cried and said: O Messenger of God, won’t you hear him? He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his voice. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever is hostile to Ammar, God will be hostile to him, and whoever hates Ammar will be hated by God. He said: So I went out. There was nothing I hated more than Ammar’s anger, so I met him and was pleased with him. (Ahmad 891 Hakim 390)"
"32919","(32919) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: The first to build A mosque in which Ammar bin Yasir prays. (Ibn Abi Asim 117)"
"32920","(32920) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik: {Except he who is forced while his heart is at ease with faith} He said: She stayed in Ammar. (Ibn Jarir 182)"
"32921","(32921) Uthman bin Ali told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani bin Hani, he said: He asked for permission. Ammar Ali Ali, and he said: Welcome to the perfumed and perfumed one. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Ammar is filled with faith. NS"
"32922","(32922) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hikam: (Except he who is forced while his heart is at peace with faith) he said. : It was revealed in Ammar."
"32923","(32923) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A people with softer hearts will come to you. He said: Then the Ash’arites came and among them is Abu Musa. He said: They began to tremble. And they say: Tomorrow we will meet the beloved Muhammad and his party. (Ahmed 105)"
"32924","(32924) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Mughul, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Al-Ash’ari was given a psalm from the psalms of the family of David."
"32925","(32925) It was narrated on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Al-Ash’ari was given a flute from the psalms of the family of David."
"32926","(32926) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: Abu Musa was given a psalm from the psalms of the family of David."
"32927","(32927) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Iyad al-Ash’ari, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: To Abu Musa: They are the people of this, meaning in his saying: {God will surely bring a people whom He will love and who will love Him} The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They are the people of this. (Ibn Saad 1071 Hakim 313)"
"32928","(32928) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays, who said: There was a dispute between Khalid ibn al-Walid and a man from among the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was interlocutor, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: What is the matter with you and any of the swords of God? Ask him. May God protect the unbelievers. (Ibn Saad 395 and Ahmed 1479)"
"32929","(32929) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: I landed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the backs of Harshi, and his stomach was cut off, so I took him to him. My sandals, but he refused to accept them and sat in the shade of a tree to mend his sandals. He said to me: Look who you see. I said: This is so-and-so, son of so-and-so. He said: Wretched is the servant of God so-and-so, then he said to me: Look at whom you see. I said, This is so-and-so. He said: What a good servant of God is so-and-so, and what he said To him: What a wonderful servant of God, Khalid bin Al-Walid. (Tirmidhi 3846)"
"32930","(32930) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: Umar sent Abu Ubaidah Ali the Levant and removed Khaled bin Al-Walid, and he said: Khaled bin Al-Walid: The trustee of this nation has been sent to you, Abu Ubaidah, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Khaled is one of the swords of God, and what a good boy of the clan. (Ahmed 90)"
"32931","(32931) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Uthman Abi Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad. Al-Dili, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr say: I heard the Messenger of God say: The dust has not diminished, nor has the green shade increased from a man. More truthful than Abu Dharr. (Tirmidhi 3801 and Ahmad 163)"
"32932","(32932) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Bilal bin Abi Al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: The green ones have not shaded, nor have the dusty ones diminished. His speech is more truthful than that of Abu Dharr. (Ahmad 442, Ibn Saad 228)"
"32933","(32933) Yazid told us, on the authority of Abu Umayyah ibn Ali al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The green ones have not given shade, nor have the dust become fewer in number. He is more truthful than Abu Dharr, and whoever would be pleased to see the humility of Jesus, son of Mary, should look at Abu Dharr. (Ibn Saad 228)"
"32934","(32934) Yazid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, he said: Abu Dharr said: I The closest of you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will sit on the Day of Resurrection. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever leaves this world like what I left him in it, and by God, there is not one of you who has not clung to it. With something else.\n(Ahmad 1650, Ibn Saad 228)"
"32935","(32935) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Only a part of me made her wean, so whoever makes her angry, she makes me angry."
"32936","(32936) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I told Fatima The son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I saw you when you fell upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his illness. So I cried, then I leaned on him a second time and she laughed, saying: I leaned on him and he told me that he was dead. So I cried, then I cried for him the second time, and he told me that I was the first of his family to join him, and that he was the master of women. The people of Paradise except Maryam, daughter of Imran, so I laughed.\n(Bukhari 3423. Muslim 99)"
"32937","(32937) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Misra al-Nahdi, on the authority of al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came out, so I followed him, and he said: A king presented to me He asked his Lord for permission to greet me and tell me that Fatima is the master of the wives of the people of Paradise."
"32938","(32938) Shazan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He used to pass by Fatima’s house for six months, and when he went out at dawn, he would say: Prayer, O people. The House {Allah only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you with a thorough purification}"
"32939","(32939) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Fatima is the master of the women of the worlds after Mary, the son of Imran, Asiya, the wife of Pharaoh, and Khadija, his son. Khuwailid.\n(Tirmidhi 3878, Nasa’i 8355)"
"32940","(32940) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ali, the daughter of Abi Jahl, proposed to her uncle Al-Harith. Ibn Hisham, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, consulted about it and said: You will ask me about what is sufficient for it. Ali said: It is enough for you to ask me. I know what they calculated, but do you command me to do so? He said: No, I will give you a portion of my fat, and I do not like for you to be upset. So Ali said: I will not do anything that you dislike. (Hakim 158)"
"32941","(32941) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Aisha, my wife in Paradise. (Ibn Saad 66)"
"32942","(32942) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Many of the men were perfect, but none of the women were perfect except Asiya, Pharaoh’s wife, and Miriam his son. Imran, and the superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over food. (Muslim 1886. Tirmidhi 1834)"
"32943","(32943) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Aisha prefers women just as porridge prefers other foods."
"32944","(32944) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Dahhak, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Zayd bin Jad`an, he said: We were told that Abdullah bin Safwan and another with him came to Aisha, Aisha said: Oh so-and-so, have you heard the hadith of Hafsiya? He said: Yes, O Mother of the Believers. Then Abdullah bin Safwan said to her: And what is that, O Mother of the Believers? She said: During the course of nine, there was not among any of the people except what God gave Mary, the son of Imran. By God, I am not saying this because I am proud of my companions. Abdullah bin Safwan said: And what is that, O Mother of the Believers? She said: The king descended in my image, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me for seven years, and I was given to him as a gift for nine. For years, he married me to a virgin whom no one shared with him, and the revelation came to him, and I and him were in one blanket. And I was one of the most beloved people to him, and verses were revealed from the Qur’an that almost destroyed the nation there, and I saw Gabriel but he did not None of his wives saw him except me, and he was detained in my house, and no one was there except the king and me.\n(Bukhari 1096. Hakim 10)"
"32945","(32945) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Aisha informed me, she said: Between us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in the house when a man on a horse entered the chamber over us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose up to him. May God bless him and grant him peace: Then he placed his hand on the horse’s handle and began to speak to it. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned. And he greeted me, so I said: O Messenger of God, who is this you were conversing with? He said: Did you see anyone? She said: I said: Yes, I saw A man riding a horse. He said: To whom she compared it. She said: To the sacrifice of Al-Kalbiyyah. He said: That is Gabriel. He said: You have seen goodness. She said: Then she stayed for as long as God wished to stay, and Gabriel and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the chamber, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the chamber. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Aisha, I said: May God bless you and grant you peace, O Messenger of God. He said: This is Gabriel. He commanded me to convey his greetings to you. She said: I said: Return to him with his greetings, may God’s mercy and blessings be upon him. May God reward you from An intruder is the best repellant of intruders. She said: And the revelation was descending upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he and I. In one quilt. (Tabarani 95. Hamidi 277)"
"32946","(32946) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Mus’ab bin Ishaq bin Talha narrated to me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I showed Aisha in Paradise, to make my death easier for me, as if I were seeing her sufficiency. (Ibn Saad 65)"
"32947","(32947) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over all other foods.\n(Bukhari 5419. Tirmidhi 3887)"
"32948","(32948) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died in my house and between my dawn and our dawn hours. (Bukhari 3100, Ahmed 48)"
"32949","(32949) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il that Ali sent Ammar and Al-Hasan to mobilize The people said: Then a man stood up and fell on Aisha, and Ammar said: She is the wife of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this world. And the Hereafter, but God tested us with it to know which one we will obey, or which one. (Bukhari 3772, Ahmed 265)"
"32950","(32950) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ammar, he said: Aisha The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is in Paradise."
"32951","(32951) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Musa al-Janni narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, he said: Roman’s mother came Umm Aisha and Abu Bakr went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, pray to God for Aisha. He made a supplication that we would hear, and then he said: O God, grant Aisha, the son of Abu Bakr, a clear and obligatory forgiveness. And inwardly. (Hakim 12)"
"32952","(32952) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, who said: Abu Salma bin Abd al-Rahman narrated to us that Aisha told her that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Gabriel is reciting peace be upon you. Aisha said: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon him."
"32953","(32953) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: I heard him say: Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This Khadija has come to you, she has a vessel in it. Adam, or food, or drink, so if she comes to you, read peace upon her from her Lord and give her good tidings of a home in Paradise from Qasab does not contain any noise or accusative case. (Bukhari 3820, Muslim 1887)"
"32954","(32954) Waki’ and Ya’li narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave good tidings to Khadija of a house in Paradise made of reeds in which there will be no noise or stress.\n(Muslim 1888 and Bukhari 1792)"
"32955","(32955) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, on the authority of Ali, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The best of her wives is Maryam, his sons Imran and the best. Her wives are Khadija. (Bukhari 3432. Muslim 69)"
"32956","(32956) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Give good news to Khadija of a dwelling in Paradise of reeds without noise. Nor is it in the accusative case?"
"32957","(32957) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are four: Khadija, the son of Khuwalid, and Fatima, the son of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace and peace. Pharaoh's wife and Maryam, the son of Imran. (Tirmidhi 3878 and Ahmad 1338)"
"32958","(32958) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting with Gabriel, when Khadija came, and Gabriel said: O Messenger of God, this is Khadija, so confer upon her the blessings and blessings of God Almighty."
"32959","(32959) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Al-Thaqafi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Mu’adh will be in the hands of the scholars on the Day of Resurrection. Recitation. (Tabarani 41)"
"32960","(32960) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Moaz is in the hands of the scholars on the Day of Resurrection."
"32961","(32961) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he greeted: Every mother has a trustworthy person, and our trustworthy mother is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. (Muslim 1881, Abu Ali 2800)"
"32962","(32962) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no My companions are none, unless, if you wish, you can adopt some of his character over him other than Abu Ubaidah."
"32963","(32963) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria ibn Abi Zaydah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salah ibn Zafar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the bishop of Najran, Al-Aqib, and Al-Sayyid, and said: Send with us an honest man. Truly, Amen. Then the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked to her and said: Get up, O Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.\n(Bukhari 37451 Muslim 1882)"
"32964","(32964) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salah, on the authority of Hudhaifa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Muslim 1882. Tirmidhi 3796)"
"32965","(32965) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: Who would be appointed as successor if he were Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah."
"32966","(32966) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: What a wonderful man, Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah."
"32967","(32967) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Atiyya, who said: A man called Ubad bin al-Samit came. He said: O Messenger of God, I have allies among the Jews, many of whom are present in their victory, and I disavow before God and His Messenger any And the Jews, so God revealed concerning His servants: {Indeed, your guardian is God and His Messenger and those who believe} the verses to his saying: {Indeed, they are a people who do not understand}"
"32968","(32968) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: When Ali walked to Siffin He appointed Abu Masoud as his successor over the people. He said: When he came to Ali, he said to him: You are the one who said, “What I heard about you, O Farrukh, you are an old man.” Your mind has gone. He said: My mind has gone, and the jinn has become certain for you in God and His Messenger. You know that."
"32969","(32969) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: Aisha said: It should not be No one should hate his name after what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He who loves God and His Messenger. Let him love Asama. (Ahmed 156)"
"32970","(32970) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qays, that when Usama bin Zaid was killed, he rose up between The hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and tears came from the eyes of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he came the next day and took his place. Yesterday, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: I will meet from you today what I have encountered from you yesterday. (Ahmed 1530)"
"32971","(32971) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, had begun a mission before his death and appointed Asama bin Zayd over them, and at that mission included Abu Bakr and Omar. He said: It was as if some of the people were challenging this because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had ordered Asama over them, so the Messenger of God stood up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he addressed the people and said: Some of you have challenged me regarding the appointment of your names, but they have only attacked me. The appointment of Asama just as they challenged the appointment of his father, and I swear to God that he was a creation for the Emirate, even if he was for whomever he loved. people to me, and his son is the most beloved of people to me after him, and I hope that he will be among your good deeds, so treat him well.\n(Bukhari 3730, Muslim 1884)"
"32972","(32972) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Al-Bayhi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Usama stumbled upon the threshold of the door. Then his face swelled, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Remove the filth from him, so I made him filthy and he began to suck the blood. And He glorifies him, on his face, and says: If Osama had been a maid, I would have clothed and adorn him until I paid for him. (Ibn Majah 1976. Ibn Saad 61)"
"32973","(32973) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Wael bin Dawud, who said: I heard Al-Bayhi narrating that Aisha used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never sent Zayd bin Haritha with an army without commanding him over them, even if he were still alive. He appointed him as his successor. (Ahmed 227)"
"32974","(32974) Affan narrated to us, Wahib narrated to us, he said: Musa bin Uqba narrated to us, he said: Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar narrated to me. That Abdullah bin Omar said: We did not call upon anyone except Zayd bin Muhammad until the Qur’an was revealed: {Call them by their fathers. He is more equitable when Allah}"
"32975","(32975) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He greeted Zaid: As for you, O Zaid, you are our brother and our master."
"32976","(32976) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani bin Hani, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"32977","(32977) Abu Usama told us, he said: Khalid bin Abi Karimah told me, on the authority of Sa`id that Al-Sadoosi walked, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ubayy bin Ka’b: I have been commanded to recite the Qur’an to you. He said: And my Lord reminded me. He said: Yes. He said: He did not teach me a verse. So I repeated it to him a second time. (Bukhari 3809. Muslim 550)"
"32978","(32978) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ubayy, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was commanded to recite the Qur’an to you. He said: I said: O Messenger of God: And I mentioned then? He said: Yes, my father said: By the grace and mercy of God, let them rejoice in its recitation. My father: let them rejoice."
"32979","(32979) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: The throne was shaken by the death of Saad bin Muadh. (Bukhari 3803, Muslim 1915)"
"32980","(32980) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Usayd Bin Hudair, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The throne shook at the death of Saad bin Muadh.\n(Tabarani 553, Ibn Abi Asim 1927)"
"32981","(32981) Hudhu narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The throne was shaken by the death of Saad bin Muadh. (Ahmad 23. Abu Ali 1255)"
"32982","(32982) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The throne shook for the love of meeting Sa’d. He said: Rather, he means the bed. He said: Its sticks rotted. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered his grave and was shut up. He came out. It was said: O Messenger of God, what has imprisoned you? He said: Saad was held tightly together in the grave, so I prayed to God to reveal him.\n(Nasa’i 2182 and Hakim 206)"
"32983","(32983) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man who narrated to him, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: When he died Saad bin Muadh. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The throne shook for the spirit of Saad bin Muadh. (Ibn Saad 434)"
"32984","(32984) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of A woman from the Ansar who was told the names of Ibn Zayd said: When he was brought out for the funeral of Saad bin Muadh, his mother cried out. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Umm Saad: Will your tears not stop and your sadness go away, for your son was the first to laugh? May the Throne shake for Him. (Ahmad 456. Tabarani 467)"
"32985","(32985) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, and he said: Waqid bin Amr bin Saad bin Muadh told us, he said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik when he came to Medina with my nephew, and I greeted him. He said: Who are you? So I said: I am Waqid bin Amr bin Saad bin Muadh. He said: Then he cried and cried more, then he said: You are like Saad. Sa'd was one of the greatest and most eloquent people, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a mission to Akkadir Doumah. With a garment of brocade woven with gold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wore it and the people began to touch it. With their hands, he said: Do you marvel at this? They said: O Messenger of God, we have not seen you better than you today. The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Saad’s handkerchiefs in Paradise are better than what you see. (Ahmad 121. Tirmidhi 1723)"
"32986","(32986) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, who said: It was given to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. A garment of silk, and they began to marvel at its softness. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For handkerchiefs. Saad in Paradise is softer than this. (Bukhari 6440 and Ibn Majah 157)"
"32987","(32987) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To Saad, who was confident in himself: May God reward you better than the leader of a people, for God has fulfilled what He promised him, and He is absolutely truthful. He promised you"
"32988","(32988) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Shurahbil, he said: When Saad ibn Muadh was injured With the shooting on the day of the ditch, he made his blood flow on the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Abu Bakr came and started saying: And his appearance stopped, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Abu Bakr, then Omar came and said: We belong to God and to Him. We will return. (Ahmed 1502)"
"32989","(32989) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, who said: Abu Darda’ was among those who were given knowledge."
"32990","(32990) Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, Al-A’mash said: I see him, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I came to him. Omar made a garment, so he started dividing it among the people, and a new Najrani garment passed by him, so he placed it under his thigh until he passed by My name is, so I said: Clothe her, and he said: Clothe her, by God, a man better than you and whose father is better than your father. So he called Abdullah. Bin Hanzalah bin Al-Rahib, so he clothed it."
"32991","(32991) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, saying: I heard Amir saying: He resembled the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted three people from his nation, saying: Dihiya al-Kalbi resembles Gabriel, and Urwah ibn Masoud al-Thaqafi. He resembles Jesus, son of Mary, and Abdul-Uzza resembles the Antichrist. (Ibn Saad 250)"
"32992","(32992) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicated to Abdullah bin Rawahih: Oh God, increase his obedience to your obedience. And he obeyed your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bayhaqi 257)"
"32993","(32993) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abdullah: Ibn Rawahiha: Will you not move the passengers for us? Abdullah said: You have neglected what I said. Omar Ibn al-Khattab said: Listen and obey, so he descended. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drives and says:\nOh God, had it not been for you, we would not have followed the right path, nor given charity, nor prayed.\nSo send down a knife upon us and make our feet firm if we meet us.\nIndeed, those who disbelieve have transgressed against us.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, have mercy on him, and Omar said: It is obligatory."
"32994","(32994) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, conveyed what Salman said By Abu Darda’: Your family has a right over you and your sight has a right over you. He said: So he said: Salman has become bereaved of his mother. He has expanded his knowledge. (Ibn Saad 84)"
"32995","(32995) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Salman is a Persian racer."
"32996","(32996) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, he said: They said to Ali: Tell us about Salman. He said: He has attained the first knowledge and the other knowledge. He is a sea whose bottom cannot be removed. He is one of us, Ahl al-Bayt. (Ruler 598)"
"32997","(32997) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: You have seen us and we are present. And there is no one among us who has more control over himself than Abdullah bin Omar."
"32998","(32998) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, who said: None of us has reached the world without having He favored it, or she favored it, except Abdullah bin Omar."
"32999","(32999) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zayed narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The first to demonstrate their Islam were seven people: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Ammar and his mother named Samaya. And Sahib, Bilal, and Al-Miqdad. As for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, God protected him from his uncle Abu Talib. Abu Bakr, so God protected him from his people, and as for the rest of them, the polytheists took them and dressed them in iron armor. And they fasted in the sun, and there was not one of them who did not give them what they wanted, except for Bilal, for he was disgraced in his soul. And God bequeathed to his people, so they took him and gave him to his children, and they made him go around the highways of Mecca, and he said: One Sunday (Hakim 284. Ibn Hibban 7083)"
"33000","(33000) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first to demonstrate Islam were seven people: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr, Bilal, Khabbab, Sahib, and Ammar, and she was named Umm Ammar. He said: As for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, but his uncle prevented him, and as for Abu Bakr, his people prevented him, and they took the others and dressed them in iron armor, then They fasted in the sun until the effort of every one of them reached its peak, so they gave them everything they asked for, and every man came to him. Among them were his people, with water pouring into them, and they threw them into them, then they were carried by their sides, except for Bilal, and they were placed around his neck. A rope, then they ordered their boys to pull it together between the woods of Mecca, and he made the saying: Uhud Uhud. (Ahmed 282)"
"33001","(33001) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated to me, on the authority of His father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard a rattle in front of me, so I said, Who is this? They said: Bilal, So he told him, he said: Because you preceded me to Paradise, he said: O Messenger of God, I did not speak except that I performed ablution, and I did not perform ablution except that I saw Indeed, Allah has two rak'ahs upon me, which I pray, and he said: By this. (Ibn Hibban 7087 and Ibn Khuzaymah 1209)"
"33002","(33002) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Bakr bought Bilal for five uqiqs, then He freed him, he said: Then Bilal said to him: O Abu Bakr, if you only freed me to take me as a keeper, then take me as a keeper. You only freed me for the sake of God, so he called me to work for God. He said: Then Abu Bakr cried, then he said: Rather, I freed you for the sake of God. (Bukhari 3755)"
"33003","(33003) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Majishun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mandir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Omar said: Abu Bakr is our master and he freed our master, meaning Bilal."
"33004","(33004) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: He narrated to us. Bilal was Abu Bakr’s treasurer and the Prophet’s muezzin, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"33005","(33005) Abu Asama told us, he said: I heard Hisham, he said: Al-Hasan told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Bilal, a former Abyssinian."
"33006","(33006) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir bin Abd. God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has not blocked me since I converted to Islam, and he has never seen me without smiling.\n(Muslim 1925. Tabarani 1221)"
"33007","(33007) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shibl bin Awf, on the authority of Jarir, he said: When I approached Medina, I unbuttoned my mount, then removed my cloak and put on my robe. He said: So I entered with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was giving a sermon. I greeted the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the people stared at me, so I said to my companion: O Abdullah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned something about my matter. He said: Yes, he reminded you of the best of remembrance, and he said: While the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was delivering a sermon, he presented his sermon to him and said: Someone will enter upon you. This dawn, or from this door, from the best of those on whose face the anointing of an angel. Jarir said: So I thanked God for what he had done. Ablaniya. (Nasa’i 8304. Ahmad 359)"
"33008","(33008) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He said, “Won’t you relieve me of Dhul-Khalasa, a house that Khath’am had in the pre-Islamic era and it was called Al-Ka’bah Al-Yamaniyya?” He said. I said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who is not stable on horses. He said: Then he rubbed his chest and said: O God, make him a guide. Until she found her cold. (Muslim 1926. Ahmad 360)"
"33009","(33009) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He enters Paradise through the intercession of a man from my nation, such as Rabi’i and Mudar. He said: Hawshab narrated to me: He said: So we said to Al-Hasan: Did he name it for you? He said: Yes, Uwais Al-Qarni. (Tirmidhi 2438 and Ahmad 469)"
"33010","(33010) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariyi, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Asir bin Jabir, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: A man called Uwais will come to you. There was whiteness on it, so he prayed to God for it, and God took it away, so whoever of you meets it and passes it over, let him ask forgiveness for it. He said: Then Omar met him and said: Ask forgiveness for me, so he asked forgiveness for him. (Muslim 1968. Ahmad 38)"
"33011","(33011) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’i bin Rafi’ al-Ansari. An angel came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How were the people of Badr among you? He said: The best of people. The Angel: And likewise one of the angels who witnesses a full moon. (Bukhari 3992)"
"33012","(33012) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’ who informed him, On the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You don’t know, perhaps God has seen the people of Badr, so he said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you. (Bukhari 3007, Muslim 1941)"
"33013","(33013) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, Blessed and Most High, looked at the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you. (Abu Dawud 4422 and Ahmed 296)"
"33014","(33014) Shababi bin Suwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir that Abd Hatib bin Abi Rather, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to complain to a woodcutter, and he said: O Messenger of God, let a woodcutter enter Hell. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: She lied, he does not enter it. He witnessed Badr and Al-Hudaybiya."
"33015","(33015) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {You were the best of people raised among people} He said: Those who migrated with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina."
"33016","(33016) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, saw women and boys from the Ansar coming from a wedding, and he said: Oh God, you are among the most beloved people to me. \n(Bukhari 37851 Muslim 1948)"
"33017","(33017) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Shurahbil, On the authority of Qais bin Saad bin Ubadah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: O God, bless the Ansar and my descendants. The Ansar and his descendants, the descendants of the Ansar. (Tabarani 890)"
"33018","(33018) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Labid, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If people walked through a valley and a path, and you walked through a valley And by people I would have followed your valley and your people. You are a symbol and the people a cover. Had it not been for the emigration, I would have been one of the Ansar. Then He raised his hands so that I could see the whites of his armpits under his shoulders, and he said: O God, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar. And to the sons of the Ansar. (Abu Ali 1087)"
"33019","(33019) Shababhi told us, he said: Shu’babi told us, he said: Adi bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No one loves the Ansar except a believer, and no one hates them except a hypocrite, and whoever loves them God loves you, and whoever hates you, God hates you. (Bukhari 3783. Muslim 85)"
"33020","(33020) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the people had taken a valley, or a path, and the Ansar had taken a valley, or a path I would have taken the valley of the Ansar, or their people, and had it not been for the migration, I would have been one of the Ansar. (Dharmi 2514)"
"33021","(33021) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who loves the Ansar; Whoever God loves, and whoever hates the Ansar; God hates him\n(Ahmad 501, Abu Ali 7329)"
"33022","(33022) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Saad bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, on the authority of Hamza bin Abi Asaid Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Ziyad, one of the people of Badr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever loves God loves the Ansar until he meets them, and whoever hates the Ansar, God will hate him when he meets him. (Ahmad 221. Tabarani 3357)"
"33023","(33023) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us that Saad bin Ibrahim told him, about Al-Hakam bin Mina, on the authority of Yazid bin Jariyah, that he was sitting with a group of the Ansar, and Mu’awiyah passed by them. So he asked them about their hadith, and they said: We were talking about a hadith from the Ansar, so Muawiyah said: Shall I not add a hadith to you? I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever loves the Ansar, God will love him, and whoever hates the Ansar, God will hate him. (Ahmad 961 Abu Ali 7330)"
"33024","(33024) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Indeed, my defect is the one to which my household has taken refuge, and the throne of the Ansar, so pardon their transgressor. And accept from their doers of good. \n(Tirmidhi 3904, Ahmad 89)"
"33025","(33025) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of Al-Bara’ that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said : Accept from their doers of good, and ignore their wrongdoers, meaning the Ansar."
"33026","(33026) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Shamila, he said: A man narrated to me, On the authority of Sa’id al-Sarraf - or he is on the authority of Sa’id al-Sarraf - on the authority of Ishaq bin Sa’d bin Ubadah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, this living Ansar is a test, their love is faith, and their hatred is hypocrisy. (Ahmed 7)"
"33027","(33027) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel. On the authority of Al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Had it not been for the Hijra I would have been one of the Ansar, and if people had taken a valley or a path, I would have walked with the Ansar. (Tirmidhi 3899. Ahmad 137)"
"33028","(33028) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: People are a cover and the Ansar are a symbol. The Ansar are my thorns and my blemishes, and had it not been for the migration, I would have been one of the Ansar.\n(Nasa’i 8326. Ahmed 201)"
"33029","(33029) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Anas, he said: He wrote Zaid bin Arqam went to Anas to offer his condolences to his son and his family who were injured on the day of the heat, so he wrote in his letter: And I am bringing you good tidings from God. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: O God, forgive the Ansar and their sons. The Ansar, for the sons of the Ansar’s sons, for the women of the Ansar, for the women of the Ansar’s sons, and for the wives of the sons of the Ansar’s sons. (Ibn Hibban 7281 and Ahmad 374)"
"33030","(33030) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he mentioned the Ansar, peace be upon him, he said: The most pardoned and patient. (Tirmidhi 3903, Ahmed 150)"
"33031","(33031) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada that Qatadah bin Al-Nu’man fell. His eye was on his cheek on the day of Uhud, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned it, and it was the best of his eyes and the one of them.\n(Ibn Saad 453; Abu Ali 1546)"
"33032","(33032) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned the hand of Khubayb bin Yasaf was struck on the day of Badr on the man’s rope, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought her back, and nothing was visible of her except what was like a line. (Bayhaqi 1788, Ahmad 454)"
"33033","(33033) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So he began to mention the Quraysh and what they had gathered, and he began to threaten them with them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: And he greeted: The Banu Qayla refuse to do that to you. They are a people whose punishment is extreme."
"33034","(33034) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, he said: I heard Abu Hamza, he said: The Ansar said: O Messenger God, every prophet has followers, and we have followed you, so pray to God to make our followers among us. So he prayed for them to make Follow them from among them.\n He said: I conveyed that to Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, and he said: Zaid claimed that. (Bukhari 3788, Hakim 85)"
"33035","(33035) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: His people informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Asad ibn Hudhir. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar: After me you will see a trace of me. They said: So what do you command us? He said: Be patient. Until you meet me at the basin."
"33036","(33036) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had it not been for the Hijra, I would have been one of the Ansar, even if the people had followed suit. A valley, or a path. I would have taken the valley of the Ansar and their people. The Ansar are a symbol and the people are a covering, and you will meet them after me. So be patient until you meet me at the Fountain."
"33037","(33037) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Jahin, Muzain, Aslam, and Ghafar. A loyalist of God and His Messenger, they have no other master but Him. (Bukhari 3504, Muslim 1954)"
"33038","(33038) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out for a cold lunch. The Muhajireen and Ansar were digging the trench, and when he looked at them, he said:\n Indeed, the life of the Hereafter is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajir.\n They answered him: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad for jihad as long as we remain alive. (Nasa’i 8333)"
"33039","(33039) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Ansar does not hate a man who believes in God and the Last Day."
"33040","(33040) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The Ansar is not hated by a man who believes in God and the Last Day. (Muslim 86. Ahmad 34)"
"33041","(33041) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Rabah, he said: We sent delegations of Muawiyah, and Abu Hurairah was among us, and that was in Ramadan, so he said: Shall I not inform you of a hadith? From your hadith, O community of Ansar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O community of Ansar, they said: Here you go. O Messenger of God, he said: You said: As for the man, his desire for his family and compassion for his family overtook him. He said: We said that. O Messenger of God, he said: What is my name then? He said: No, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. I emigrated to you. My life will be your life and my death will be Your death. He said: Then they came to him weeping and saying: By God, O Messenger of God, we did not say what we said except in spite of God. And His Messenger, he said: Indeed, Allah and His Messenger believe you and excuse you. (Muslim 1405. Ibn Hibban 4760)"
"33042","(33042) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, He said: I was informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Were it not for the migration, I would have been one of the Ansar."
"33043","(33043) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Harun Al-Ansari, who said: Muadh bin Rifa’i bin Rafi’ narrated to me, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, forgive the Ansar and his descendants. The Ansar and his descendants. Their descendants, their friends, and their neighbors. (Musnad 4137. Ibn Hibban 7283)"
"33044","(33044) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Ibn Al-Ghasil narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: One day the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sat on the pulpit, wearing a veil, with a bandana around his head. Dasmaa, he said: So he thanked God and praised Him, then he said: O people, you are multiplying, and the supporters are few and far between. Like salt in food, so whoever takes charge of any of their affairs, let it accept it from their doers of good, and let him turn away from their wrongdoers.\n(Bukhari 927, Ahmed 289)"
"33045","(33045) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, who said: It used to be said: Hating the Ansar is hypocrisy.\n(Bukhari 3784, Muslim 129)"
"33046","(33046) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh that he heard a people narrating about The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, make good the Ansar and the Muhajir. (Ahmed 172)"
"33047","(33047) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God saw May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, seeing women and boys from the Ansar coming from a wedding, and he said: O God, the most beloved of people to me.\n(Muslim 1949. Ibn Hibban 7270)"
"33048","(33048) Abdullah bin Idris told us, he said: Hashim bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Do not go ahead of Quraysh, lest you go astray, and do not lag behind them, lest you go astray. The best of Quraysh are the best of people, and the worst of Quraysh are the best. The worst of people, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, had Quraysh not been arrogant, I would have told them what their choice would be with God, or what it would be for them. With God"
"33049","(33049) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: The people follow the Quraysh in good and evil. (Muslim 1451, Ahmad 379)"
"33050","(33050) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah bin Rifa`ah, on the authority of his father On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered a group of Quraysh and said: Is there anyone besides you among you? They said: No, except Ibn Our sister, our master, and our ally. Then your sister’s son said, “Your sister is among you, your ally is among you, and your master is among you.” Indeed, the Quraysh They are people of truth and trustworthiness, so whoever transgresses against them will have misfortunes, may God castigate him on his face."
"33051","(33051) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The people follow the Quraysh in this matter, the best of them follow the best and the evil of them follow For their evil.\n(Bukhari 34951, Muslim 1451)"
"33052","(33052) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf. On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Mut’im, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Qurayshi has a parable: The strength of two men other than Quraysh. It was said to Al-Zuhri: What did he mean by that? He said about the nobility of opinion. (Ahmad 81, Ibn Hibban 6265)"
"33053","(33053) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sahl ibn Abi Hathami that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Learn from Quraysh, but do not teach it, and advance Quraysh, and do not delay it, for Quraysh has power. The two men are from other than Quraysh. (Abdul Razzaq 19893, Bayhaqi 121)"
"33054","(33054) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mubashir, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Attab, who said: Mu’awiyah rose On the pulpit, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people follow the Quraysh in this matter, their choices are The ignorant people have their choice regarding Islam if they understand it. By God, had Quraysh not been arrogant, I would have informed them of their choice when God (Tabarani 792)"
"33055","(33055) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, he said: Sahil Abu Al-Aswad narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair Al-Jazari, on the authority of Anas, he said: He came to us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were in the house of a man from the Ansar, he took the two door jambs, then said: The Imams are from Quraysh (Bukhari 1875, Ahmed 183)"
"33056","(33056) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Kinanani, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He rose The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a gate where a group of Quraysh was, and he said: This matter is among Quraysh."
"33057","(33057) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Quraysh: This matter is within you. And you are his guardians. (Tabarani 720)"
"33058","(33058) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Asim bin Muhammad bin Zaid, who said: I heard my father saying, I heard Ibn Umar saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: This matter will continue among the Quraysh as long as two of the people remain.\n Asim said in his hadith: And he moved his fingers. (Bukhari 3501, Ahmed 29)"
"33059","(33059) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abi Aqeel, on the authority of Saad, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever rejects the humiliation of Quraysh, God will curse him. (Tirmidhi 3905. Ahmad 171)"
"33060","(33060) Qubaisa bin Uqba narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hasira, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Ali, he said : Quraysh are the imams of the Arabs, the most righteous are the imams of the righteous, and the immoral ones are the imams of the immoral ones."
"33061","(33061) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Mughirah al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Rabi’a ibn Najid, on the authority of Ali, said: The Quraysh are the imams of the righteous Arabs, the imams of the righteous, and the immoral ones are the imams of the immoral ones. And each has a right, so give to each person his due. (Bazzar 7591 Hakim 75)"
"33062","(33062) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, he said: Abu Maryam narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Huraira says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Kingship is with Quraysh, judgment is with the Ansar, and the call to prayer is with The Abyssinians and the Sura in Yemen. (Ahmad 364, Tirmidhi 3936)"
"33063","(33063) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, he said: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ubaid ibn Umair. He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for the Quraysh and said: Oh God, just as You made the first of them taste a torment, so make the last of them taste. Nawala\n(Ahmad 242. Tirmidhi 3908)"
"33064","(33064) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Yazid told us, he said: My uncle Abu Sadiq told me, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Imams are from Quraysh."
"33065","(33065) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abdullah bin Muti’ bin Al-Aswad informed me, On the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say on the day of the conquest of Mecca: No Qurayshite shall be killed. Be patient after this day until the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmad 412. Ibn Hibban 3718)"
"33066","(33066) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Jubayr bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, that a man was killed, and it was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: May God keep him away. He hated Quraysh. (Bazzar 1183. Tabarani 895)"
